	(2, 'CVE-2005-4515', '7.5', 'AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:P/I:P/A:P', '"[\"CWE-89\"]"', 'SQL injection vulnerability in WebDB 1.1 and earlier allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary SQL commands via unspecified search parameters, possibly Search0.  NOTE: the vendor has disputed this issue, saying that "WebDB is a generic online database system used by many of the clients of Lois Software. The flaw that was identified was some code that was added for a client to do some testing of his system and only certain safe commands were allowed. This code has now been removed and it is not now possible to use SQL queries as part of the query string.  No installation or patch is required All clients use a common code library and have their own front end and databases and connections. So as soon as a change / upgrade / enhancement is made to the code, all users of the software begin to use the latest changes immediately."  Since the issue appeared in a custom web site and no action is required on the part of customers, this issue should not be included in CVE', '2005-12-23 00:03:00', '2025-04-02 23:03:51.193', '"[\"cpe:2.3:a:lois_software:webdb:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*\",\"cpe:2.3:a:lois_software:webdb:1.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*\"]"', '"[{\"url\":\"http://pridels0.blogspot.com/2005/12/webdb-sql-inj-vuln.html\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://pridels0.blogspot.com/2005/12/webdb-sql-inj-vuln.html#c114176251867558161\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/18226\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"Patch\",\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.osvdb.org/21910\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/16038\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2005/3071\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/23840\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://pridels0.blogspot.com/2005/12/webdb-sql-inj-vuln.html\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"},{\"url\":\"http://pridels0.blogspot.com/2005/12/webdb-sql-inj-vuln.html#c114176251867558161\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"},{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/18226\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\",\"tags\":[\"Patch\",\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.osvdb.org/21910\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"},{\"url\":\"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/16038\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"},{\"url\":\"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2005/3071\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\",\"tags\":[\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/23840\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"}]"', '"{\"id\":\"CVE-2005-4515\",\"sourceIdentifier\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"published\":\"2005-12-23T01:03:00.000\",\"lastModified\":\"2025-04-03T01:03:51.193\",\"vulnStatus\":\"Deferred\",\"cveTags\":[{\"sourceIdentifier\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"disputed\"]}],\"descriptions\":[{\"lang\":\"en\",\"value\":\"SQL injection vulnerability in WebDB 1.1 and earlier allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary SQL commands via unspecified search parameters, possibly Search0.  NOTE: the vendor has disputed this issue, saying that \\\"WebDB is a generic online database system used by many of the clients of Lois Software. The flaw that was identified was some code that was added for a client to do some testing of his system and only certain safe commands were allowed. This code has now been removed and it is not now possible to use SQL queries as part of the query string.  No installation or patch is required All clients use a common code library and have their own front end and databases and connections. So as soon as a change / upgrade / enhancement is made to the code, all users of the software begin to use the latest changes immediately.\\\"  Since the issue appeared in a custom web site and no action is required on the part of customers, this issue should not be included in CVE\"}],\"metrics\":{\"cvssMetricV2\":[{\"source\":\"nvd@nist.gov\",\"type\":\"Primary\",\"cvssData\":{\"version\":\"2.0\",\"vectorString\":\"AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:P/I:P/A:P\",\"baseScore\":7.5,\"accessVector\":\"NETWORK\",\"accessComplexity\":\"LOW\",\"authentication\":\"NONE\",\"confidentialityImpact\":\"PARTIAL\",\"integrityImpact\":\"PARTIAL\",\"availabilityImpact\":\"PARTIAL\"},\"baseSeverity\":\"HIGH\",\"exploitabilityScore\":10,\"impactScore\":6.4,\"acInsufInfo\":false,\"obtainAllPrivilege\":false,\"obtainUserPrivilege\":false,\"obtainOtherPrivilege\":true,\"userInteractionRequired\":false}]},\"weaknesses\":[{\"source\":\"nvd@nist.gov\",\"type\":\"Primary\",\"description\":[{\"lang\":\"en\",\"value\":\"CWE-89\"}]}],\"configurations\":[{\"nodes\":[{\"operator\":\"OR\",\"negate\":false,\"cpeMatch\":[{\"vulnerable\":true,\"criteria\":\"cpe:2.3:a:lois_software:webdb:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*\",\"versionEndIncluding\":\"1.1\",\"matchCriteriaId\":\"A61ECCAB-52B0-4140-801E-0560501DF796\"},{\"vulnerable\":true,\"criteria\":\"cpe:2.3:a:lois_software:webdb:1.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*\",\"matchCriteriaId\":\"55954F79-CB1A-429A-B98B-E2922E9C21A4\"}]}]}],\"references\":[{\"url\":\"http://pridels0.blogspot.com/2005/12/webdb-sql-inj-vuln.html\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://pridels0.blogspot.com/2005/12/webdb-sql-inj-vuln.html#c114176251867558161\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/18226\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"Patch\",\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.osvdb.org/21910\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/16038\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2005/3071\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/23840\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://pridels0.blogspot.com/2005/12/webdb-sql-inj-vuln.html\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"},{\"url\":\"http://pridels0.blogspot.com/2005/12/webdb-sql-inj-vuln.html#c114176251867558161\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"},{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/18226\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\",\"tags\":[\"Patch\",\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.osvdb.org/21910\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"},{\"url\":\"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/16038\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"},{\"url\":\"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2005/3071\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\",\"tags\":[\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/23840\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"}]}"', '2025-12-26 14:12:31.381', '2025-12-27 14:12:31.381'),
	(3, 'CVE-2006-1050', '2.1', 'AV:L/AC:L/Au:N/C:P/I:N/A:N', '"[]"', 'Kwik-Pay Payroll 4.2.20, and possibly other versions, stores the KwikPay.mdb database file with insecure permissions, which allows local users to obtain sensitive information such as employment and payment data.  NOTE: the provenance of this information is unknown; the details are obtained solely from third party information.  NOTE: the vendor has disputed this vulnerability, stating that "The kwikpay.mdb file supplied with kwikpay is a template for the database structure of user databases created by kwikpay and to store a demonstration payroll. It does not contain any sensitive user information.  When a user payroll database is opened, the encryption of the database is checked and if the database is not encrypted, the user is prompted to encrypt the database, but the choice is the customers.', '2006-03-07 19:02:00', '2025-04-02 23:03:51.193', '"[\"cpe:2.3:a:kwik-pay:kwik-pay_payroll:4.2.20:*:*:*:*:*:*:*\"]"', '"[{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/19075\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.osvdb.org/23617\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/25114\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/19075\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\",\"tags\":[\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.osvdb.org/23617\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"},{\"url\":\"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/25114\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"}]"', '"{\"id\":\"CVE-2006-1050\",\"sourceIdentifier\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"published\":\"2006-03-07T20:02:00.000\",\"lastModified\":\"2025-04-03T01:03:51.193\",\"vulnStatus\":\"Deferred\",\"cveTags\":[{\"sourceIdentifier\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"disputed\"]}],\"descriptions\":[{\"lang\":\"en\",\"value\":\"Kwik-Pay Payroll 4.2.20, and possibly other versions, stores the KwikPay.mdb database file with insecure permissions, which allows local users to obtain sensitive information such as employment and payment data.  NOTE: the provenance of this information is unknown; the details are obtained solely from third party information.  NOTE: the vendor has disputed this vulnerability, stating that \\\"The kwikpay.mdb file supplied with kwikpay is a template for the database structure of user databases created by kwikpay and to store a demonstration payroll. It does not contain any sensitive user information.  When a user payroll database is opened, the encryption of the database is checked and if the database is not encrypted, the user is prompted to encrypt the database, but the choice is the customers.\"}],\"metrics\":{\"cvssMetricV2\":[{\"source\":\"nvd@nist.gov\",\"type\":\"Primary\",\"cvssData\":{\"version\":\"2.0\",\"vectorString\":\"AV:L/AC:L/Au:N/C:P/I:N/A:N\",\"baseScore\":2.1,\"accessVector\":\"LOCAL\",\"accessComplexity\":\"LOW\",\"authentication\":\"NONE\",\"confidentialityImpact\":\"PARTIAL\",\"integrityImpact\":\"NONE\",\"availabilityImpact\":\"NONE\"},\"baseSeverity\":\"LOW\",\"exploitabilityScore\":3.9,\"impactScore\":2.9,\"acInsufInfo\":false,\"obtainAllPrivilege\":false,\"obtainUserPrivilege\":false,\"obtainOtherPrivilege\":false,\"userInteractionRequired\":false}]},\"weaknesses\":[{\"source\":\"nvd@nist.gov\",\"type\":\"Primary\",\"description\":[{\"lang\":\"en\",\"value\":\"NVD-CWE-Other\"}]}],\"configurations\":[{\"nodes\":[{\"operator\":\"OR\",\"negate\":false,\"cpeMatch\":[{\"vulnerable\":true,\"criteria\":\"cpe:2.3:a:kwik-pay:kwik-pay_payroll:4.2.20:*:*:*:*:*:*:*\",\"matchCriteriaId\":\"1BEEF51B-69C4-4122-9FFD-07C613C337D3\"}]}]}],\"references\":[{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/19075\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.osvdb.org/23617\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/25114\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/19075\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\",\"tags\":[\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.osvdb.org/23617\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"},{\"url\":\"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/25114\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"}],\"vendorComments\":[{\"organization\":\"Kwik-Pay\",\"comment\":\"The kwikpay.mdb file supplied with kwikpay is a template for the database structure of user databases created by kwikpay and to store a demonstration payroll. It does not contain any sensitive user information. The file is open for view by any user by design. We do not consider it to be a security vulnerability.\",\"lastModified\":\"2007-02-19T00:00:00\"}]}"', '2025-12-26 14:12:31.622', '2025-12-27 14:12:31.622'),
	(4, 'CVE-2006-5248', '7.8', 'AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:C/I:N/A:N', '"[]"', 'Eazy Cart stores sensitive information under the web root with insufficient access control, which allows remote attackers to download a customer database via a direct request for admin/config/customer.dat.  NOTE: the provenance of this information is unknown; the details are obtained from third party information.', '2006-10-11 22:07:00', '2025-04-08 22:30:58.49', '"[\"cpe:2.3:a:eazy_cart:eazy_cart:2.01:*:*:*:*:*:*:*\"]"', '"[{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/22286\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"Exploit\",\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/22286\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\",\"tags\":[\"Exploit\",\"Vendor Advisory\"]}]"', '"{\"id\":\"CVE-2006-5248\",\"sourceIdentifier\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"published\":\"2006-10-12T00:07:00.000\",\"lastModified\":\"2025-04-09T00:30:58.490\",\"vulnStatus\":\"Deferred\",\"cveTags\":[],\"descriptions\":[{\"lang\":\"en\",\"value\":\"Eazy Cart stores sensitive information under the web root with insufficient access control, which allows remote attackers to download a customer database via a direct request for admin/config/customer.dat.  NOTE: the provenance of this information is unknown; the details are obtained from third party information.\"},{\"lang\":\"es\",\"value\":\"Eazy Cart almacena información sensible bajo el directorio Web raíz con insuficiente control de acceso, lo que permite a los atacantes remotos descargarse la base de datos del cliente mediante una petición directa al admin/config/customer.dat. NOTA: la procedencia de esta información es desconocida; los detalles se obtienen a partir de la información de terceros.\"}],\"metrics\":{\"cvssMetricV2\":[{\"source\":\"nvd@nist.gov\",\"type\":\"Primary\",\"cvssData\":{\"version\":\"2.0\",\"vectorString\":\"AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:C/I:N/A:N\",\"baseScore\":7.8,\"accessVector\":\"NETWORK\",\"accessComplexity\":\"LOW\",\"authentication\":\"NONE\",\"confidentialityImpact\":\"COMPLETE\",\"integrityImpact\":\"NONE\",\"availabilityImpact\":\"NONE\"},\"baseSeverity\":\"HIGH\",\"exploitabilityScore\":10,\"impactScore\":6.9,\"acInsufInfo\":false,\"obtainAllPrivilege\":false,\"obtainUserPrivilege\":false,\"obtainOtherPrivilege\":false,\"userInteractionRequired\":false}]},\"weaknesses\":[{\"source\":\"nvd@nist.gov\",\"type\":\"Primary\",\"description\":[{\"lang\":\"en\",\"value\":\"NVD-CWE-Other\"}]}],\"configurations\":[{\"nodes\":[{\"operator\":\"OR\",\"negate\":false,\"cpeMatch\":[{\"vulnerable\":true,\"criteria\":\"cpe:2.3:a:eazy_cart:eazy_cart:2.01:*:*:*:*:*:*:*\",\"matchCriteriaId\":\"BE52ACC3-D2A8-442C-88EF-D6E83C657855\"}]}]}],\"references\":[{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/22286\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"Exploit\",\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/22286\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\",\"tags\":[\"Exploit\",\"Vendor Advisory\"]}]}"', '2025-12-26 14:12:31.847', '2025-12-27 14:12:31.847'),
	(5, 'CVE-2008-5952', '6', 'AV:N/AC:M/Au:S/C:P/I:P/A:P', '"[\"CWE-89\"]"', 'SQL injection vulnerability in KTP Computer Customer Database (KTPCCD) CMS, when magic_quotes_gpc is disabled, allows remote authenticated users to execute arbitrary SQL commands via the tid parameter in a vtech action to the default URI.', '2009-01-23 18:00:04.967', '2025-04-08 22:30:58.49', '"[\"cpe:2.3:a:ktp_computer_customer_database:ktp_computer_customer_database:_nil_:*:*:*:*:*:*:*\"]"', '"[{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/32888\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/32539\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"Exploit\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2008/3292\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/46897\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/7305\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/32888\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\",\"tags\":[\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/32539\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\",\"tags\":[\"Exploit\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2008/3292\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"},{\"url\":\"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/46897\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"},{\"url\":\"https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/7305\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364da2661108\"}]"', '"{\"id\":\"CVE-2008-5952\",\"sourceIdentifier\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"published\":\"2009-01-23T19:00:04.967\",\"lastModified\":\"2025-04-09T00:30:58.490\",\"vulnStatus\":\"Deferred\",\"cveTags\":[],\"descriptions\":[{\"lang\":\"en\",\"value\":\"SQL injection vulnerability in KTP Computer Customer Database (KTPCCD) CMS, when magic_quotes_gpc is disabled, allows remote authenticated users to execute arbitrary SQL commands via the tid parameter in a vtech action to the default URI.\"},{\"lang\":\"es\",\"value\":\"Vulnerabilidad de inyección SQL en KTP Computer Customer Database (KTPCCD) CMS, cuando magic_quotes_gpc está deshabilitado, permite a los usuarios remotos autentificados ejecutar comandos SQL de su elección a través del parámetro \\\"tid\\\" en una acción \\\"vtech\\\" a la URI por defecto.\"}],\"metrics\":{\"cvssMetricV2\":[{\"source\":\"nvd@nist.gov\",\"type\":\"Primary\",\"cvssData\":{\"version\":\"2.0\",\"vectorString\":\"AV:N/AC:M/Au:S/C:P/I:P/A:P\",\"baseScore\":6,\"accessVector\":\"NETWORK\",\"accessComplexity\":\"MEDIUM\",\"authentication\":\"SINGLE\",\"confidentialityImpact\":\"PARTIAL\",\"integrityImpact\":\"PARTIAL\",\"availabilityImpact\":\"PARTIAL\"},\"baseSeverity\":\"MEDIUM\",\"exploitabilityScore\":6.8,\"impactScore\":6.4,\"acInsufInfo\":false,\"obtainAllPrivilege\":false,\"obtainUserPrivilege\":false,\"obtainOtherPrivilege\":true,\"userInteractionRequired\":false}]},\"weaknesses\":[{\"source\":\"nvd@nist.gov\",\"type\":\"Primary\",\"description\":[{\"lang\":\"en\",\"value\":\"CWE-89\"}]}],\"configurations\":[{\"nodes\":[{\"operator\":\"OR\",\"negate\":false,\"cpeMatch\":[{\"vulnerable\":true,\"criteria\":\"cpe:2.3:a:ktp_computer_customer_database:ktp_computer_customer_database:_nil_:*:*:*:*:*:*:*\",\"matchCriteriaId\":\"03ABF571-0C70-4A32-AD57-2DAF33513F51\"}]}]}],\"references\":[{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/32888\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"Vendor Advisory\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/32539\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\",\"tags\":[\"Exploit\"]},{\"url\":\"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2008/3292\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/46897\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/7305\",\"source\":\"cve@mitre.org\"},{\"url\":\"http://secunia.com/advisories/32888\",\"source\":\"af854a3a-2127-422b-91ae-364d