      In use.
      Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-06 19:50:07.952263', '2026-01-06 19:50:07.952263', NULL, 'Determine If: ', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(908, '3.2', '3.2 - Storage of account data is kept to a minimum.', 'Storage of account data is kept to a minimum.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:41.48784', '2026-01-08 22:29:41.48784', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(634, '3.2.1', '3.2.1 - Account data storage is kept to a minimum through implementation of data retenti...', 'Account data storage is kept to a minimum through implementation of data retention and disposal policies, procedures, and processes that include at least the following:
    Coverage for all locations of stored account data.
    Coverage for any sensitive authentication data (SAD) stored prior to completion of authorization. This bullet is a best practice until its effective date; refer to Applicability Notes below for details.
    Limiting data storage amount and retention time to that which is required for legal or regulatory, and/or business requirements.
    Specific retention requirements for stored account data that defines length of retention period and includes a documented business justification.
    Processes for secure deletion or rendering account data unrecoverable when no longer needed per the retention policy.
    A process for verifying, at least once every three months, that stored account data exceeding the defined retention period has been securely deleted or rendered unrecoverable.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-06 19:50:10.088106', '2026-01-06 19:50:10.088106', NULL, 'Determine if:', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(910, '3.3', '3.3 - Sensitive authentication data (SAD) is not stored after authorization.', 'Sensitive authentication data (SAD) is not stored after authorization.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:41.698395', '2026-01-08 22:29:41.698395', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(912, '3.3.1.1', '3.3.1.1 - The full contents of any track are not retained upon completion of the authoriza...', 'The full contents of any track are not retained upon completion of the authorization process.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:41.915607', '2026-01-08 22:29:41.915607', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(913, '3.3.1.2', '3.3.1.2 - The card verification code is not retained upon completion of the authorization ...', 'The card verification code is not retained upon completion of the authorization process.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:42.023705', '2026-01-08 22:29:42.023705', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(914, '3.3.1.3', '3.3.1.3 - The personal identification number (PIN) and the PIN block are not retained upon...', 'The personal identification number (PIN) and the PIN block are not retained upon completion of the authorization process.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:42.129915', '2026-01-08 22:29:42.129915', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(917, '3.4', '3.4 - Access to displays of full PAN and ability to copy PAN is restricted.', 'Access to displays of full PAN and ability to copy PAN is restricted.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:42.447899', '2026-01-08 22:29:42.447899', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(920, '3.5', '3.5 - Primary account number (PAN) is secured wherever it is stored.', 'Primary account number (PAN) is secured wherever it is stored.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:42.763383', '2026-01-08 22:29:42.763383', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(655, '3.5.1', '3.5.1 - PAN is rendered unreadable anywhere it is stored by using any of the following a...', 'PAN is rendered unreadable anywhere it is stored by using any of the following approaches:
    One-way hashes based on strong cryptography of the entire PAN.
    Truncation (hashing cannot be used to replace the truncated segment of PAN).
–    If hashed and truncated versions of the same PAN, or different truncation formats of the same PAN, are present in an environment, additional controls are in place such that the different versions cannot be correlated to reconstruct the original PAN.
    Index tokens.
    Strong cryptography with associated key- management processes and procedures.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-06 19:50:12.048785', '2026-01-06 19:50:12.048785', NULL, 'Determine if:', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(922, '3.5.1.1', '3.5.1.1 - Hashes used to render PAN unreadable (per the first bullet of Requirement 3.5.1)...', 'Hashes used to render PAN unreadable (per the first bullet of Requirement 3.5.1) are keyed cryptographic hashes of the entire PAN, with associated key-management processes and procedures in accordance with Requirements 3.6 and 3.7.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:42.982599', '2026-01-08 22:29:42.982599', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(923, '3.5.1.2', '3.5.1.2 - If disk-level or partition-level encryption (rather than file-, column-, or fiel...', 'If disk-level or partition-level encryption (rather than file-, column-, or field-level database encryption) is used to render PAN unreadable, it is implemented only as follows:
    On removable electronic media
OR
    If used for non-removable electronic media, PAN is also rendered unreadable via another mechanism that meets Requirement 3.5.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:43.089406', '2026-01-08 22:29:43.089406', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(924, '3.5.1.3', '3.5.1.3 - If disk-level or partition-level encryption is used (rather than file-, column-,...', 'If disk-level or partition-level encryption is used (rather than file-, column-, or field--level database encryption) to render PAN unreadable, it is managed as follows:
      Logical access is managed separately and independently of native operating system authentication and access control mechanisms.
      Decryption keys are not associated with user accounts.
      Authentication factors (passwords, passphrases, or cryptographic keys) that allow access to unencrypted data are stored securely.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:43.195975', '2026-01-08 22:29:43.195975', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(925, '3.6', '3.6 - Cryptographic keys used to protect stored account data are secured.', 'Cryptographic keys used to protect stored account data are secured.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:43.305039', '2026-01-08 22:29:43.305039', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(666, '3.6.1', '3.6.1 - Procedures are defined and implemented to protect cryptographic keys used to pro...', 'Procedures are defined and implemented to protect cryptographic keys used to protect stored account data against disclosure and misuse that include:
    Access to keys is restricted to the fewest number of custodians necessary.
    Key-encrypting keys are at least as strong as the data-encrypting keys they protect.
    Key-encrypting keys are stored separately from data-encrypting keys.
    Keys are stored securely in the fewest possible locations and forms.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-06 19:50:13.090062', '2026-01-06 19:50:13.090062', NULL, 'Determine if:', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(948, '4.2.2', '4.2.2 - PAN is secured with strong cryptography whenever it is sent via end-user messagi...', 'PAN is secured with strong cryptography whenever it is sent via end-user messaging technologies.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:45.770733', '2026-01-08 22:29:45.770733', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1062, '9.4.5', '9.4.5 - Inventory logs of all electronic media with cardholder data are maintained.', 'Inventory logs of all electronic media with cardholder data are maintained.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:58.278184', '2026-01-08 22:29:58.278184', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(927, '3.6.1.1', '3.6.1.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: A documented description of t...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: A documented description of the cryptographic architecture is maintained that includes:
    Details of all algorithms, protocols, and keys used for the protection of stored account data, including key strength and expiry date.
    Preventing the use of the same cryptographic keys in production and test environments. This bullet is a best practice until its effective date; refer to Applicability Notes below for details.
    Description of the key usage for each key.
    Inventory of any hardware security modules (HSMs), key management systems (KMS), and other secure cryptographic devices (SCDs) used for key management, including type and location of devices, as outlined in Requirement 12.3.4.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:43.516952', '2026-01-08 22:29:43.516952', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(928, '3.6.1.2', '3.6.1.2 - Secret and private keys used to encrypt/decrypt stored account data are stored i...', 'Secret and private keys used to encrypt/decrypt stored account data are stored in one (or more) of the following forms at all times:
    Encrypted with a key-encrypting key that is at least as strong as the data-encrypting key, and that is stored separately from the data- encrypting key.
    Within a secure cryptographic device (SCD), such as a hardware security module (HSM) or PTS-approved point-of-interaction device.
    As at least two full-length key components or key shares, in accordance with an industry-accepted method.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:43.625903', '2026-01-08 22:29:43.625903', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(929, '3.6.1.3', '3.6.1.3 - Access to cleartext cryptographic key components is restricted to the fewest num...', 'Access to cleartext cryptographic key components is restricted to the fewest number of custodians necessary.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:43.732929', '2026-01-08 22:29:43.732929', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(930, '3.6.1.4', '3.6.1.4 - Cryptographic keys are stored in the fewest possible locations.', 'Cryptographic keys are stored in the fewest possible locations.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:43.840488', '2026-01-08 22:29:43.840488', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(931, '3.7', '3.7 - Where cryptography is used to protect stored account data, key management proces...', 'Where cryptography is used to protect stored account data, key management processes and procedures covering all aspects of the key lifecycle are defined and implemented.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:43.950085', '2026-01-08 22:29:43.950085', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(672, '3.7.4', '3.7.4 - Key management policies and procedures are implemented for cryptographic key cha...', 'Key management policies and procedures are implemented for cryptographic key changes for keys that have reached the end of their cryptoperiod, as defined by the associated application vendor or key owner, and based on industry best practices and guidelines, including the following:
    A defined cryptoperiod for each key type in use.
    A process for key changes at the end of the defined cryptoperiod.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-06 19:50:13.647666', '2026-01-06 19:50:13.647666', NULL, 'Determine if media containing diagnostic and test programs are checked for malicious code before being used in organizational systems that process, store, or transmit CUI.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(938, '3.7.7', '3.7.7 - Key management policies and procedures are implemented to include the prevention...', 'Key management policies and procedures are implemented to include the prevention of unauthorized substitution of cryptographic keys.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:44.705854', '2026-01-08 22:29:44.705854', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(939, '3.7.8', '3.7.8 - Key management policies and procedures are implemented to include that cryptogra...', 'Key management policies and procedures are implemented to include that cryptographic key custodians formally acknowledge (in writing or electronically) that they understand and accept their key-custodian responsibilities.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:44.811484', '2026-01-08 22:29:44.811484', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(940, '3.7.9', '3.7.9 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Where a service provider shar...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Where a service provider shares cryptographic keys with its customers for transmission or storage of account data, guidance on secure transmission, storage and updating of such keys is documented and distributed to the service provider’s customers.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:44.924445', '2026-01-08 22:29:44.924445', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(721, '4.1', '4.1 - Processes and mechanisms for protecting cardholder data with strong cryptography...', 'Processes and mechanisms for protecting cardholder data with strong cryptography during transmission over open, public networks are defined and documented.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 20:12:25.539862', '2026-01-08 20:12:25.539862', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(942, '4.1.1', '4.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 4 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:45.13342', '2026-01-08 22:29:45.13342', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(943, '4.1.2', '4.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 4 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 4 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:45.239062', '2026-01-08 22:29:45.239062', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(945, '4.2.1', '4.2.1 - Strong cryptography and security protocols are implemented as follows to safegua...', 'Strong cryptography and security protocols are implemented as follows to safeguard PAN during transmission over open, public networks:
    Only trusted keys and certificates are accepted.
    Certificates used to safeguard PAN during transmission over open, public networks are confirmed as valid and are not expired or revoked. This bullet is a best practice until its effective date; refer to applicability notes below for details.
    The protocol in use supports only secure versions or configurations and does not support fallback to, or use of insecure versions, algorithms, key sizes, or implementations.
    The encryption strength is appropriate for the encryption methodology in use.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:45.452351', '2026-01-08 22:29:45.452351', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(946, '4.2.1.1', '4.2.1.1 - An inventory of the entity’s trusted keys and certificates used to protect PAN d...', 'An inventory of the entity’s trusted keys and certificates used to protect PAN during transmission is maintained.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:45.559904', '2026-01-08 22:29:45.559904', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(947, '4.2.1.2', '4.2.1.2 - Wireless networks transmitting PAN or connected to the CDE use industry best pra...', 'Wireless networks transmitting PAN or connected to the CDE use industry best practices to implement strong cryptography for authentication and transmission.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:45.664678', '2026-01-08 22:29:45.664678', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(950, '5.1.1', '5.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 5 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:45.986483', '2026-01-08 22:29:45.986483', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(951, '5.1.2', '5.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 5 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 5 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:46.099035', '2026-01-08 22:29:46.099035', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(953, '5.2.1', '5.2.1 - An anti-malware solution(s) is deployed on all system components, except for tho...', 'An anti-malware solution(s) is deployed on all system components, except for those system components identified in periodic evaluations per Requirement 5.2.3 that concludes the system components are not at risk from malware.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:46.312507', '2026-01-08 22:29:46.312507', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(954, '5.2.2', '5.2.2 - The deployed anti-malware solution(s):     Detects all known types of malware....', 'The deployed anti-malware solution(s):
    Detects all known types of malware.
    Removes, blocks, or contains all known types of malware.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:46.420487', '2026-01-08 22:29:46.420487', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(955, '5.2.3', '5.2.3 - Any system components that are not at risk for malware are evaluated periodicall...', 'Any system components that are not at risk for malware are evaluated periodically to include the following:
      A documented list of all system components not at risk for malware.
      Identification and evaluation of evolving malware threats for those system components.
      Confirmation whether such system components continue to not require anti-malware protection.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:46.530034', '2026-01-08 22:29:46.530034', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(956, '5.2.3.1', '5.2.3.1 - The frequency of periodic evaluations of system components identified as not at ...', 'The frequency of periodic evaluations of system components identified as not at risk for malware is defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:46.635543', '2026-01-08 22:29:46.635543', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(958, '5.3.1', '5.3.1 - The anti-malware solution(s) is kept current via automatic updates.', 'The anti-malware solution(s) is kept current via automatic updates.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:46.849954', '2026-01-08 22:29:46.849954', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(959, '5.3.2', '5.3.2 - The anti-malware solution(s):     Performs periodic scans and active or real-t...', 'The anti-malware solution(s):
    Performs periodic scans and active or real-time scans.
OR
    Performs continuous behavioral analysis of systems or processes.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:46.956884', '2026-01-08 22:29:46.956884', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(960, '5.3.2.1', '5.3.2.1 - If periodic malware scans are performed to meet Requirement 5.3.2, the frequency...', 'If periodic malware scans are performed to meet Requirement 5.3.2, the frequency of scans is defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:47.065489', '2026-01-08 22:29:47.065489', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(961, '5.3.3', '5.3.3 - For removable electronic media, the anti- malware solution(s):     Performs au...', 'For removable electronic media, the anti- malware solution(s):
    Performs automatic scans of when the media is inserted, connected, or logically mounted,
OR
    Performs continuous behavioral analysis of systems or processes when the media is inserted, connected, or logically mounted.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:47.17054', '2026-01-08 22:29:47.17054', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(962, '5.3.4', '5.3.4 - Audit logs for the anti-malware solution(s) are enabled and retained in accordan...', 'Audit logs for the anti-malware solution(s) are enabled and retained in accordance with Requirement 10.5.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:47.277694', '2026-01-08 22:29:47.277694', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(963, '5.3.5', '5.3.5 - Anti-malware mechanisms cannot be disabled or altered by users, unless specifica...', 'Anti-malware mechanisms cannot be disabled or altered by users, unless specifically documented, and authorized by management on a case-by-case basis for a limited time period.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:47.383079', '2026-01-08 22:29:47.383079', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(964, '5.4', '5.4 - Anti-phishing mechanisms protect users against phishing attacks.', 'Anti-phishing mechanisms protect users against phishing attacks.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:47.489466', '2026-01-08 22:29:47.489466', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(965, '5.4.1', '5.4.1 - Processes and automated mechanisms are in place to detect and protect personnel ...', 'Processes and automated mechanisms are in place to detect and protect personnel against phishing attacks.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:47.595567', '2026-01-08 22:29:47.595567', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(728, '6.1', '6.1 - Processes and mechanisms for developing and maintaining secure systems and softw...', 'Processes and mechanisms for developing and maintaining secure systems and software are defined and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 20:12:27.236217', '2026-01-08 20:12:27.236217', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(967, '6.1.1', '6.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 6 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:47.807453', '2026-01-08 22:29:47.807453', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(968, '6.1.2', '6.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 6 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 6 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:47.917509', '2026-01-08 22:29:47.917509', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(970, '6.2.1', '6.2.1 - Bespoke and custom software are developed securely, as follows:     Based on i...', 'Bespoke and custom software are developed securely, as follows:
    Based on industry standards and/or best practices for secure development.
    In accordance with PCI DSS (for example, secure authentication and logging).
    Incorporating consideration of information security issues during each stage of the software development lifecycle.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:48.133477', '2026-01-08 22:29:48.133477', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1021, '8.3.4', '8.3.4 - Invalid authentication attempts are limited by:     Locking out the user ID af...', 'Invalid authentication attempts are limited by:
    Locking out the user ID after not more than 10 attempts.
    Setting the lockout duration to a minimum of 30 minutes or until the user’s identity is confirmed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:53.807692', '2026-01-08 22:29:53.807692', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(971, '6.2.2', '6.2.2 - Software development personnel working on bespoke and custom software are traine...', 'Software development personnel working on bespoke and custom software are trained at least once every 12 months as follows:
    On software security relevant to their job function and development languages.
    Including secure software design and secure coding techniques.
    Including, if security testing tools are used, how to use the tools for detecting vulnerabilities in software.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:48.237499', '2026-01-08 22:29:48.237499', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(972, '6.2.3', '6.2.3 - Bespoke and custom software is reviewed prior to being released into production ...', 'Bespoke and custom software is reviewed prior to being released into production or to customers, to identify and correct potential coding vulnerabilities, as follows:
    Code reviews ensure code is developed according to secure coding guidelines.
    Code reviews look for both existing and emerging software vulnerabilities.
    Appropriate corrections are implemented prior to release.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:48.350006', '2026-01-08 22:29:48.350006', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(973, '6.2.3.1', '6.2.3.1 - If manual code reviews are performed for bespoke and custom software prior to re...', 'If manual code reviews are performed for bespoke and custom software prior to release to production, code changes are:
    Reviewed by individuals other than the originating code author, and who are knowledgeable about code-review techniques and secure coding practices.
    Reviewed and approved by management prior to release.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:48.454451', '2026-01-08 22:29:48.454451', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(974, '6.2.4', '6.2.4 - Software engineering techniques or other methods are defined and in use by softw...', 'Software engineering techniques or other methods are defined and in use by software development personnel to prevent or mitigate common software attacks and related vulnerabilities in bespoke and custom software, including but not limited to the following:
    Injection attacks, including SQL, LDAP, XPath, or other command, parameter, object, fault, or injection-type flaws.
    Attacks on data and data structures, including attempts to manipulate buffers, pointers, input data, or shared data.
    Attacks on cryptography usage, including attempts to exploit weak, insecure, or inappropriate cryptographic implementations, algorithms, cipher suites, or modes of operation.
    Attacks on business logic, including attempts to abuse or bypass application features and functionalities through the manipulation of APIs, communication protocols and channels, client- side functionality, or other system/application functions and resources. This includes cross-site scripting (XSS) and cross-site request forgery (CSRF).
    Attacks on access control mechanisms, including attempts to bypass or abuse identification, authentication, or authorization mechanisms, or attempts to exploit weaknesses in the implementation of such mechanisms.
    Attacks via any “high-risk” vulnerabilities identified in the vulnerability identification process, as defined in Requirement 6.3.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:48.561997', '2026-01-08 22:29:48.561997', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(975, '6.3', '6.3 - Security vulnerabilities are identified and addressed.', 'Security vulnerabilities are identified and addressed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:48.692496', '2026-01-08 22:29:48.692496', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(976, '6.3.1', '6.3.1 - Security vulnerabilities are identified and managed as follows:     New securi...', 'Security vulnerabilities are identified and managed as follows:
    New security vulnerabilities are identified using industry-recognized sources for security vulnerability information, including alerts from international and national computer emergency response teams (CERTs).
    Vulnerabilities are assigned a risk ranking based on industry best practices and consideration of potential impact.
    Risk rankings identify, at a minimum, all vulnerabilities considered to be a high-risk or critical to the environment.
    Vulnerabilities for bespoke and custom, and third-party software (for example operating systems and databases) are covered.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:48.82797', '2026-01-08 22:29:48.82797', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(977, '6.3.2', '6.3.2 - An inventory of bespoke and custom software, and third-party software components...', 'An inventory of bespoke and custom software, and third-party software components incorporated into bespoke and custom software is maintained to facilitate vulnerability and patch management.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:48.94176', '2026-01-08 22:29:48.94176', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(978, '6.3.3', '6.3.3 - All system components are protected from known vulnerabilities by installing app...', 'All system components are protected from known vulnerabilities by installing applicable security patches/updates as follows:
    Critical or high-security patches/updates (identified according to the risk ranking process at Requirement 6.3.1) are installed within one month of release.
    All other applicable security patches/updates are installed within an appropriate time frame as determined by the entity (for example, within three months of release).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:49.080066', '2026-01-08 22:29:49.080066', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(979, '6.4', '6.4 - Public-facing web applications are protected against attacks.', 'Public-facing web applications are protected against attacks.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:49.193502', '2026-01-08 22:29:49.193502', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(980, '6.4.1', '6.4.1 - For public-facing web applications, new threats and vulnerabilities are addresse...', 'For public-facing web applications, new threats and vulnerabilities are addressed on an ongoing basis and these applications are protected against known attacks as follows:
    Reviewing public-facing web applications via manual or automated application vulnerability security assessment tools or methods as follows:
–    At least once every 12 months and after significant changes.
–    By an entity that specializes in application security.
–    Including, at a minimum, all common software attacks in Requirement 6.2.4.
–    All vulnerabilities are ranked in accordance with requirement 6.3.1.
–    All vulnerabilities are corrected.
–    The application is re-evaluated after the corrections
OR
    Installing an automated technical solution(s) that continually detects and prevents web-based attacks as follows:
–    Installed in front of public-facing web applications to detect and prevent web- based attacks.
–    Actively running and up to date as applicable.
–    Generating audit logs.
–    Configured to either block web-based attacks or generate an alert that is immediately investigated.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:49.301261', '2026-01-08 22:29:49.301261', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1022, '8.3.5', '8.3.5 - If passwords/passphrases are used as authentication factors to meet Requirement ...', 'If passwords/passphrases are used as authentication factors to meet Requirement 8.3.1, they are set and reset for each user as follows:
    Set to a unique value for first-time use and upon reset.
    Forced to be changed immediately after the first use.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:53.914027', '2026-01-08 22:29:53.914027', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(981, '6.4.2', '6.4.2 - For public-facing web applications, an automated technical solution is deployed ...', 'For public-facing web applications, an automated technical solution is deployed that continually detects and prevents web-based attacks, with at least the following:
    Is installed in front of public-facing web applications and is configured to detect and prevent web-based attacks.
    Actively running and up to date as applicable.
    Generating audit logs.
    Configured to either block web-based attacks or generate an alert that is immediately investigated.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:49.409156', '2026-01-08 22:29:49.409156', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(982, '6.4.3', '6.4.3 - All payment page scripts that are loaded and executed in the consumer’s browser ...', 'All payment page scripts that are loaded and executed in the consumer’s browser are managed as follows:
    A method is implemented to confirm that each script is authorized.
    A method is implemented to assure the integrity of each script.
    An inventory of all scripts is maintained with written justification as to why each is necessary.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:49.520584', '2026-01-08 22:29:49.520584', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(983, '6.5', '6.5 - Changes to all system components are managed securely.', 'Changes to all system components are managed securely.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:49.629479', '2026-01-08 22:29:49.629479', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(984, '6.5.1', '6.5.1 - Changes to all system components in the production environment are made accordin...', 'Changes to all system components in the production environment are made according to established procedures that include:
    Reason for, and description of, the change.
    Documentation of security impact.
    Documented change approval by authorized parties.
    Testing to verify that the change does not adversely impact system security.
    For bespoke and custom software changes, all updates are tested for compliance with Requirement 6.2.4 before being deployed into production.
    Procedures to address failures and return to a secure state.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:49.736872', '2026-01-08 22:29:49.736872', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(985, '6.5.2', '6.5.2 - Upon completion of a significant change, all applicable PCI DSS requirements are...', 'Upon completion of a significant change, all applicable PCI DSS requirements are confirmed to be in place on all new or changed systems and networks, and documentation is updated as applicable.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:49.845856', '2026-01-08 22:29:49.845856', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(986, '6.5.3', '6.5.3 - Pre-production environments are separated from production environments and the s...', 'Pre-production environments are separated from production environments and the separation is enforced with access controls.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:49.953013', '2026-01-08 22:29:49.953013', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(987, '6.5.4', '6.5.4 - Roles and functions are separated between production and pre-production environm...', 'Roles and functions are separated between production and pre-production environments to provide accountability such that only reviewed and approved changes are deployed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:50.069038', '2026-01-08 22:29:50.069038', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(988, '6.5.5', '6.5.5 - Live PANs are not used in pre-production environments, except where those enviro...', 'Live PANs are not used in pre-production environments, except where those environments are included in the CDE and protected in accordance with all applicable PCI DSS requirements.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:50.177203', '2026-01-08 22:29:50.177203', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(989, '6.5.6', '6.5.6 - Test data and test accounts are removed from system components before the system...', 'Test data and test accounts are removed from system components before the system goes into production.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:50.284098', '2026-01-08 22:29:50.284098', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(991, '7.1.1', '7.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 7 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:50.497483', '2026-01-08 22:29:50.497483', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(992, '7.1.2', '7.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 7 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 7 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:50.606986', '2026-01-08 22:29:50.606986', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(994, '7.2.1', '7.2.1 - An access control model is defined and includes granting access as follows:   ...', 'An access control model is defined and includes granting access as follows:
    Appropriate access depending on the entity’s business and access needs.
    Access to system components and data resources that is based on users’ job classification and functions.
    The least privileges required (for example, user, administrator) to perform a job function.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:50.818611', '2026-01-08 22:29:50.818611', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(995, '7.2.2', '7.2.2 - Access is assigned to users, including privileged users, based on:     Job cla...', 'Access is assigned to users, including privileged users, based on:
    Job classification and function.
    Least privileges necessary to perform job responsibilities.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:50.923514', '2026-01-08 22:29:50.923514', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(996, '7.2.3', '7.2.3 - Required privileges are approved by authorized personnel.', 'Required privileges are approved by authorized personnel.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:51.035033', '2026-01-08 22:29:51.035033', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(997, '7.2.4', '7.2.4 - All user accounts and related access privileges, including third-party/vendor ac...', 'All user accounts and related access privileges, including third-party/vendor accounts, are reviewed as follows:
    At least once every six months.
    To ensure user accounts and access remain appropriate based on job function.
    Any inappropriate access is addressed.
    Management acknowledges that access remains appropriate.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:51.143741', '2026-01-08 22:29:51.143741', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(998, '7.2.5', '7.2.5 - All application and system accounts and related access privileges are assigned a...', 'All application and system accounts and related access privileges are assigned and managed as follows:
    Based on the least privileges necessary for the operability of the system or application.
    Access is limited to the systems, applications, or processes that specifically require their use.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:51.249184', '2026-01-08 22:29:51.249184', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1041, '9.1.1', '9.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 9 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:55.956587', '2026-01-08 22:29:55.956587', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(999, '7.2.5.1', '7.2.5.1 - All access by application and system accounts and related access privileges are ...', 'All access by application and system accounts and related access privileges are reviewed as follows:
    Periodically (at the frequency defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1).
    The application/system access remains appropriate for the function being performed.
    Any inappropriate access is addressed.
    Management acknowledges that access remains appropriate.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:51.364582', '2026-01-08 22:29:51.364582', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1000, '7.2.6', '7.2.6 - All user access to query repositories of stored cardholder data is restricted as...', 'All user access to query repositories of stored cardholder data is restricted as follows:
    Via applications or other programmatic methods, with access and allowed actions based on user roles and least privileges.
    Only the responsible administrator(s) can directly access or query repositories of stored CHD.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:51.471341', '2026-01-08 22:29:51.471341', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1002, '7.3.1', '7.3.1 - An access control system(s) is in place that restricts access based on a user’s ...', 'An access control system(s) is in place that restricts access based on a user’s need to know and covers all system components.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:51.686093', '2026-01-08 22:29:51.686093', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1003, '7.3.2', '7.3.2 - The access control system(s) is configured to enforce permissions assigned to in...', 'The access control system(s) is configured to enforce permissions assigned to individuals, applications, and systems based on job classification and function.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:51.791578', '2026-01-08 22:29:51.791578', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1004, '7.3.3', '7.3.3 - The access control system(s) is set to “deny all” by default.', 'The access control system(s) is set to “deny all” by default.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:51.901018', '2026-01-08 22:29:51.901018', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1006, '8.1.1', '8.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 8 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:52.11705', '2026-01-08 22:29:52.11705', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1007, '8.1.2', '8.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 8 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 8 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:52.223045', '2026-01-08 22:29:52.223045', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1009, '8.2.1', '8.2.1 - All users are assigned a unique ID before access to system components or cardhol...', 'All users are assigned a unique ID before access to system components or cardholder data is allowed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:52.450682', '2026-01-08 22:29:52.450682', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1010, '8.2.2', '8.2.2 - Group, shared, or generic accounts, or other shared authentication credentials a...', 'Group, shared, or generic accounts, or other shared authentication credentials are only used when necessary on an exception basis, and are managed as follows:
    Account use is prevented unless needed for an exceptional circumstance.
    Use is limited to the time needed for the exceptional circumstance.
    Business justification for use is documented.
    Use is explicitly approved by management.
    Individual user identity is confirmed before access to an account is granted.
    Every action taken is attributable to an individual user.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:52.561562', '2026-01-08 22:29:52.561562', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1011, '8.2.3', '8.2.3 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Service providers with remote...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Service providers with remote access to customer premises use unique authentication factors for each customer premises.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:52.68151', '2026-01-08 22:29:52.68151', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
    Authorized with the appropriate approval.
    Implemented with only the privileges specified on the documented approval.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:52.818565', '2026-01-08 22:29:52.818565', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1013, '8.2.5', '8.2.5 - Access for terminated users is immediately revoked.', 'Access for terminated users is immediately revoked.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:52.949621', '2026-01-08 22:29:52.949621', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1014, '8.2.6', '8.2.6 - Inactive user accounts are removed or disabled within 90 days of inactivity.', 'Inactive user accounts are removed or disabled within 90 days of inactivity.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:53.060526', '2026-01-08 22:29:53.060526', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1015, '8.2.7', '8.2.7 - Accounts used by third parties to access, support, or maintain system components...', 'Accounts used by third parties to access, support, or maintain system components via remote access are managed as follows:
    Enabled only during the time period needed and disabled when not in use.
    Use is monitored for unexpected activity.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:53.16511', '2026-01-08 22:29:53.16511', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1016, '8.2.8', '8.2.8 - If a user session has been idle for more than 15 minutes, the user is required t...', 'If a user session has been idle for more than 15 minutes, the user is required to re-authenticate to re-activate the terminal or session.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:53.276022', '2026-01-08 22:29:53.276022', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1018, '8.3.1', '8.3.1 - All user access to system components for users and administrators is authenticat...', 'All user access to system components for users and administrators is authenticated via at least one of the following authentication factors:
    Something you know, such as a password or passphrase.
    Something you have, such as a token device or smart card.
    Something you are, such as a biometric element.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:53.488043', '2026-01-08 22:29:53.488043', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1019, '8.3.2', '8.3.2 - Strong cryptography is used to render all authentication factors unreadable duri...', 'Strong cryptography is used to render all authentication factors unreadable during transmission and storage on all system components.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:53.593553', '2026-01-08 22:29:53.593553', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1020, '8.3.3', '8.3.3 - User identity is verified before modifying any authentication factor.', 'User identity is verified before modifying any authentication factor.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:53.698529', '2026-01-08 22:29:53.698529', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1023, '8.3.6', '8.3.6 - If passwords/passphrases are used as authentication factors to meet Requirement ...', 'If passwords/passphrases are used as authentication factors to meet Requirement 8.3.1, they meet the following minimum level of complexity:
    A minimum length of 12 characters (or IF the system does not support 12 characters, a minimum length of eight characters).
    Contain both numeric and alphabetic characters.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:54.024056', '2026-01-08 22:29:54.024056', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1024, '8.3.7', '8.3.7 - Individuals are not allowed to submit a new password/passphrase that is the same...', 'Individuals are not allowed to submit a new password/passphrase that is the same as any of the last four passwords/passphrases used.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:54.136626', '2026-01-08 22:29:54.136626', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1025, '8.3.8', '8.3.8 - Authentication policies and procedures are documented and communicated to all us...', 'Authentication policies and procedures are documented and communicated to all users including:
    Guidance on selecting strong authentication factors.
    Guidance for how users should protect their authentication factors.
    Instructions not to reuse previously used passwords/passphrases.
    Instructions to change passwords/passphrases if there is any suspicion or knowledge that the password/passphrases have been compromised and how to report the incident.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:54.24559', '2026-01-08 22:29:54.24559', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1026, '8.3.9', '8.3.9 - If passwords/passphrases are used as the only authentication factor for user acc...', 'If passwords/passphrases are used as the only authentication factor for user access (i.e., in any single-factor authentication implementation) then either:
    Passwords/passphrases are changed at least once every 90 days,
OR
    The security posture of accounts is dynamically analyzed, and real-time access to resources is automatically determined accordingly.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:54.350488', '2026-01-08 22:29:54.350488', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1027, '8.3.10', '8.3.10 - Additional requirement for service providers only: If passwords/passphrases are ...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: If passwords/passphrases are used as the only authentication factor for customer user access to cardholder data (i.e., in any single- factor authentication implementation), then guidance is provided to customer users including:
    Guidance for customers to change their user passwords/passphrases periodically.
    Guidance as to when, and under what circumstances, passwords/passphrases are to be changed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:54.455491', '2026-01-08 22:29:54.455491', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1028, '8.3.10.1', '8.3.10.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: If passwords/passphrases are ...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: If passwords/passphrases are used as the only authentication factor for customer user access (i.e., in any single-factor authentication implementation) then either:
    Passwords/passphrases are changed at least once every 90 days,
OR
    The security posture of accounts is dynamically analyzed, and real-time access to resources is automatically determined accordingly.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:54.563051', '2026-01-08 22:29:54.563051', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1029, '8.3.11', '8.3.11 - Where authentication factors such as physical or logical security tokens, smart ...', 'Where authentication factors such as physical or logical security tokens, smart cards, or certificates are used:
    Factors are assigned to an individual user and not shared among multiple users.
    Physical and/or logical controls ensure only the intended user can use that factor to gain access.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:54.668069', '2026-01-08 22:29:54.668069', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1031, '8.4.1', '8.4.1 - MFA is implemented for all non-console access into the CDE for personnel with ad...', 'MFA is implemented for all non-console access into the CDE for personnel with administrative access.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:54.884082', '2026-01-08 22:29:54.884082', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1032, '8.4.2', '8.4.2 - MFA is implemented for all access into the CDE.', 'MFA is implemented for all access into the CDE.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:54.99357', '2026-01-08 22:29:54.99357', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1033, '8.4.3', '8.4.3 - MFA is implemented for all remote network access originating from outside the en...', 'MFA is implemented for all remote network access originating from outside the entity’s network that could access or impact the CDE as follows:
    All remote access by all personnel, both users and administrators, originating from outside the entity’s network.
    All remote access by third parties and vendors.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:55.100107', '2026-01-08 22:29:55.100107', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1035, '8.5.1', '8.5.1 - MFA systems are implemented as follows:     The MFA system is not susceptible ...', 'MFA systems are implemented as follows:
    The MFA system is not susceptible to replay attacks.
    MFA systems cannot be bypassed by any users, including administrative users unless specifically documented, and authorized by management on an exception basis, for a limited time period.
    At least two different types of authentication factors are used.
    Success of all authentication factors is required before access is granted.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:55.312038', '2026-01-08 22:29:55.312038', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1037, '8.6.1', '8.6.1 - If accounts used by systems or applications can be used for interactive login, t...', 'If accounts used by systems or applications can be used for interactive login, they are managed as follows:
    Interactive use is prevented unless needed for an exceptional circumstance.
    Interactive use is limited to the time needed for the exceptional circumstance.
    Business justification for interactive use is documented.
    Interactive use is explicitly approved by management.
    Individual user identity is confirmed before access to account is granted.
    Every action taken is attributable to an individual user.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:55.527068', '2026-01-08 22:29:55.527068', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1038, '8.6.2', '8.6.2 - Passwords/passphrases for any application and system accounts that can be used f...', 'Passwords/passphrases for any application and system accounts that can be used for interactive login are not hard coded in scripts, configuration/property files, or bespoke and custom source code.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:55.636553', '2026-01-08 22:29:55.636553', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1039, '8.6.3', '8.6.3 - Passwords/passphrases for any application and system accounts are protected agai...', 'Passwords/passphrases for any application and system accounts are protected against misuse as follows:
    Passwords/passphrases are changed periodically (at the frequency defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1) and upon suspicion or confirmation of compromise.
    Passwords/passphrases are constructed with sufficient complexity appropriate for how frequently the entity changes the passwords/passphrases.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:55.743072', '2026-01-08 22:29:55.743072', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1042, '9.1.2', '9.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 9 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 9 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:56.063536', '2026-01-08 22:29:56.063536', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1044, '9.2.1', '9.2.1 - Appropriate facility entry controls are in place to restrict physical access to ...', 'Appropriate facility entry controls are in place to restrict physical access to systems in the CDE.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:56.336556', '2026-01-08 22:29:56.336556', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1045, '9.2.1.1', '9.2.1.1 - Individual physical access to sensitive areas within the CDE is monitored with e...', 'Individual physical access to sensitive areas within the CDE is monitored with either video cameras or physical access control mechanisms (or both) as follows:
    Entry and exit points to/from sensitive areas within the CDE are monitored.
    Monitoring devices or mechanisms are protected from tampering or disabling.
    Collected data is reviewed and correlated with other entries.
    Collected data is stored for at least three months, unless otherwise restricted by law.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:56.448615', '2026-01-08 22:29:56.448615', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1046, '9.2.2', '9.2.2 - Physical and/or logical controls are implemented to restrict use of publicly acc...', 'Physical and/or logical controls are implemented to restrict use of publicly accessible network jacks within the facility.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:56.553568', '2026-01-08 22:29:56.553568', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1047, '9.2.3', '9.2.3 - Physical access to wireless access points, gateways, networking/communications h...', 'Physical access to wireless access points, gateways, networking/communications hardware, and telecommunication lines within the facility is restricted.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:56.659543', '2026-01-08 22:29:56.659543', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1048, '9.2.4', '9.2.4 - Access to consoles in sensitive areas is restricted via locking when not in use.', 'Access to consoles in sensitive areas is restricted via locking when not in use.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:56.766412', '2026-01-08 22:29:56.766412', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1050, '9.3.1', '9.3.1 - Procedures are implemented for authorizing and managing physical access of perso...', 'Procedures are implemented for authorizing and managing physical access of personnel to the CDE, including:
    Identifying personnel.
    Managing changes to an individual’s physical access requirements.
    Revoking or terminating personnel identification.
    Limiting access to the identification process or system to authorized personnel.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:56.984615', '2026-01-08 22:29:56.984615', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1051, '9.3.1.1', '9.3.1.1 - Physical access to sensitive areas within the CDE for personnel is controlled as...', 'Physical access to sensitive areas within the CDE for personnel is controlled as follows:
    Access is authorized and based on individual job function.
    Access is revoked immediately upon termination.
    All physical access mechanisms, such as keys, access cards, etc., are returned or disabled upon termination.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:57.093913', '2026-01-08 22:29:57.093913', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1052, '9.3.2', '9.3.2 - Procedures are implemented for authorizing and managing visitor access to the CD...', 'Procedures are implemented for authorizing and managing visitor access to the CDE, including:
    Visitors are authorized before entering.
    Visitors are escorted at all times.
    Visitors are clearly identified and given a badge or other identification that expires.
    Visitor badges or other identification visibly distinguishes visitors from personnel.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:57.199348', '2026-01-08 22:29:57.199348', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1053, '9.3.3', '9.3.3 - Visitor badges or identification are surrendered or deactivated before visitors ...', 'Visitor badges or identification are surrendered or deactivated before visitors leave the facility or at the date of expiration.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:57.306076', '2026-01-08 22:29:57.306076', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1054, '9.3.4', '9.3.4 - A visitor log is used to maintain a physical record of visitor activity within t...', 'A visitor log is used to maintain a physical record of visitor activity within the facility and within sensitive areas, including:
    The visitor’s name and the organization represented.
    The date and time of the visit.
    The name of the personnel authorizing physical access.
    Retaining the log for at least three months, unless otherwise restricted by law.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:57.419121', '2026-01-08 22:29:57.419121', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1055, '9.4', '9.4 - Media with cardholder data is securely stored, accessed, distributed, and destro...', 'Media with cardholder data is securely stored, accessed, distributed, and destroyed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:57.52623', '2026-01-08 22:29:57.52623', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1056, '9.4.1', '9.4.1 - All media with cardholder data is physically secured.', 'All media with cardholder data is physically secured.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:57.632089', '2026-01-08 22:29:57.632089', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1057, '9.4.1.1', '9.4.1.1 - Offline media backups with cardholder data are stored in a secure location.', 'Offline media backups with cardholder data are stored in a secure location.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:57.739576', '2026-01-08 22:29:57.739576', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1058, '9.4.1.2', '9.4.1.2 - The security of the offline media backup location(s) with cardholder data is rev...', 'The security of the offline media backup location(s) with cardholder data is reviewed at least once every 12 months.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:57.850123', '2026-01-08 22:29:57.850123', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1059, '9.4.2', '9.4.2 - All media with cardholder data is classified in accordance with the sensitivity ...', 'All media with cardholder data is classified in accordance with the sensitivity of the data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:57.955612', '2026-01-08 22:29:57.955612', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1060, '9.4.3', '9.4.3 - Media with cardholder data sent outside the facility is secured as follows:   ...', 'Media with cardholder data sent outside the facility is secured as follows:
    Media sent outside the facility is logged.
    Media is sent by secured courier or other delivery method that can be accurately tracked.
    Offsite tracking logs include details about media location.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:58.064631', '2026-01-08 22:29:58.064631', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1061, '9.4.4', '9.4.4 - Management approves all media with cardholder data that is moved outside the fac...', 'Management approves all media with cardholder data that is moved outside the facility (including when media is distributed to individuals).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:58.17364', '2026-01-08 22:29:58.17364', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1063, '9.4.5.1', '9.4.5.1 - Inventories of electronic media with cardholder data are conducted at least once...', 'Inventories of electronic media with cardholder data are conducted at least once every 12 months.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:58.383684', '2026-01-08 22:29:58.383684', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1064, '9.4.6', '9.4.6 - Hard-copy materials with cardholder data are destroyed when no longer needed for...', 'Hard-copy materials with cardholder data are destroyed when no longer needed for business or legal reasons, as follows:
    Materials are cross-cut shredded, incinerated, or pulped so that cardholder data cannot be reconstructed.
    Materials are stored in secure storage containers prior to destruction.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:58.493107', '2026-01-08 22:29:58.493107', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1065, '9.4.7', '9.4.7 - Electronic media with cardholder data is destroyed when no longer needed for bus...', 'Electronic media with cardholder data is destroyed when no longer needed for business or legal reasons via one of the following:
    The electronic media is destroyed.
    The cardholder data is rendered unrecoverable so that it cannot be reconstructed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:58.601651', '2026-01-08 22:29:58.601651', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1066, '9.5', '9.5 - Point-of-interaction (POI) devices are protected from tampering and unauthorized...', 'Point-of-interaction (POI) devices are protected from tampering and unauthorized substitution.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:58.706868', '2026-01-08 22:29:58.706868', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1067, '9.5.1', '9.5.1 - POI devices that capture payment card data via direct physical interaction with ...', 'POI devices that capture payment card data via direct physical interaction with the payment card form factor are protected from tampering and unauthorized substitution, including the following:
      Maintaining a list of POI devices.
      Periodically inspecting POI devices to look for tampering or unauthorized substitution.
      Training personnel to be aware of suspicious behavior and to report tampering or unauthorized substitution of devices.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:58.81706', '2026-01-08 22:29:58.81706', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1068, '9.5.1.1', '9.5.1.1 - An up-to-date list of POI devices is maintained, including:     Make and model...', 'An up-to-date list of POI devices is maintained, including:
    Make and model of the device.
    Location of device.
    Device serial number or other methods of unique identification.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:58.92162', '2026-01-08 22:29:58.92162', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1069, '9.5.1.2', '9.5.1.2 - POI device surfaces are periodically inspected to detect tampering and unauthori...', 'POI device surfaces are periodically inspected to detect tampering and unauthorized substitution.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:59.027174', '2026-01-08 22:29:59.027174', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1070, '9.5.1.2.1', '9.5.1.2.1 - The frequency of periodic POI device inspections and the type of inspections per...', 'The frequency of periodic POI device inspections and the type of inspections performed is defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:59.137167', '2026-01-08 22:29:59.137167', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1071, '9.5.1.3', '9.5.1.3 - Training is provided for personnel in POI environments to be aware of attempted ...', 'Training is provided for personnel in POI environments to be aware of attempted tampering or replacement of POI devices, and includes:
    Verifying the identity of any third-party persons claiming to be repair or maintenance personnel, before granting them access to modify or troubleshoot devices.
    Procedures to ensure devices are not installed, replaced, or returned without verification.
    Being aware of suspicious behavior around devices.
    Reporting suspicious behavior and indications of device tampering or substitution to appropriate personnel.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:59.241299', '2026-01-08 22:29:59.241299', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1073, '10.1.1', '10.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 10 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:59.455184', '2026-01-08 22:29:59.455184', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1074, '10.1.2', '10.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 10 are docum...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 10 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:59.561116', '2026-01-08 22:29:59.561116', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1076, '10.2.1', '10.2.1 - Audit logs are enabled and active for all system components and cardholder data.', 'Audit logs are enabled and active for all system components and cardholder data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:59.770617', '2026-01-08 22:29:59.770617', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1077, '10.2.1.1', '10.2.1.1 - Audit logs capture all individual user access to cardholder data.', 'Audit logs capture all individual user access to cardholder data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:59.874758', '2026-01-08 22:29:59.874758', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1078, '10.2.1.2', '10.2.1.2 - Audit logs capture all actions taken by any individual with administrative acces...', 'Audit logs capture all actions taken by any individual with administrative access, including any interactive use of application or system accounts.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:29:59.984661', '2026-01-08 22:29:59.984661', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1079, '10.2.1.3', '10.2.1.3 - Audit logs capture all access to audit logs.', 'Audit logs capture all access to audit logs.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:00.093069', '2026-01-08 22:30:00.093069', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1080, '10.2.1.4', '10.2.1.4 - Audit logs capture all invalid logical access attempts.', 'Audit logs capture all invalid logical access attempts.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:00.200648', '2026-01-08 22:30:00.200648', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1081, '10.2.1.5', '10.2.1.5 - Audit logs capture all changes to identification and authentication credentials ...', 'Audit logs capture all changes to identification and authentication credentials including, but not limited to:
    Creation of new accounts.
    Elevation of privileges.
    All changes, additions, or deletions to accounts with administrative access.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:00.305107', '2026-01-08 22:30:00.305107', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1082, '10.2.1.6', '10.2.1.6 - Audit logs capture the following:     All initialization of new audit logs, an...', 'Audit logs capture the following:
    All initialization of new audit logs, and
    All starting, stopping, or pausing of the existing audit logs.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:00.413152', '2026-01-08 22:30:00.413152', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1083, '10.2.1.7', '10.2.1.7 - Audit logs capture all creation and deletion of system-level objects.', 'Audit logs capture all creation and deletion of system-level objects.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:00.531072', '2026-01-08 22:30:00.531072', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1084, '10.2.2', '10.2.2 - Audit logs record the following details for each auditable event:     User ide...', 'Audit logs record the following details for each auditable event:
    User identification.
    Type of event.
    Date and time.
    Success and failure indication.
    Origination of event.
    Identity or name of affected data, system component, resource, or service (for example, name and protocol).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:00.639118', '2026-01-08 22:30:00.639118', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1085, '10.3', '10.3 - Audit logs are protected from destruction and unauthorized modifications.', 'Audit logs are protected from destruction and unauthorized modifications.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:00.744186', '2026-01-08 22:30:00.744186', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1086, '10.3.1', '10.3.1 - Read access to audit logs files is limited to those with a job-related need.', 'Read access to audit logs files is limited to those with a job-related need.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:00.849614', '2026-01-08 22:30:00.849614', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1087, '10.3.2', '10.3.2 - Audit log files are protected to prevent modifications by individuals.', 'Audit log files are protected to prevent modifications by individuals.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:00.960237', '2026-01-08 22:30:00.960237', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1088, '10.3.3', '10.3.3 - Audit log files, including those for external- facing technologies, are promptly...', 'Audit log files, including those for external- facing technologies, are promptly backed up to a secure, central, internal log server(s) or other media that is difficult to modify.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:01.065182', '2026-01-08 22:30:01.065182', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1089, '10.3.4', '10.3.4 - File integrity monitoring or change-detection mechanisms is used on audit logs t...', 'File integrity monitoring or change-detection mechanisms is used on audit logs to ensure that existing log data cannot be changed without generating alerts.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:01.171171', '2026-01-08 22:30:01.171171', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1090, '10.4', '10.4 - Audit logs are reviewed to identify anomalies or suspicious activity.', 'Audit logs are reviewed to identify anomalies or suspicious activity.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:01.294166', '2026-01-08 22:30:01.294166', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1091, '10.4.1', '10.4.1 - The following audit logs are reviewed at least once daily:     All security ev...', 'The following audit logs are reviewed at least once daily:
    All security events.
    Logs of all system components that store, process, or transmit CHD and/or SAD.
    Logs of all critical system components.
    Logs of all servers and system components that perform security functions (for example, network security controls, intrusion-detection systems/intrusion-prevention systems (IDS/IPS), authentication servers).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:01.417174', '2026-01-08 22:30:01.417174', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1092, '10.4.1.1', '10.4.1.1 - Automated mechanisms are used to perform audit log reviews.', 'Automated mechanisms are used to perform audit log reviews.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:01.534163', '2026-01-08 22:30:01.534163', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1093, '10.4.2', '10.4.2 - Logs of all other system components (those not specified in Requirement 10.4.1) ...', 'Logs of all other system components (those not specified in Requirement 10.4.1) are reviewed periodically.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:01.642457', '2026-01-08 22:30:01.642457', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1094, '10.4.2.1', '10.4.2.1 - The frequency of periodic log reviews for all other system components (not defin...', 'The frequency of periodic log reviews for all other system components (not defined in Requirement 10.4.1) is defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:01.748613', '2026-01-08 22:30:01.748613', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1095, '10.4.3', '10.4.3 - Exceptions and anomalies identified during the review process are addressed.', 'Exceptions and anomalies identified during the review process are addressed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:01.859202', '2026-01-08 22:30:01.859202', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1096, '10.5', '10.5 - Audit log history is retained and available for analysis.', 'Audit log history is retained and available for analysis.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:01.967699', '2026-01-08 22:30:01.967699', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1097, '10.5.1', '10.5.1 - Retain audit log history for at least 12 months, with at least the most recent t...', 'Retain audit log history for at least 12 months, with at least the most recent three months immediately available for analysis.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:02.076175', '2026-01-08 22:30:02.076175', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1098, '10.6', '10.6 - Time-synchronization mechanisms support consistent time settings across all syst...', 'Time-synchronization mechanisms support consistent time settings across all systems.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:02.180631', '2026-01-08 22:30:02.180631', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1099, '10.6.1', '10.6.1 - System clocks and time are synchronized using time-synchronization technology.', 'System clocks and time are synchronized using time-synchronization technology.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:02.28469', '2026-01-08 22:30:02.28469', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1100, '10.6.2', '10.6.2 - Systems are configured to the correct and consistent time as follows:     One ...', 'Systems are configured to the correct and consistent time as follows:
    One or more designated time servers are in use.
    Only the designated central time server(s) receives time from external sources.
    Time received from external sources is based on International Atomic Time or Coordinated Universal Time (UTC).
    The designated time server(s) accept time updates only from specific industry-accepted external sources.
    Where there is more than one designated time server, the time servers peer with one another to keep accurate time.
    Internal systems receive time information only from designated central time server(s).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:02.389438', '2026-01-08 22:30:02.389438', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1101, '10.6.3', '10.6.3 - Time synchronization settings and data are protected as follows:     Access to...', 'Time synchronization settings and data are protected as follows:
    Access to time data is restricted to only personnel with a business need.
    Any changes to time settings on critical systems are logged, monitored, and reviewed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:02.495618', '2026-01-08 22:30:02.495618', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1102, '10.7', '10.7 - Failures of critical security control systems are detected, reported, and respon...', 'Failures of critical security control systems are detected, reported, and responded to promptly.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:02.600179', '2026-01-08 22:30:02.600179', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1299, '6.5.3', '6.5.3 - Pre-production environments are separated from production environments and the s...', 'Pre-production environments are separated from production environments and the separation is enforced with access controls.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1103, '10.7.1', '10.7.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Failures of critical security...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Failures of critical security control systems are detected, alerted, and addressed promptly, including but not limited to failure of the following critical security control systems:
    Network security controls.
    IDS/IPS.
    FIM.
    Anti-malware solutions.
    Physical access controls.
    Logical access controls.
    Audit logging mechanisms.
    Segmentation controls (if used).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:02.708618', '2026-01-08 22:30:02.708618', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1104, '10.7.2', '10.7.2 - Failures of critical security control systems are detected, alerted, and address...', 'Failures of critical security control systems are detected, alerted, and addressed promptly, including but not limited to failure of the following critical security control systems:
    Network security controls.
    IDS/IPS.
    Change-detection mechanisms.
    Anti-malware solutions.
    Physical access controls.
    Logical access controls.
    Audit logging mechanisms.
    Segmentation controls (if used).
    Audit log review mechanisms.
    Automated security testing tools (if used).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:02.815375', '2026-01-08 22:30:02.815375', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1105, '10.7.3', '10.7.3 - Failures of any critical security controls systems are responded to promptly, in...', 'Failures of any critical security controls systems are responded to promptly, including but not limited to:
    Restoring security functions.
    Identifying and documenting the duration (date and time from start to end) of the security failure.
    Identifying and documenting the cause(s) of failure and documenting required remediation.
    Identifying and addressing any security issues that arose during the failure.
    Determining whether further actions are required as a result of the security failure.
    Implementing controls to prevent the cause of failure from reoccurring.
    Resuming monitoring of security controls.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:02.921992', '2026-01-08 22:30:02.921992', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1106, '11.1', '11.1 - Processes and mechanisms for regularly testing security of systems and networks ...', 'Processes and mechanisms for regularly testing security of systems and networks are defined and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:03.03968', '2026-01-08 22:30:03.03968', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1107, '11.1.1', '11.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 11 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:03.146647', '2026-01-08 22:30:03.146647', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1108, '11.1.2', '11.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 11 are docum...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 11 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:03.250165', '2026-01-08 22:30:03.250165', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1109, '11.2', '11.2 - Wireless access points are identified and monitored, and unauthorized wireless a...', 'Wireless access points are identified and monitored, and unauthorized wireless access points are addressed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:03.359103', '2026-01-08 22:30:03.359103', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1110, '11.2.1', '11.2.1 - Authorized and unauthorized wireless access points are managed as follows:    ...', 'Authorized and unauthorized wireless access points are managed as follows:
    The presence of wireless (Wi-Fi) access points is tested for,
    All authorized and unauthorized wireless access points are detected and identified,
    Testing, detection, and identification occurs at least once every three months.
    If automated monitoring is used, personnel are notified via generated alerts.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:03.469179', '2026-01-08 22:30:03.469179', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1111, '11.2.2', '11.2.2 - An inventory of authorized wireless access points is maintained, including a doc...', 'An inventory of authorized wireless access points is maintained, including a documented business justification.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:03.574206', '2026-01-08 22:30:03.574206', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1112, '11.3', '11.3 - External and internal vulnerabilities are regularly identified, prioritized, and...', 'External and internal vulnerabilities are regularly identified, prioritized, and addressed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:03.679643', '2026-01-08 22:30:03.679643', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1113, '11.3.1', '11.3.1 - Internal vulnerability scans are performed as follows:     At least once every...', 'Internal vulnerability scans are performed as follows:
    At least once every three months.
    High-risk and critical vulnerabilities (per the entity’s vulnerability risk rankings defined at Requirement 6.3.1) are resolved.
      Rescans are performed that confirm all high- risk and critical vulnerabilities (as noted above) have been resolved.
    Scan tool is kept up to date with latest vulnerability information.
    Scans are performed by qualified personnel and organizational independence of the tester exists.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:03.787199', '2026-01-08 22:30:03.787199', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1114, '11.3.1.1', '11.3.1.1 - All other applicable vulnerabilities (those not ranked as high-risk or critical ...', 'All other applicable vulnerabilities (those not ranked as high-risk or critical per the entity’s vulnerability risk rankings defined at Requirement
6.3.1) are managed as follows:
      Addressed based on the risk defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1.
      Rescans are conducted as needed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:03.894648', '2026-01-08 22:30:03.894648', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1115, '11.3.1.2', '11.3.1.2 - Internal vulnerability scans are performed via authenticated scanning as follows...', 'Internal vulnerability scans are performed via authenticated scanning as follows:
    Systems that are unable to accept credentials for authenticated scanning are documented.
    Sufficient privileges are used for those systems that accept credentials for scanning.
    If accounts used for authenticated scanning can be used for interactive login, they are managed in accordance with Requirement 8.2.2.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:04.001652', '2026-01-08 22:30:04.001652', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1116, '11.3.1.3', '11.3.1.3 - Internal vulnerability scans are performed after any significant change as follo...', 'Internal vulnerability scans are performed after any significant change as follows:
    High-risk and critical vulnerabilities (per the entity’s vulnerability risk rankings defined at Requirement 6.3.1) are resolved.
    Rescans are conducted as needed.
    Scans are performed by qualified personnel and organizational independence of the tester exists (not required to be a QSA or ASV).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:04.109713', '2026-01-08 22:30:04.109713', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1117, '11.3.2', '11.3.2 - External vulnerability scans are performed as follows:       At least once eve...', 'External vulnerability scans are performed as follows:
      At least once every three months.
      By a PCI SSC Approved Scanning Vendor (ASV).
      Vulnerabilities are resolved and ASV Program Guide requirements for a passing scan are met.
      Rescans are performed as needed to confirm that vulnerabilities are resolved per the ASV Program Guide requirements for a passing scan.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:04.215813', '2026-01-08 22:30:04.215813', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1118, '11.3.2.1', '11.3.2.1 - External vulnerability scans are performed after any significant change as follo...', 'External vulnerability scans are performed after any significant change as follows:
    Vulnerabilities that are scored 4.0 or higher by the CVSS are resolved.
    Rescans are conducted as needed.
    Scans are performed by qualified personnel and organizational independence of the tester exists (not required to be a QSA or ASV).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:04.321175', '2026-01-08 22:30:04.321175', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1119, '11.4', '11.4 - External and internal penetration testing is regularly performed, and exploitabl...', 'External and internal penetration testing is regularly performed, and exploitable vulnerabilities and security weaknesses are corrected.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:04.427182', '2026-01-08 22:30:04.427182', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1120, '11.4.1', '11.4.1 - A penetration testing methodology is defined, documented, and implemented by the...', 'A penetration testing methodology is defined, documented, and implemented by the entity, and includes:
    Industry-accepted penetration testing approaches.
    Coverage for the entire CDE perimeter and critical systems.
    Testing from both inside and outside the network.
    Testing to validate any segmentation and scope- reduction controls.
    Application-layer penetration testing to identify, at a minimum, the vulnerabilities listed in Requirement 6.2.4.
    Network-layer penetration tests that encompass all components that support network functions as well as operating systems.
    Review and consideration of threats and vulnerabilities experienced in the last 12 months.
    Documented approach to assessing and addressing the risk posed by exploitable vulnerabilities and security weaknesses found during penetration testing.
    Retention of penetration testing results and remediation activities results for at least 12 months.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:04.530664', '2026-01-08 22:30:04.530664', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1121, '11.4.2', '11.4.2 - Internal penetration testing is performed:     Per the entity’s defined method...', 'Internal penetration testing is performed:
    Per the entity’s defined methodology,
    At least once every 12 months
    After any significant infrastructure or application upgrade or change
    By a qualified internal resource or qualified external third-party
    Organizational independence of the tester exists (not required to be a QSA or ASV).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:04.635188', '2026-01-08 22:30:04.635188', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1122, '11.4.3', '11.4.3 - External penetration testing is performed:     Per the entity’s defined method...', 'External penetration testing is performed:
    Per the entity’s defined methodology
    At least once every 12 months
    After any significant infrastructure or application upgrade or change
    By a qualified internal resource or qualified external third party
    Organizational independence of the tester exists (not required to be a QSA or ASV).
(continued on next page)', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:04.784437', '2026-01-08 22:30:04.784437', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1123, '11.4.4', '11.4.4 - Exploitable vulnerabilities and security weaknesses found during penetration tes...', 'Exploitable vulnerabilities and security weaknesses found during penetration testing are corrected as follows:
    In accordance with the entity’s assessment of the risk posed by the security issue as defined in Requirement 6.3.1.
    Penetration testing is repeated to verify the corrections.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:04.913657', '2026-01-08 22:30:04.913657', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
    At least once every 12 months and after any changes to segmentation controls/methods
    Covering all segmentation controls/methods in use.
    According to the entity’s defined penetration testing methodology.
    Confirming that the segmentation controls/methods are operational and effective, and isolate the CDE from all out-of-scope systems.
    Confirming effectiveness of any use of isolation to separate systems with differing security levels (see Requirement 2.2.3).
    Performed by a qualified internal resource or qualified external third party.
    Organizational independence of the tester exists (not required to be a QSA or ASV).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:05.033438', '2026-01-08 22:30:05.033438', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1125, '11.4.6', '11.4.6 - Additional requirement for service providers only: If segmentation is used to is...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: If segmentation is used to isolate the CDE from other networks, penetration tests are performed on segmentation controls as follows:
    At least once every six months and after any changes to segmentation controls/methods.
    Covering all segmentation controls/methods in use.
    According to the entity’s defined penetration testing methodology.
    Confirming that the segmentation controls/methods are operational and effective, and isolate the CDE from all out-of-scope systems.
    Confirming effectiveness of any use of isolation to separate systems with differing security levels (see Requirement 2.2.3).
    Performed by a qualified internal resource or qualified external third party.
    Organizational independence of the tester exists (not required to be a QSA or ASV).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:05.13821', '2026-01-08 22:30:05.13821', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1126, '11.4.7', '11.4.7 - Additional requirement for multi-tenant service providers only: Multi-tenant ser...', 'Additional requirement for multi-tenant service providers only: Multi-tenant service providers support their customers for external penetration testing per Requirement 11.4.3 and 11.4.4.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:05.241654', '2026-01-08 22:30:05.241654', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1127, '11.5', '11.5 - Network intrusions and unexpected file changes are detected and responded to.', 'Network intrusions and unexpected file changes are detected and responded to.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:05.347243', '2026-01-08 22:30:05.347243', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1189, '1.2.6', '1.2.6 - Security features are defined and implemented for all services, protocols, and p...', 'Security features are defined and implemented for all services, protocols, and ports that are in use and considered to be insecure, such that the risk is mitigated.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1128, '11.5.1', '11.5.1 - Intrusion-detection and/or intrusion- prevention techniques are used to detect a...', 'Intrusion-detection and/or intrusion- prevention techniques are used to detect and/or prevent intrusions into the network as follows:
    All traffic is monitored at the perimeter of the CDE.
    All traffic is monitored at critical points in the CDE.
    Personnel are alerted to suspected compromises.
    All intrusion-detection and prevention engines, baselines, and signatures are kept up to date.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:05.45223', '2026-01-08 22:30:05.45223', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1129, '11.5.1.1', '11.5.1.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Intrusion-detection and/or in...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Intrusion-detection and/or intrusion-prevention techniques detect, alert on/prevent, and address covert malware communication channels.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:05.557194', '2026-01-08 22:30:05.557194', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1130, '11.5.2', '11.5.2 - A change-detection mechanism (for example, file integrity monitoring tools) is d...', 'A change-detection mechanism (for example, file integrity monitoring tools) is deployed as follows:
      To alert personnel to unauthorized modification (including changes, additions, and deletions) of critical files.
      To perform critical file comparisons at least once weekly.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:05.662158', '2026-01-08 22:30:05.662158', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1131, '11.6', '11.6 - Unauthorized changes on payment pages are detected and responded to.', 'Unauthorized changes on payment pages are detected and responded to.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:05.769169', '2026-01-08 22:30:05.769169', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1132, '11.6.1', '11.6.1 - A change- and tamper-detection mechanism is deployed as follows:     To alert ...', 'A change- and tamper-detection mechanism is deployed as follows:
    To alert personnel to unauthorized modification (including indicators of compromise, changes, additions, and deletions) to the HTTP headers and the contents of payment pages as received by the consumer browser.
    The mechanism is configured to evaluate the received HTTP header and payment page.
    The mechanism functions are performed as follows:
–    At least once every seven days
OR
–    Periodically (at the frequency defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:05.875253', '2026-01-08 22:30:05.875253', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1133, '12.1', '12.1 - A comprehensive information security policy that governs and provides direction ...', 'A comprehensive information security policy that governs and provides direction for protection of the entity’s information assets is known and current.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:05.98525', '2026-01-08 22:30:05.98525', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1134, '12.1.1', '12.1.1 - An overall information security policy is:     Established.     Published. ...', 'An overall information security policy is:
    Established.
    Published.
    Maintained.
    Disseminated to all relevant personnel, as well as to relevant vendors and business partners.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:06.092643', '2026-01-08 22:30:06.092643', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1135, '12.1.2', '12.1.2 - The information security policy is:     Reviewed at least once every 12 months...', 'The information security policy is:
    Reviewed at least once every 12 months.
    Updated as needed to reflect changes to business objectives or risks to the environment.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:06.198393', '2026-01-08 22:30:06.198393', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1136, '12.1.3', '12.1.3 - The security policy clearly defines information security roles and responsibilit...', 'The security policy clearly defines information security roles and responsibilities for all personnel, and all personnel are aware of and acknowledge their information security responsibilities.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:06.304667', '2026-01-08 22:30:06.304667', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1137, '12.1.4', '12.1.4 - Responsibility for information security is formally assigned to a Chief Informat...', 'Responsibility for information security is formally assigned to a Chief Information Security Officer or other information security knowledgeable member of executive management.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:06.414719', '2026-01-08 22:30:06.414719', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1138, '12.2', '12.2 - Acceptable use policies for end-user technologies are defined and implemented.', 'Acceptable use policies for end-user technologies are defined and implemented.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:06.519332', '2026-01-08 22:30:06.519332', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1139, '12.2.1', '12.2.1 - Acceptable use policies for end-user technologies are documented and implemented...', 'Acceptable use policies for end-user technologies are documented and implemented, including:
    Explicit approval by authorized parties.
    Acceptable uses of the technology.
    List of products approved by the company for employee use, including hardware and software.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:06.628742', '2026-01-08 22:30:06.628742', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1140, '12.3', '12.3 - Risks to the cardholder data environment are formally identified, evaluated, and...', 'Risks to the cardholder data environment are formally identified, evaluated, and managed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:06.737978', '2026-01-08 22:30:06.737978', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1141, '12.3.1', '12.3.1 - Each PCI DSS requirement that provides flexibility for how frequently it is perf...', 'Each PCI DSS requirement that provides flexibility for how frequently it is performed (for example, requirements to be performed periodically) is supported by a targeted risk analysis that is documented and includes:
    Identification of the assets being protected.
    Identification of the threat(s) that the requirement is protecting against.
    Identification of factors that contribute to the likelihood and/or impact of a threat being realized.
    Resulting analysis that determines, and includes justification for, how frequently the requirement must be performed to minimize the likelihood of the threat being realized.
    Review of each targeted risk analysis at least once every 12 months to determine whether the results are still valid or if an updated risk analysis is needed.
    Performance of updated risk analyses when needed, as determined by the annual review.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:06.848717', '2026-01-08 22:30:06.848717', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1142, '12.3.2', '12.3.2 - A targeted risk analysis is performed for each PCI DSS requirement that the enti...', 'A targeted risk analysis is performed for each PCI DSS requirement that the entity meets with the customized approach, to include:
    Documented evidence detailing each element specified in Appendix D: Customized Approach (including, at a minimum, a controls matrix and risk analysis).
    Approval of documented evidence by senior management.
    Performance of the targeted analysis of risk at least once every 12 months.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:06.955686', '2026-01-08 22:30:06.955686', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1143, '12.3.3', '12.3.3 - Cryptographic cipher suites and protocols in use are documented and reviewed at ...', 'Cryptographic cipher suites and protocols in use are documented and reviewed at least once every 12 months, including at least the following:
    An up-to-date inventory of all cryptographic cipher suites and protocols in use, including purpose and where used.
    Active monitoring of industry trends regarding continued viability of all cryptographic cipher suites and protocols in use.
    A documented strategy to respond to anticipated changes in cryptographic vulnerabilities.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:07.063252', '2026-01-08 22:30:07.063252', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1144, '12.3.4', '12.3.4 - Hardware and software technologies in use are reviewed at least once every 12 mo...', 'Hardware and software technologies in use are reviewed at least once every 12 months, including at least the following:
    Analysis that the technologies continue to receive security fixes from vendors promptly.
    Analysis that the technologies continue to support (and do not preclude) the entity’s PCI DSS compliance.
    Documentation of any industry announcements or trends related to a technology, such as when a vendor has announced “end of life” plans for a technology.
    Documentation of a plan, approved by senior management, to remediate outdated technologies, including those for which vendors have announced “end of life” plans.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:07.168674', '2026-01-08 22:30:07.168674', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1145, '12.4', '12.4 - PCI DSS compliance is managed.', 'PCI DSS compliance is managed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:07.278219', '2026-01-08 22:30:07.278219', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1146, '12.4.1', '12.4.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Responsibility is established...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Responsibility is established by executive management for the protection of cardholder data and a PCI DSS compliance program to include:
    Overall accountability for maintaining PCI DSS compliance.
    Defining a charter for a PCI DSS compliance program and communication to executive management.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:07.382342', '2026-01-08 22:30:07.382342', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1147, '12.4.2', '12.4.2 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Reviews are performed at leas...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Reviews are performed at least once every three months to confirm that personnel are performing their tasks in accordance with all security policies and operational procedures. Reviews are performed by personnel other than those responsible for performing the given task and include, but are not limited to, the following tasks:
    Daily log reviews.
    Configuration reviews for network security controls.
    Applying configuration standards to new systems.
    Responding to security alerts.
    Change-management processes.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:07.488289', '2026-01-08 22:30:07.488289', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1148, '12.4.2.1', '12.4.2.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Reviews conducted in accordan...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Reviews conducted in accordance with Requirement 12.4.2 are documented to include:
    Results of the reviews.
    Documented remediation actions taken for any tasks that were found to not be performed at Requirement 12.4.2.
    Review and sign-off of results by personnel assigned responsibility for the PCI DSS compliance program.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:07.595731', '2026-01-08 22:30:07.595731', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1149, '12.5', '12.5 - PCI DSS scope is documented and validated.', 'PCI DSS scope is documented and validated.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:07.700248', '2026-01-08 22:30:07.700248', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1150, '12.5.1', '12.5.1 - An inventory of system components that are in scope for PCI DSS, including a des...', 'An inventory of system components that are in scope for PCI DSS, including a description of function/use, is maintained and kept current.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:07.807718', '2026-01-08 22:30:07.807718', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1151, '12.5.2', '12.5.2 - PCI DSS scope is documented and confirmed by the entity at least once every 12 m...', 'PCI DSS scope is documented and confirmed by the entity at least once every 12 months and upon significant change to the in-scope environment. At a minimum, the scoping validation includes:
    Identifying all data flows for the various payment stages (for example, authorization, capture settlement, chargebacks, and refunds) and acceptance channels (for example, card-present, card-not-present, and e-commerce).
    Updating all data-flow diagrams per Requirement 1.2.4.
    Identifying all locations where account data is stored, processed, and transmitted, including but not limited to: 1) any locations outside of the currently defined CDE, 2) applications that process CHD, 3) transmissions between systems and networks, and 4) file backups.
    Identifying all system components in the CDE, connected to the CDE, or that could impact security of the CDE.
    Identifying all segmentation controls in use and the environment(s) from which the CDE is segmented, including justification for environments being out of scope.
    Identifying all connections from third-party entities with access to the CDE.
    Confirming that all identified data flows, account data, system components, segmentation controls, and connections from third parties with access to the CDE are included in scope.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:07.930851', '2026-01-08 22:30:07.930851', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1152, '12.5.2.1', '12.5.2.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: PCI DSS scope is documented a...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: PCI DSS scope is documented and confirmed by the entity at least once every six months and upon significant change to the in-scope environment. At a minimum, the scoping validation includes all the elements specified in Requirement 12.5.2.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:08.058297', '2026-01-08 22:30:08.058297', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1153, '12.5.3', '12.5.3 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Significant changes to organi...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Significant changes to organizational structure result in a documented (internal) review of the impact to PCI DSS scope and applicability of controls, with results communicated to executive management.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:08.167708', '2026-01-08 22:30:08.167708', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1154, '12.6', '12.6 - Security awareness education is an ongoing activity.', 'Security awareness education is an ongoing activity.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:08.311526', '2026-01-08 22:30:08.311526', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1155, '12.6.1', '12.6.1 - A formal security awareness program is implemented to make all personnel aware o...', 'A formal security awareness program is implemented to make all personnel aware of the entity’s information security policy and procedures, and their role in protecting the cardholder data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:08.434252', '2026-01-08 22:30:08.434252', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1156, '12.6.2', '12.6.2 - The security awareness program is:     Reviewed at least once every 12 months,...', 'The security awareness program is:
    Reviewed at least once every 12 months, and
    Updated as needed to address any new threats and vulnerabilities that may impact the security of the entity’s CDE, or the information provided to personnel about their role in protecting cardholder data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:08.546017', '2026-01-08 22:30:08.546017', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1157, '12.6.3', '12.6.3 - Personnel receive security awareness training as follows:     Upon hire and at...', 'Personnel receive security awareness training as follows:
    Upon hire and at least once every 12 months.
    Multiple methods of communication are used.
    Personnel acknowledge at least once every 12 months that they have read and understood the information security policy and procedures.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:08.654675', '2026-01-08 22:30:08.654675', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1158, '12.6.3.1', '12.6.3.1 - Security awareness training includes awareness of threats and vulnerabilities th...', 'Security awareness training includes awareness of threats and vulnerabilities that could impact the security of the CDE, including but not limited to:
    Phishing and related attacks.
    Social engineering.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:08.75976', '2026-01-08 22:30:08.75976', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1159, '12.6.3.2', '12.6.3.2 - Security awareness training includes awareness about the acceptable use of end-u...', 'Security awareness training includes awareness about the acceptable use of end-user technologies in accordance with Requirement 12.2.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:08.87528', '2026-01-08 22:30:08.87528', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1160, '12.7', '12.7 - Personnel are screened to reduce risks from insider threats.', 'Personnel are screened to reduce risks from insider threats.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:08.984709', '2026-01-08 22:30:08.984709', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1161, '12.7.1', '12.7.1 - Potential personnel who will have access to the CDE are screened, within the con...', 'Potential personnel who will have access to the CDE are screened, within the constraints of local laws, prior to hire to minimize the risk of attacks from internal sources.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:09.089254', '2026-01-08 22:30:09.089254', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1162, '12.8', '12.8 - Risk to information assets associated with third-party service provider (TPSP) r...', 'Risk to information assets associated with third-party service provider (TPSP) relationships is managed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:09.19987', '2026-01-08 22:30:09.19987', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1163, '12.8.1', '12.8.1 - A list of all third-party service providers (TPSPs) with which account data is s...', 'A list of all third-party service providers (TPSPs) with which account data is shared or that could affect the security of account data is maintained, including a description for each of the services provided.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:09.307377', '2026-01-08 22:30:09.307377', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1164, '12.8.2', '12.8.2 - Written agreements with TPSPs are maintained as follows:     Written agreement...', 'Written agreements with TPSPs are maintained as follows:
    Written agreements are maintained with all TPSPs with which account data is shared or that could affect the security of the CDE.
    Written agreements include acknowledgments from TPSPs that they are responsible for the security of account data the TPSPs possess or otherwise store, process, or transmit on behalf of the entity, or to the extent that they could impact the security of the entity’s CDE.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:09.41327', '2026-01-08 22:30:09.41327', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1165, '12.8.3', '12.8.3 - An established process is implemented for engaging TPSPs, including proper due d...', 'An established process is implemented for engaging TPSPs, including proper due diligence prior to engagement.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:09.518321', '2026-01-08 22:30:09.518321', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1166, '12.8.4', '12.8.4 - A program is implemented to monitor TPSPs’ PCI DSS compliance status at least on...', 'A program is implemented to monitor TPSPs’ PCI DSS compliance status at least once every 12 months.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:09.623228', '2026-01-08 22:30:09.623228', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1167, '12.8.5', '12.8.5 - Information is maintained about which PCI DSS requirements are managed by each T...', 'Information is maintained about which PCI DSS requirements are managed by each TPSP, which are managed by the entity, and any that are shared between the TPSP and the entity.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:09.729783', '2026-01-08 22:30:09.729783', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1168, '12.9', '12.9 - Third-party service providers (TPSPs) support their customers’ PCI DSS complianc...', 'Third-party service providers (TPSPs) support their customers’ PCI DSS compliance.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:09.834712', '2026-01-08 22:30:09.834712', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1169, '12.9.1', '12.9.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: TPSPs acknowledge in writing ...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: TPSPs acknowledge in writing to customers that they are responsible for the security of account data the TPSP possesses or otherwise stores, processes, or transmits on behalf of the customer, or to the extent that they could impact the security of the customer’s CDE.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:09.946157', '2026-01-08 22:30:09.946157', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1170, '12.9.2', '12.9.2 - Additional requirement for service providers only: TPSPs support their customers...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: TPSPs support their customers’ requests for information to meet Requirements
12.8.4 and 12.8.5 by providing the following upon customer request:
    PCI DSS compliance status information for any service the TPSP performs on behalf of customers (Requirement 12.8.4).
    Information about which PCI DSS requirements are the responsibility of the TPSP and which are the responsibility of the customer, including any shared responsibilities (Requirement 12.8.5).', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:10.053243', '2026-01-08 22:30:10.053243', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1171, '12.10', '12.10 - Suspected and confirmed security incidents that could impact the CDE are respond...', 'Suspected and confirmed security incidents that could impact the CDE are responded to immediately.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:10.161759', '2026-01-08 22:30:10.161759', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1190, '1.2.7', '1.2.7 - Configurations of NSCs are reviewed at least once every six months to confirm th...', 'Configurations of NSCs are reviewed at least once every six months to confirm they are relevant and effective.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1191, '1.2.8', '1.2.8 - Configuration files for NSCs are:       Secured from unauthorized access.   ...', 'Configuration files for NSCs are:
      Secured from unauthorized access.
      Kept consistent with active network configurations.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1172, '12.10.1', '12.10.1 - An incident response plan exists and is ready to be activated in the event of a ...', 'An incident response plan exists and is ready to be activated in the event of a suspected or confirmed security incident. The plan includes, but is not limited to:
    Roles, responsibilities, and communication and contact strategies in the event of a suspected or confirmed security incident, including notification of payment brands and acquirers, at a minimum.
    Incident response procedures with specific containment and mitigation activities for different types of incidents.
    Business recovery and continuity procedures.
    Data backup processes.
    Analysis of legal requirements for reporting compromises.
    Coverage and responses of all critical system components.
    Reference or inclusion of incident response procedures from the payment brands.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:10.269661', '2026-01-08 22:30:10.269661', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1173, '12.10.2', '12.10.2 - At least once every 12 months, the security incident response plan is:     Rev...', 'At least once every 12 months, the security incident response plan is:
    Reviewed and the content is updated as needed.
    Tested, including all elements listed in Requirement 12.10.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:10.380811', '2026-01-08 22:30:10.380811', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1174, '12.10.3', '12.10.3 - Specific personnel are designated to be available on a 24/7 basis to respond to ...', 'Specific personnel are designated to be available on a 24/7 basis to respond to suspected or confirmed security incidents.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:10.488153', '2026-01-08 22:30:10.488153', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1175, '12.10.4', '12.10.4 - Personnel responsible for responding to suspected and confirmed security inciden...', 'Personnel responsible for responding to suspected and confirmed security incidents are appropriately and periodically trained on their incident response responsibilities.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:10.599346', '2026-01-08 22:30:10.599346', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1176, '12.10.4.1', '12.10.4.1 - The frequency of periodic training for incident response personnel is defined in...', 'The frequency of periodic training for incident response personnel is defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:10.704263', '2026-01-08 22:30:10.704263', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1177, '12.10.5', '12.10.5 - The security incident response plan includes monitoring and responding to alerts...', 'The security incident response plan includes monitoring and responding to alerts from security monitoring systems, including but not limited to:
    Intrusion-detection and intrusion-prevention systems.
    Network security controls.
    Change-detection mechanisms for critical files.
    The change-and tamper-detection mechanism for payment pages. This bullet is a best practice until its effective date; refer to Applicability Notes below for details.
    Detection of unauthorized wireless access points.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:10.814278', '2026-01-08 22:30:10.814278', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1178, '12.10.6', '12.10.6 - The security incident response plan is modified and evolved according to lessons...', 'The security incident response plan is modified and evolved according to lessons learned and to incorporate industry developments.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:10.921321', '2026-01-08 22:30:10.921321', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1179, '12.10.7', '12.10.7 - Incident response procedures are in place, to be initiated upon the detection of...', 'Incident response procedures are in place, to be initiated upon the detection of stored PAN anywhere it is not expected, and include:
    Determining what to do if PAN is discovered outside the CDE, including its retrieval, secure deletion, and/or migration into the currently defined CDE, as applicable.
    Identifying whether sensitive authentication data is stored with PAN.
    Determining where the account data came from and how it ended up where it was not expected.
    Remediating data leaks or process gaps that resulted in the account data being where it was not expected.', 'PCI DSS v4.0', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:30:11.029241', '2026-01-08 22:30:11.029241', NULL, 'Refer to official PCI DSS v4.0 standard.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1180, '1.1', '1.1 - Processes and mechanisms for installing and maintaining network security control...', 'Processes and mechanisms for installing and maintaining network security controls are defined and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1181, '1.1.1', '1.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 1 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1182, '1.1.2', '1.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 1 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 1 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1183, '1.2', '1.2 - Network security controls (NSCs) are configured and maintained.', 'Network security controls (NSCs) are configured and maintained.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1184, '1.2.1', '1.2.1 - Configuration standards for NSC rulesets are:     Defined.     Implemented. ...', 'Configuration standards for NSC rulesets are:
    Defined.
    Implemented.
    Maintained.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1185, '1.2.2', '1.2.2 - All changes to network connections and to configurations of NSCs are approved an...', 'All changes to network connections and to configurations of NSCs are approved and managed in accordance with the change control process defined at Requirement 6.5.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1186, '1.2.3', '1.2.3 - An accurate network diagram(s) is maintained that shows all connections between ...', 'An accurate network diagram(s) is maintained that shows all connections between the CDE and other networks, including any wireless networks.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1187, '1.2.4', '1.2.4 - An accurate data-flow diagram(s) is maintained that meets the following:     S...', 'An accurate data-flow diagram(s) is maintained that meets the following:
    Shows all account data flows across systems and networks.
    Updated as needed upon changes to the environment.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1188, '1.2.5', '1.2.5 - All services, protocols, and ports allowed are identified, approved, and have a ...', 'All services, protocols, and ports allowed are identified, approved, and have a defined business need.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1194, '1.3.2', '1.3.2 - Outbound traffic from the CDE is restricted as follows:     To only traffic th...', 'Outbound traffic from the CDE is restricted as follows:
    To only traffic that is necessary.
    All other traffic is specifically denied.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1195, '1.3.3', '1.3.3 - NSCs are installed between all wireless networks and the CDE, regardless of whet...', 'NSCs are installed between all wireless networks and the CDE, regardless of whether the wireless network is a CDE, such that:
    All wireless traffic from wireless networks into the CDE is denied by default.
    Only wireless traffic with an authorized business purpose is allowed into the CDE.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1196, '1.4', '1.4 - Network connections between trusted and untrusted networks are controlled.', 'Network connections between trusted and untrusted networks are controlled.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1197, '1.4.1', '1.4.1 - NSCs are implemented between trusted and untrusted networks.', 'NSCs are implemented between trusted and untrusted networks.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1198, '1.4.2', '1.4.2 - Inbound traffic from untrusted networks to trusted networks is restricted to: ...', 'Inbound traffic from untrusted networks to trusted networks is restricted to:
    Communications with system components that are authorized to provide publicly accessible services, protocols, and ports.
    Stateful responses to communications initiated by system components in a trusted network.
    All other traffic is denied.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1199, '1.4.3', '1.4.3 - Anti-spoofing measures are implemented to detect and block forged source IP addr...', 'Anti-spoofing measures are implemented to detect and block forged source IP addresses from entering the trusted network.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1200, '1.4.4', '1.4.4 - System components that store cardholder data are not directly accessible from un...', 'System components that store cardholder data are not directly accessible from untrusted networks.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1201, '1.4.5', '1.4.5 - The disclosure of internal IP addresses and routing information is limited to on...', 'The disclosure of internal IP addresses and routing information is limited to only authorized parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1202, '1.5', '1.5 - Risks to the CDE from computing devices that are able to connect to both untrust...', 'Risks to the CDE from computing devices that are able to connect to both untrusted networks and the CDE are mitigated.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1203, '1.5.1', '1.5.1 - Security controls are implemented on any computing devices, including company- a...', 'Security controls are implemented on any computing devices, including company- and employee-owned devices, that connect to both untrusted networks (including the Internet) and the CDE as follows:
      Specific configuration settings are defined to prevent threats being introduced into the entity’s network.
      Security controls are actively running.
      Security controls are not alterable by users of the computing devices unless specifically documented and authorized by management on a case-by-case basis for a limited period.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 1', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1204, '2.1', '2.1 - Processes and mechanisms for applying secure configurations to all system compon...', 'Processes and mechanisms for applying secure configurations to all system components are defined and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 2', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1205, '2.1.1', '2.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 2 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 2', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1206, '2.1.2', '2.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 2 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 2 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 2', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1207, '2.2', '2.2 - System components are configured and managed securely.', 'System components are configured and managed securely.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 2', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1208, '2.2.1', '2.2.1 - Configuration standards are developed, implemented, and maintained to:     Cov...', 'Configuration standards are developed, implemented, and maintained to:
    Cover all system components.
    Address all known security vulnerabilities.
    Be consistent with industry-accepted system hardening standards or vendor hardening recommendations.
    Be updated as new vulnerability issues are identified, as defined in Requirement 6.3.1.
    Be applied when new systems are configured and verified as in place before or immediately after a system component is connected to a production environment.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 2', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1209, '2.2.2', '2.2.2 - Vendor default accounts are managed as follows:     If the vendor default acco...', 'Vendor default accounts are managed as follows:
    If the vendor default account(s) will be used, the default password is changed per Requirement 8.3.6.
    If the vendor default account(s) will not be used, the account is removed or disabled.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 2', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1210, '2.2.3', '2.2.3 - Primary functions requiring different security levels are managed as follows: ...', 'Primary functions requiring different security levels are managed as follows:
    Only one primary function exists on a system component,
OR
    Primary functions with differing security levels that exist on the same system component are isolated from each other,
OR', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 2', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1211, '2.2.4', '2.2.4 - Only necessary services, protocols, daemons, and functions are enabled, and all ...', 'Only necessary services, protocols, daemons, and functions are enabled, and all unnecessary functionality is removed or disabled.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 2', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1212, '2.2.5', '2.2.5 - If any insecure services, protocols, or daemons are present:     Business just...', 'If any insecure services, protocols, or daemons are present:
    Business justification is documented.
    Additional security features are documented and implemented that reduce the risk of using insecure services, protocols, or daemons.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 2', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1216, '2.3.1', '2.3.1 - For wireless environments connected to the CDE or transmitting account data, all...', 'For wireless environments connected to the CDE or transmitting account data, all wireless vendor defaults are changed at installation or are confirmed to be secure, including but not limited to:
    Default wireless encryption keys.
    Passwords on wireless access points.
    SNMP defaults.
    Any other security-related wireless vendor defaults.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 2', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1217, '2.3.2', '2.3.2 - For wireless environments connected to the CDE or transmitting account data, wir...', 'For wireless environments connected to the CDE or transmitting account data, wireless encryption keys are changed as follows:
    Whenever personnel with knowledge of the key leave the company or the role for which the knowledge was necessary.
    Whenever a key is suspected of or known to be compromised.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 2', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1218, '3.1', '3.1 - Processes and mechanisms for protecting stored account data are defined and unde...', 'Processes and mechanisms for protecting stored account data are defined and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1219, '3.1.1', '3.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 3 are:
      Documented.
      Kept up to date.
      In use.
      Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1220, '3.1.2', '3.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 3 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 3 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1221, '3.2', '3.2 - Storage of account data is kept to a minimum.', 'Storage of account data is kept to a minimum.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1222, '3.2.1', '3.2.1 - Account data storage is kept to a minimum through implementation of data retenti...', 'Account data storage is kept to a minimum through implementation of data retention and disposal policies, procedures, and processes that include at least the following:
    Coverage for all locations of stored account data.
    Coverage for any sensitive authentication data (SAD) stored prior to completion of authorization. This bullet is a best practice until its effective date; refer to Applicability Notes below for details.
    Limiting data storage amount and retention time to that which is required for legal or regulatory, and/or business requirements.
    Specific retention requirements for stored account data that defines length of retention period and includes a documented business justification.
    Processes for secure deletion or rendering account data unrecoverable when no longer needed per the retention policy.
    A process for verifying, at least once every three months, that stored account data exceeding the defined retention period has been securely deleted or rendered unrecoverable.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1223, '3.3', '3.3 - Sensitive authentication data (SAD) is not stored after authorization.', 'Sensitive authentication data (SAD) is not stored after authorization.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1224, '3.3.1', '3.3.1 - SAD is not retained after authorization, even if encrypted. All sensitive authen...', 'SAD is not retained after authorization, even if encrypted. All sensitive authentication data received is rendered unrecoverable upon completion of the authorization process.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1225, '3.3.1.1', '3.3.1.1 - The full contents of any track are not retained upon completion of the authoriza...', 'The full contents of any track are not retained upon completion of the authorization process.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1226, '3.3.1.2', '3.3.1.2 - The card verification code is not retained upon completion of the authorization ...', 'The card verification code is not retained upon completion of the authorization process.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1227, '3.3.1.3', '3.3.1.3 - The personal identification number (PIN) and the PIN block are not retained upon...', 'The personal identification number (PIN) and the PIN block are not retained upon completion of the authorization process.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1228, '3.3.2', '3.3.2 - SAD that is stored electronically prior to completion of authorization is encryp...', 'SAD that is stored electronically prior to completion of authorization is encrypted using strong cryptography.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
      Limited to that which is needed for a legitimate issuing business need and is secured.
      Encrypted using strong cryptography. This bullet is a best practice until its effective date; refer to Applicability Notes below for details.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1230, '3.4', '3.4 - Access to displays of full PAN and ability to copy PAN is restricted.', 'Access to displays of full PAN and ability to copy PAN is restricted.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1231, '3.4.1', '3.4.1 - PAN is masked when displayed (the BIN and last four digits are the maximum numbe...', 'PAN is masked when displayed (the BIN and last four digits are the maximum number of digits to be displayed), such that only personnel with a legitimate business need can see more than the BIN and last four digits of the PAN.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1232, '3.4.2', '3.4.2 - When using remote-access technologies, technical controls prevent copy and/or re...', 'When using remote-access technologies, technical controls prevent copy and/or relocation of PAN for all personnel, except for those with documented, explicit authorization and a legitimate, defined business need.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1233, '3.5', '3.5 - Primary account number (PAN) is secured wherever it is stored.', 'Primary account number (PAN) is secured wherever it is stored.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1298, '6.5.2', '6.5.2 - Upon completion of a significant change, all applicable PCI DSS requirements are...', 'Upon completion of a significant change, all applicable PCI DSS requirements are confirmed to be in place on all new or changed systems and networks, and documentation is updated as applicable.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1234, '3.5.1', '3.5.1 - PAN is rendered unreadable anywhere it is stored by using any of the following a...', 'PAN is rendered unreadable anywhere it is stored by using any of the following approaches:
    One-way hashes based on strong cryptography of the entire PAN.
    Truncation (hashing cannot be used to replace the truncated segment of PAN).
–    If hashed and truncated versions of the same PAN, or different truncation formats of the same PAN, are present in an environment, additional controls are in place such that the different versions cannot be correlated to reconstruct the original PAN.
    Index tokens.
    Strong cryptography with associated key- management processes and procedures.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1235, '3.5.1.1', '3.5.1.1 - Hashes used to render PAN unreadable (per the first bullet of Requirement 3.5.1)...', 'Hashes used to render PAN unreadable (per the first bullet of Requirement 3.5.1) are keyed cryptographic hashes of the entire PAN, with associated key-management processes and procedures in accordance with Requirements 3.6 and 3.7.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1236, '3.5.1.2', '3.5.1.2 - If disk-level or partition-level encryption (rather than file-, column-, or fiel...', 'If disk-level or partition-level encryption (rather than file-, column-, or field-level database encryption) is used to render PAN unreadable, it is implemented only as follows:
    On removable electronic media
OR
    If used for non-removable electronic media, PAN is also rendered unreadable via another mechanism that meets Requirement 3.5.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1237, '3.5.1.3', '3.5.1.3 - If disk-level or partition-level encryption is used (rather than file-, column-,...', 'If disk-level or partition-level encryption is used (rather than file-, column-, or field--level database encryption) to render PAN unreadable, it is managed as follows:
      Logical access is managed separately and independently of native operating system authentication and access control mechanisms.
      Decryption keys are not associated with user accounts.
      Authentication factors (passwords, passphrases, or cryptographic keys) that allow access to unencrypted data are stored securely.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1238, '3.6', '3.6 - Cryptographic keys used to protect stored account data are secured.', 'Cryptographic keys used to protect stored account data are secured.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1239, '3.6.1', '3.6.1 - Procedures are defined and implemented to protect cryptographic keys used to pro...', 'Procedures are defined and implemented to protect cryptographic keys used to protect stored account data against disclosure and misuse that include:
    Access to keys is restricted to the fewest number of custodians necessary.
    Key-encrypting keys are at least as strong as the data-encrypting keys they protect.
    Key-encrypting keys are stored separately from data-encrypting keys.
    Keys are stored securely in the fewest possible locations and forms.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1240, '3.6.1.1', '3.6.1.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: A documented description of t...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: A documented description of the cryptographic architecture is maintained that includes:
    Details of all algorithms, protocols, and keys used for the protection of stored account data, including key strength and expiry date.
    Preventing the use of the same cryptographic keys in production and test environments. This bullet is a best practice until its effective date; refer to Applicability Notes below for details.
    Description of the key usage for each key.
    Inventory of any hardware security modules (HSMs), key management systems (KMS), and other secure cryptographic devices (SCDs) used for key management, including type and location of devices, as outlined in Requirement 12.3.4.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1241, '3.6.1.2', '3.6.1.2 - Secret and private keys used to encrypt/decrypt stored account data are stored i...', 'Secret and private keys used to encrypt/decrypt stored account data are stored in one (or more) of the following forms at all times:
    Encrypted with a key-encrypting key that is at least as strong as the data-encrypting key, and that is stored separately from the data- encrypting key.
    Within a secure cryptographic device (SCD), such as a hardware security module (HSM) or PTS-approved point-of-interaction device.
    As at least two full-length key components or key shares, in accordance with an industry-accepted method.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1242, '3.6.1.3', '3.6.1.3 - Access to cleartext cryptographic key components is restricted to the fewest num...', 'Access to cleartext cryptographic key components is restricted to the fewest number of custodians necessary.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1243, '3.6.1.4', '3.6.1.4 - Cryptographic keys are stored in the fewest possible locations.', 'Cryptographic keys are stored in the fewest possible locations.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1244, '3.7', '3.7 - Where cryptography is used to protect stored account data, key management proces...', 'Where cryptography is used to protect stored account data, key management processes and procedures covering all aspects of the key lifecycle are defined and implemented.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1245, '3.7.1', '3.7.1 - Key-management policies and procedures are implemented to include generation of ...', 'Key-management policies and procedures are implemented to include generation of strong cryptographic keys used to protect stored account data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1246, '3.7.2', '3.7.2 - Key-management policies and procedures are implemented to include secure distrib...', 'Key-management policies and procedures are implemented to include secure distribution of cryptographic keys used to protect stored account data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1247, '3.7.3', '3.7.3 - Key-management policies and procedures are implemented to include secure storage...', 'Key-management policies and procedures are implemented to include secure storage of cryptographic keys used to protect stored account data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1248, '3.7.4', '3.7.4 - Key management policies and procedures are implemented for cryptographic key cha...', 'Key management policies and procedures are implemented for cryptographic key changes for keys that have reached the end of their cryptoperiod, as defined by the associated application vendor or key owner, and based on industry best practices and guidelines, including the following:
    A defined cryptoperiod for each key type in use.
    A process for key changes at the end of the defined cryptoperiod.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1249, '3.7.5', '3.7.5 - Key management policies procedures are implemented to include the retirement, re...', 'Key management policies procedures are implemented to include the retirement, replacement, or destruction of keys used to protect stored account data, as deemed necessary when:
    The key has reached the end of its defined cryptoperiod.
    The integrity of the key has been weakened, including when personnel with knowledge of a cleartext key component leaves the company, or the role for which the key component was known.
    The key is suspected of or known to be compromised.
Retired or replaced keys are not used for encryption operations.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1250, '3.7.6', '3.7.6 - Where manual cleartext cryptographic key- management operations are performed by...', 'Where manual cleartext cryptographic key- management operations are performed by personnel, key-management policies and procedures are implemented include managing these operations using split knowledge and dual control.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1251, '3.7.7', '3.7.7 - Key management policies and procedures are implemented to include the prevention...', 'Key management policies and procedures are implemented to include the prevention of unauthorized substitution of cryptographic keys.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1252, '3.7.8', '3.7.8 - Key management policies and procedures are implemented to include that cryptogra...', 'Key management policies and procedures are implemented to include that cryptographic key custodians formally acknowledge (in writing or electronically) that they understand and accept their key-custodian responsibilities.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1253, '3.7.9', '3.7.9 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Where a service provider shar...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Where a service provider shares cryptographic keys with its customers for transmission or storage of account data, guidance on secure transmission, storage and updating of such keys is documented and distributed to the service provider’s customers.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 3', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1254, '4.1', '4.1 - Processes and mechanisms for protecting cardholder data with strong cryptography...', 'Processes and mechanisms for protecting cardholder data with strong cryptography during transmission over open, public networks are defined and documented.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1255, '4.1.1', '4.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 4 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1256, '4.1.2', '4.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 4 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 4 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1257, '4.2', '4.2 - PAN is protected with strong cryptography during transmission.', 'PAN is protected with strong cryptography during transmission.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1258, '4.2.1', '4.2.1 - Strong cryptography and security protocols are implemented as follows to safegua...', 'Strong cryptography and security protocols are implemented as follows to safeguard PAN during transmission over open, public networks:
    Only trusted keys and certificates are accepted.
    Certificates used to safeguard PAN during transmission over open, public networks are confirmed as valid and are not expired or revoked. This bullet is a best practice until its effective date; refer to applicability notes below for details.
    The protocol in use supports only secure versions or configurations and does not support fallback to, or use of insecure versions, algorithms, key sizes, or implementations.
    The encryption strength is appropriate for the encryption methodology in use.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1259, '4.2.1.1', '4.2.1.1 - An inventory of the entity’s trusted keys and certificates used to protect PAN d...', 'An inventory of the entity’s trusted keys and certificates used to protect PAN during transmission is maintained.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1260, '4.2.1.2', '4.2.1.2 - Wireless networks transmitting PAN or connected to the CDE use industry best pra...', 'Wireless networks transmitting PAN or connected to the CDE use industry best practices to implement strong cryptography for authentication and transmission.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1261, '4.2.2', '4.2.2 - PAN is secured with strong cryptography whenever it is sent via end-user messagi...', 'PAN is secured with strong cryptography whenever it is sent via end-user messaging technologies.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 4', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1262, '5.1', '5.1 - Processes and mechanisms for protecting all systems and networks from malicious ...', 'Processes and mechanisms for protecting all systems and networks from malicious software are defined and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1263, '5.1.1', '5.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 5 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1264, '5.1.2', '5.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 5 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 5 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1265, '5.2', '5.2 - Malicious software (malware) is prevented, or detected and addressed.', 'Malicious software (malware) is prevented, or detected and addressed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1266, '5.2.1', '5.2.1 - An anti-malware solution(s) is deployed on all system components, except for tho...', 'An anti-malware solution(s) is deployed on all system components, except for those system components identified in periodic evaluations per Requirement 5.2.3 that concludes the system components are not at risk from malware.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1267, '5.2.2', '5.2.2 - The deployed anti-malware solution(s):     Detects all known types of malware....', 'The deployed anti-malware solution(s):
    Detects all known types of malware.
    Removes, blocks, or contains all known types of malware.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1268, '5.2.3', '5.2.3 - Any system components that are not at risk for malware are evaluated periodicall...', 'Any system components that are not at risk for malware are evaluated periodically to include the following:
      A documented list of all system components not at risk for malware.
      Identification and evaluation of evolving malware threats for those system components.
      Confirmation whether such system components continue to not require anti-malware protection.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1269, '5.2.3.1', '5.2.3.1 - The frequency of periodic evaluations of system components identified as not at ...', 'The frequency of periodic evaluations of system components identified as not at risk for malware is defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1270, '5.3', '5.3 - Anti-malware mechanisms and processes are active, maintained, and monitored.', 'Anti-malware mechanisms and processes are active, maintained, and monitored.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1271, '5.3.1', '5.3.1 - The anti-malware solution(s) is kept current via automatic updates.', 'The anti-malware solution(s) is kept current via automatic updates.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1272, '5.3.2', '5.3.2 - The anti-malware solution(s):     Performs periodic scans and active or real-t...', 'The anti-malware solution(s):
    Performs periodic scans and active or real-time scans.
OR
    Performs continuous behavioral analysis of systems or processes.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1273, '5.3.2.1', '5.3.2.1 - If periodic malware scans are performed to meet Requirement 5.3.2, the frequency...', 'If periodic malware scans are performed to meet Requirement 5.3.2, the frequency of scans is defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1274, '5.3.3', '5.3.3 - For removable electronic media, the anti- malware solution(s):     Performs au...', 'For removable electronic media, the anti- malware solution(s):
    Performs automatic scans of when the media is inserted, connected, or logically mounted,
OR
    Performs continuous behavioral analysis of systems or processes when the media is inserted, connected, or logically mounted.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1275, '5.3.4', '5.3.4 - Audit logs for the anti-malware solution(s) are enabled and retained in accordan...', 'Audit logs for the anti-malware solution(s) are enabled and retained in accordance with Requirement 10.5.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1276, '5.3.5', '5.3.5 - Anti-malware mechanisms cannot be disabled or altered by users, unless specifica...', 'Anti-malware mechanisms cannot be disabled or altered by users, unless specifically documented, and authorized by management on a case-by-case basis for a limited time period.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1277, '5.4', '5.4 - Anti-phishing mechanisms protect users against phishing attacks.', 'Anti-phishing mechanisms protect users against phishing attacks.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1278, '5.4.1', '5.4.1 - Processes and automated mechanisms are in place to detect and protect personnel ...', 'Processes and automated mechanisms are in place to detect and protect personnel against phishing attacks.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 5', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1279, '6.1', '6.1 - Processes and mechanisms for developing and maintaining secure systems and softw...', 'Processes and mechanisms for developing and maintaining secure systems and software are defined and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1280, '6.1.1', '6.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 6 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1281, '6.1.2', '6.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 6 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 6 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1282, '6.2', '6.2 - Bespoke and custom software are developed securely.', 'Bespoke and custom software are developed securely.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1283, '6.2.1', '6.2.1 - Bespoke and custom software are developed securely, as follows:     Based on i...', 'Bespoke and custom software are developed securely, as follows:
    Based on industry standards and/or best practices for secure development.
    In accordance with PCI DSS (for example, secure authentication and logging).
    Incorporating consideration of information security issues during each stage of the software development lifecycle.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1284, '6.2.2', '6.2.2 - Software development personnel working on bespoke and custom software are traine...', 'Software development personnel working on bespoke and custom software are trained at least once every 12 months as follows:
    On software security relevant to their job function and development languages.
    Including secure software design and secure coding techniques.
    Including, if security testing tools are used, how to use the tools for detecting vulnerabilities in software.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1285, '6.2.3', '6.2.3 - Bespoke and custom software is reviewed prior to being released into production ...', 'Bespoke and custom software is reviewed prior to being released into production or to customers, to identify and correct potential coding vulnerabilities, as follows:
    Code reviews ensure code is developed according to secure coding guidelines.
    Code reviews look for both existing and emerging software vulnerabilities.
    Appropriate corrections are implemented prior to release.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1286, '6.2.3.1', '6.2.3.1 - If manual code reviews are performed for bespoke and custom software prior to re...', 'If manual code reviews are performed for bespoke and custom software prior to release to production, code changes are:
    Reviewed by individuals other than the originating code author, and who are knowledgeable about code-review techniques and secure coding practices.
    Reviewed and approved by management prior to release.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1287, '6.2.4', '6.2.4 - Software engineering techniques or other methods are defined and in use by softw...', 'Software engineering techniques or other methods are defined and in use by software development personnel to prevent or mitigate common software attacks and related vulnerabilities in bespoke and custom software, including but not limited to the following:
    Injection attacks, including SQL, LDAP, XPath, or other command, parameter, object, fault, or injection-type flaws.
    Attacks on data and data structures, including attempts to manipulate buffers, pointers, input data, or shared data.
    Attacks on cryptography usage, including attempts to exploit weak, insecure, or inappropriate cryptographic implementations, algorithms, cipher suites, or modes of operation.
    Attacks on business logic, including attempts to abuse or bypass application features and functionalities through the manipulation of APIs, communication protocols and channels, client- side functionality, or other system/application functions and resources. This includes cross-site scripting (XSS) and cross-site request forgery (CSRF).
    Attacks on access control mechanisms, including attempts to bypass or abuse identification, authentication, or authorization mechanisms, or attempts to exploit weaknesses in the implementation of such mechanisms.
    Attacks via any “high-risk” vulnerabilities identified in the vulnerability identification process, as defined in Requirement 6.3.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1288, '6.3', '6.3 - Security vulnerabilities are identified and addressed.', 'Security vulnerabilities are identified and addressed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1289, '6.3.1', '6.3.1 - Security vulnerabilities are identified and managed as follows:     New securi...', 'Security vulnerabilities are identified and managed as follows:
    New security vulnerabilities are identified using industry-recognized sources for security vulnerability information, including alerts from international and national computer emergency response teams (CERTs).
    Vulnerabilities are assigned a risk ranking based on industry best practices and consideration of potential impact.
    Risk rankings identify, at a minimum, all vulnerabilities considered to be a high-risk or critical to the environment.
    Vulnerabilities for bespoke and custom, and third-party software (for example operating systems and databases) are covered.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1290, '6.3.2', '6.3.2 - An inventory of bespoke and custom software, and third-party software components...', 'An inventory of bespoke and custom software, and third-party software components incorporated into bespoke and custom software is maintained to facilitate vulnerability and patch management.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1291, '6.3.3', '6.3.3 - All system components are protected from known vulnerabilities by installing app...', 'All system components are protected from known vulnerabilities by installing applicable security patches/updates as follows:
    Critical or high-security patches/updates (identified according to the risk ranking process at Requirement 6.3.1) are installed within one month of release.
    All other applicable security patches/updates are installed within an appropriate time frame as determined by the entity (for example, within three months of release).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1292, '6.4', '6.4 - Public-facing web applications are protected against attacks.', 'Public-facing web applications are protected against attacks.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1293, '6.4.1', '6.4.1 - For public-facing web applications, new threats and vulnerabilities are addresse...', 'For public-facing web applications, new threats and vulnerabilities are addressed on an ongoing basis and these applications are protected against known attacks as follows:
    Reviewing public-facing web applications via manual or automated application vulnerability security assessment tools or methods as follows:
–    At least once every 12 months and after significant changes.
–    By an entity that specializes in application security.
–    Including, at a minimum, all common software attacks in Requirement 6.2.4.
–    All vulnerabilities are ranked in accordance with requirement 6.3.1.
–    All vulnerabilities are corrected.
–    The application is re-evaluated after the corrections
OR
    Installing an automated technical solution(s) that continually detects and prevents web-based attacks as follows:
–    Installed in front of public-facing web applications to detect and prevent web- based attacks.
–    Actively running and up to date as applicable.
–    Generating audit logs.
–    Configured to either block web-based attacks or generate an alert that is immediately investigated.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1294, '6.4.2', '6.4.2 - For public-facing web applications, an automated technical solution is deployed ...', 'For public-facing web applications, an automated technical solution is deployed that continually detects and prevents web-based attacks, with at least the following:
    Is installed in front of public-facing web applications and is configured to detect and prevent web-based attacks.
    Actively running and up to date as applicable.
    Generating audit logs.
    Configured to either block web-based attacks or generate an alert that is immediately investigated.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1295, '6.4.3', '6.4.3 - All payment page scripts that are loaded and executed in the consumer’s browser ...', 'All payment page scripts that are loaded and executed in the consumer’s browser are managed as follows:
    A method is implemented to confirm that each script is authorized.
    A method is implemented to assure the integrity of each script.
    An inventory of all scripts is maintained with written justification as to why each is necessary.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1296, '6.5', '6.5 - Changes to all system components are managed securely.', 'Changes to all system components are managed securely.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1297, '6.5.1', '6.5.1 - Changes to all system components in the production environment are made accordin...', 'Changes to all system components in the production environment are made according to established procedures that include:
    Reason for, and description of, the change.
    Documentation of security impact.
    Documented change approval by authorized parties.
    Testing to verify that the change does not adversely impact system security.
    For bespoke and custom software changes, all updates are tested for compliance with Requirement 6.2.4 before being deployed into production.
    Procedures to address failures and return to a secure state.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1356, '9.2', '9.2 - Physical access controls manage entry into facilities and systems containing car...', 'Physical access controls manage entry into facilities and systems containing cardholder data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1300, '6.5.4', '6.5.4 - Roles and functions are separated between production and pre-production environm...', 'Roles and functions are separated between production and pre-production environments to provide accountability such that only reviewed and approved changes are deployed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1301, '6.5.5', '6.5.5 - Live PANs are not used in pre-production environments, except where those enviro...', 'Live PANs are not used in pre-production environments, except where those environments are included in the CDE and protected in accordance with all applicable PCI DSS requirements.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1302, '6.5.6', '6.5.6 - Test data and test accounts are removed from system components before the system...', 'Test data and test accounts are removed from system components before the system goes into production.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 6', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1303, '7.1', '7.1 - Processes and mechanisms for restricting access to system components and cardhol...', 'Processes and mechanisms for restricting access to system components and cardholder data by business need to know are defined and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1304, '7.1.1', '7.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 7 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1305, '7.1.2', '7.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 7 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 7 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1306, '7.2', '7.2 - Access to system components and data is appropriately defined and assigned.', 'Access to system components and data is appropriately defined and assigned.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1307, '7.2.1', '7.2.1 - An access control model is defined and includes granting access as follows:   ...', 'An access control model is defined and includes granting access as follows:
    Appropriate access depending on the entity’s business and access needs.
    Access to system components and data resources that is based on users’ job classification and functions.
    The least privileges required (for example, user, administrator) to perform a job function.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1308, '7.2.2', '7.2.2 - Access is assigned to users, including privileged users, based on:     Job cla...', 'Access is assigned to users, including privileged users, based on:
    Job classification and function.
    Least privileges necessary to perform job responsibilities.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1309, '7.2.3', '7.2.3 - Required privileges are approved by authorized personnel.', 'Required privileges are approved by authorized personnel.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1310, '7.2.4', '7.2.4 - All user accounts and related access privileges, including third-party/vendor ac...', 'All user accounts and related access privileges, including third-party/vendor accounts, are reviewed as follows:
    At least once every six months.
    To ensure user accounts and access remain appropriate based on job function.
    Any inappropriate access is addressed.
    Management acknowledges that access remains appropriate.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1311, '7.2.5', '7.2.5 - All application and system accounts and related access privileges are assigned a...', 'All application and system accounts and related access privileges are assigned and managed as follows:
    Based on the least privileges necessary for the operability of the system or application.
    Access is limited to the systems, applications, or processes that specifically require their use.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1312, '7.2.5.1', '7.2.5.1 - All access by application and system accounts and related access privileges are ...', 'All access by application and system accounts and related access privileges are reviewed as follows:
    Periodically (at the frequency defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1).
    The application/system access remains appropriate for the function being performed.
    Any inappropriate access is addressed.
    Management acknowledges that access remains appropriate.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1313, '7.2.6', '7.2.6 - All user access to query repositories of stored cardholder data is restricted as...', 'All user access to query repositories of stored cardholder data is restricted as follows:
    Via applications or other programmatic methods, with access and allowed actions based on user roles and least privileges.
    Only the responsible administrator(s) can directly access or query repositories of stored CHD.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1314, '7.3', '7.3 - Access to system components and data is managed via an access control system(s).', 'Access to system components and data is managed via an access control system(s).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1315, '7.3.1', '7.3.1 - An access control system(s) is in place that restricts access based on a user’s ...', 'An access control system(s) is in place that restricts access based on a user’s need to know and covers all system components.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1316, '7.3.2', '7.3.2 - The access control system(s) is configured to enforce permissions assigned to in...', 'The access control system(s) is configured to enforce permissions assigned to individuals, applications, and systems based on job classification and function.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1317, '7.3.3', '7.3.3 - The access control system(s) is set to “deny all” by default.', 'The access control system(s) is set to “deny all” by default.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 7', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1318, '8.1', '8.1 - Processes and mechanisms for identifying users and authenticating access to syst...', 'Processes and mechanisms for identifying users and authenticating access to system components are defined and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1319, '8.1.1', '8.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 8 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1320, '8.1.2', '8.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 8 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 8 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1321, '8.2', '8.2 - User identification and related accounts for users and administrators are strict...', 'User identification and related accounts for users and administrators are strictly managed throughout an account’s lifecycle.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1322, '8.2.1', '8.2.1 - All users are assigned a unique ID before access to system components or cardhol...', 'All users are assigned a unique ID before access to system components or cardholder data is allowed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1323, '8.2.2', '8.2.2 - Group, shared, or generic accounts, or other shared authentication credentials a...', 'Group, shared, or generic accounts, or other shared authentication credentials are only used when necessary on an exception basis, and are managed as follows:
    Account use is prevented unless needed for an exceptional circumstance.
    Use is limited to the time needed for the exceptional circumstance.
    Business justification for use is documented.
    Use is explicitly approved by management.
    Individual user identity is confirmed before access to an account is granted.
    Every action taken is attributable to an individual user.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1324, '8.2.3', '8.2.3 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Service providers with remote...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Service providers with remote access to customer premises use unique authentication factors for each customer premises.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1325, '8.2.4', '8.2.4 - Addition, deletion, and modification of user IDs, authentication factors, and ot...', 'Addition, deletion, and modification of user IDs, authentication factors, and other identifier objects are managed as follows:
    Authorized with the appropriate approval.
    Implemented with only the privileges specified on the documented approval.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1326, '8.2.5', '8.2.5 - Access for terminated users is immediately revoked.', 'Access for terminated users is immediately revoked.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1327, '8.2.6', '8.2.6 - Inactive user accounts are removed or disabled within 90 days of inactivity.', 'Inactive user accounts are removed or disabled within 90 days of inactivity.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1328, '8.2.7', '8.2.7 - Accounts used by third parties to access, support, or maintain system components...', 'Accounts used by third parties to access, support, or maintain system components via remote access are managed as follows:
    Enabled only during the time period needed and disabled when not in use.
    Use is monitored for unexpected activity.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
    Something you know, such as a password or passphrase.
    Something you have, such as a token device or smart card.
    Something you are, such as a biometric element.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1332, '8.3.2', '8.3.2 - Strong cryptography is used to render all authentication factors unreadable duri...', 'Strong cryptography is used to render all authentication factors unreadable during transmission and storage on all system components.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1333, '8.3.3', '8.3.3 - User identity is verified before modifying any authentication factor.', 'User identity is verified before modifying any authentication factor.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1334, '8.3.4', '8.3.4 - Invalid authentication attempts are limited by:     Locking out the user ID af...', 'Invalid authentication attempts are limited by:
    Locking out the user ID after not more than 10 attempts.
    Setting the lockout duration to a minimum of 30 minutes or until the user’s identity is confirmed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1335, '8.3.5', '8.3.5 - If passwords/passphrases are used as authentication factors to meet Requirement ...', 'If passwords/passphrases are used as authentication factors to meet Requirement 8.3.1, they are set and reset for each user as follows:
    Set to a unique value for first-time use and upon reset.
    Forced to be changed immediately after the first use.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1336, '8.3.6', '8.3.6 - If passwords/passphrases are used as authentication factors to meet Requirement ...', 'If passwords/passphrases are used as authentication factors to meet Requirement 8.3.1, they meet the following minimum level of complexity:
    A minimum length of 12 characters (or IF the system does not support 12 characters, a minimum length of eight characters).
    Contain both numeric and alphabetic characters.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1337, '8.3.7', '8.3.7 - Individuals are not allowed to submit a new password/passphrase that is the same...', 'Individuals are not allowed to submit a new password/passphrase that is the same as any of the last four passwords/passphrases used.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1338, '8.3.8', '8.3.8 - Authentication policies and procedures are documented and communicated to all us...', 'Authentication policies and procedures are documented and communicated to all users including:
    Guidance on selecting strong authentication factors.
    Guidance for how users should protect their authentication factors.
    Instructions not to reuse previously used passwords/passphrases.
    Instructions to change passwords/passphrases if there is any suspicion or knowledge that the password/passphrases have been compromised and how to report the incident.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1339, '8.3.9', '8.3.9 - If passwords/passphrases are used as the only authentication factor for user acc...', 'If passwords/passphrases are used as the only authentication factor for user access (i.e., in any single-factor authentication implementation) then either:
    Passwords/passphrases are changed at least once every 90 days,
OR
    The security posture of accounts is dynamically analyzed, and real-time access to resources is automatically determined accordingly.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1340, '8.3.10', '8.3.10 - Additional requirement for service providers only: If passwords/passphrases are ...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: If passwords/passphrases are used as the only authentication factor for customer user access to cardholder data (i.e., in any single- factor authentication implementation), then guidance is provided to customer users including:
    Guidance for customers to change their user passwords/passphrases periodically.
    Guidance as to when, and under what circumstances, passwords/passphrases are to be changed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1341, '8.3.10.1', '8.3.10.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: If passwords/passphrases are ...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: If passwords/passphrases are used as the only authentication factor for customer user access (i.e., in any single-factor authentication implementation) then either:
    Passwords/passphrases are changed at least once every 90 days,
OR
    The security posture of accounts is dynamically analyzed, and real-time access to resources is automatically determined accordingly.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1342, '8.3.11', '8.3.11 - Where authentication factors such as physical or logical security tokens, smart ...', 'Where authentication factors such as physical or logical security tokens, smart cards, or certificates are used:
    Factors are assigned to an individual user and not shared among multiple users.
    Physical and/or logical controls ensure only the intended user can use that factor to gain access.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1343, '8.4', '8.4 - Multi-factor authentication (MFA) is implemented to secure access into the CDE.', 'Multi-factor authentication (MFA) is implemented to secure access into the CDE.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1344, '8.4.1', '8.4.1 - MFA is implemented for all non-console access into the CDE for personnel with ad...', 'MFA is implemented for all non-console access into the CDE for personnel with administrative access.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1345, '8.4.2', '8.4.2 - MFA is implemented for all access into the CDE.', 'MFA is implemented for all access into the CDE.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1346, '8.4.3', '8.4.3 - MFA is implemented for all remote network access originating from outside the en...', 'MFA is implemented for all remote network access originating from outside the entity’s network that could access or impact the CDE as follows:
    All remote access by all personnel, both users and administrators, originating from outside the entity’s network.
    All remote access by third parties and vendors.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1347, '8.5', '8.5 - Multi-factor authentication (MFA) systems are configured to prevent misuse.', 'Multi-factor authentication (MFA) systems are configured to prevent misuse.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1348, '8.5.1', '8.5.1 - MFA systems are implemented as follows:     The MFA system is not susceptible ...', 'MFA systems are implemented as follows:
    The MFA system is not susceptible to replay attacks.
    MFA systems cannot be bypassed by any users, including administrative users unless specifically documented, and authorized by management on an exception basis, for a limited time period.
    At least two different types of authentication factors are used.
    Success of all authentication factors is required before access is granted.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1349, '8.6', '8.6 - Use of application and system accounts and associated authentication factors is ...', 'Use of application and system accounts and associated authentication factors is strictly managed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1350, '8.6.1', '8.6.1 - If accounts used by systems or applications can be used for interactive login, t...', 'If accounts used by systems or applications can be used for interactive login, they are managed as follows:
    Interactive use is prevented unless needed for an exceptional circumstance.
    Interactive use is limited to the time needed for the exceptional circumstance.
    Business justification for interactive use is documented.
    Interactive use is explicitly approved by management.
    Individual user identity is confirmed before access to account is granted.
    Every action taken is attributable to an individual user.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1351, '8.6.2', '8.6.2 - Passwords/passphrases for any application and system accounts that can be used f...', 'Passwords/passphrases for any application and system accounts that can be used for interactive login are not hard coded in scripts, configuration/property files, or bespoke and custom source code.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1352, '8.6.3', '8.6.3 - Passwords/passphrases for any application and system accounts are protected agai...', 'Passwords/passphrases for any application and system accounts are protected against misuse as follows:
    Passwords/passphrases are changed periodically (at the frequency defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1) and upon suspicion or confirmation of compromise.
    Passwords/passphrases are constructed with sufficient complexity appropriate for how frequently the entity changes the passwords/passphrases.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 8', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1353, '9.1', '9.1 - Processes and mechanisms for restricting physical access to cardholder data are ...', 'Processes and mechanisms for restricting physical access to cardholder data are defined and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1354, '9.1.1', '9.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 9 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1355, '9.1.2', '9.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 9 are docume...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 9 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1358, '9.2.1.1', '9.2.1.1 - Individual physical access to sensitive areas within the CDE is monitored with e...', 'Individual physical access to sensitive areas within the CDE is monitored with either video cameras or physical access control mechanisms (or both) as follows:
    Entry and exit points to/from sensitive areas within the CDE are monitored.
    Monitoring devices or mechanisms are protected from tampering or disabling.
    Collected data is reviewed and correlated with other entries.
    Collected data is stored for at least three months, unless otherwise restricted by law.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1359, '9.2.2', '9.2.2 - Physical and/or logical controls are implemented to restrict use of publicly acc...', 'Physical and/or logical controls are implemented to restrict use of publicly accessible network jacks within the facility.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1360, '9.2.3', '9.2.3 - Physical access to wireless access points, gateways, networking/communications h...', 'Physical access to wireless access points, gateways, networking/communications hardware, and telecommunication lines within the facility is restricted.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1361, '9.2.4', '9.2.4 - Access to consoles in sensitive areas is restricted via locking when not in use.', 'Access to consoles in sensitive areas is restricted via locking when not in use.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1362, '9.3', '9.3 - Physical access for personnel and visitors is authorized and managed.', 'Physical access for personnel and visitors is authorized and managed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1363, '9.3.1', '9.3.1 - Procedures are implemented for authorizing and managing physical access of perso...', 'Procedures are implemented for authorizing and managing physical access of personnel to the CDE, including:
    Identifying personnel.
    Managing changes to an individual’s physical access requirements.
    Revoking or terminating personnel identification.
    Limiting access to the identification process or system to authorized personnel.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1364, '9.3.1.1', '9.3.1.1 - Physical access to sensitive areas within the CDE for personnel is controlled as...', 'Physical access to sensitive areas within the CDE for personnel is controlled as follows:
    Access is authorized and based on individual job function.
    Access is revoked immediately upon termination.
    All physical access mechanisms, such as keys, access cards, etc., are returned or disabled upon termination.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1365, '9.3.2', '9.3.2 - Procedures are implemented for authorizing and managing visitor access to the CD...', 'Procedures are implemented for authorizing and managing visitor access to the CDE, including:
    Visitors are authorized before entering.
    Visitors are escorted at all times.
    Visitors are clearly identified and given a badge or other identification that expires.
    Visitor badges or other identification visibly distinguishes visitors from personnel.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1366, '9.3.3', '9.3.3 - Visitor badges or identification are surrendered or deactivated before visitors ...', 'Visitor badges or identification are surrendered or deactivated before visitors leave the facility or at the date of expiration.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1367, '9.3.4', '9.3.4 - A visitor log is used to maintain a physical record of visitor activity within t...', 'A visitor log is used to maintain a physical record of visitor activity within the facility and within sensitive areas, including:
    The visitor’s name and the organization represented.
    The date and time of the visit.
    The name of the personnel authorizing physical access.
    Retaining the log for at least three months, unless otherwise restricted by law.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1368, '9.4', '9.4 - Media with cardholder data is securely stored, accessed, distributed, and destro...', 'Media with cardholder data is securely stored, accessed, distributed, and destroyed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1369, '9.4.1', '9.4.1 - All media with cardholder data is physically secured.', 'All media with cardholder data is physically secured.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1370, '9.4.1.1', '9.4.1.1 - Offline media backups with cardholder data are stored in a secure location.', 'Offline media backups with cardholder data are stored in a secure location.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', 'If stored in a non-secured facility, backups containing cardholder data may easily be lost, stolen, or copied for malicious intent.
Good Practice
For secure storage of backup media, a good practice is to store media in an off-site facility, such as an alternate or backup site or commercial storage facility.', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1371, '9.4.1.2', '9.4.1.2 - The security of the offline media backup location(s) with cardholder data is rev...', 'The security of the offline media backup location(s) with cardholder data is reviewed at least once every 12 months.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1372, '9.4.2', '9.4.2 - All media with cardholder data is classified in accordance with the sensitivity ...', 'All media with cardholder data is classified in accordance with the sensitivity of the data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1373, '9.4.3', '9.4.3 - Media with cardholder data sent outside the facility is secured as follows:   ...', 'Media with cardholder data sent outside the facility is secured as follows:
    Media sent outside the facility is logged.
    Media is sent by secured courier or other delivery method that can be accurately tracked.
    Offsite tracking logs include details about media location.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1374, '9.4.4', '9.4.4 - Management approves all media with cardholder data that is moved outside the fac...', 'Management approves all media with cardholder data that is moved outside the facility (including when media is distributed to individuals).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1375, '9.4.5', '9.4.5 - Inventory logs of all electronic media with cardholder data are maintained.', 'Inventory logs of all electronic media with cardholder data are maintained.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1376, '9.4.5.1', '9.4.5.1 - Inventories of electronic media with cardholder data are conducted at least once...', 'Inventories of electronic media with cardholder data are conducted at least once every 12 months.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1377, '9.4.6', '9.4.6 - Hard-copy materials with cardholder data are destroyed when no longer needed for...', 'Hard-copy materials with cardholder data are destroyed when no longer needed for business or legal reasons, as follows:
    Materials are cross-cut shredded, incinerated, or pulped so that cardholder data cannot be reconstructed.
    Materials are stored in secure storage containers prior to destruction.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1378, '9.4.7', '9.4.7 - Electronic media with cardholder data is destroyed when no longer needed for bus...', 'Electronic media with cardholder data is destroyed when no longer needed for business or legal reasons via one of the following:
    The electronic media is destroyed.
    The cardholder data is rendered unrecoverable so that it cannot be reconstructed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1379, '9.5', '9.5 - Point-of-interaction (POI) devices are protected from tampering and unauthorized...', 'Point-of-interaction (POI) devices are protected from tampering and unauthorized substitution.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1380, '9.5.1', '9.5.1 - POI devices that capture payment card data via direct physical interaction with ...', 'POI devices that capture payment card data via direct physical interaction with the payment card form factor are protected from tampering and unauthorized substitution, including the following:
      Maintaining a list of POI devices.
      Periodically inspecting POI devices to look for tampering or unauthorized substitution.
      Training personnel to be aware of suspicious behavior and to report tampering or unauthorized substitution of devices.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1381, '9.5.1.1', '9.5.1.1 - An up-to-date list of POI devices is maintained, including:     Make and model...', 'An up-to-date list of POI devices is maintained, including:
    Make and model of the device.
    Location of device.
    Device serial number or other methods of unique identification.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1382, '9.5.1.2', '9.5.1.2 - POI device surfaces are periodically inspected to detect tampering and unauthori...', 'POI device surfaces are periodically inspected to detect tampering and unauthorized substitution.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1383, '9.5.1.2.1', '9.5.1.2.1 - The frequency of periodic POI device inspections and the type of inspections per...', 'The frequency of periodic POI device inspections and the type of inspections performed is defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1384, '9.5.1.3', '9.5.1.3 - Training is provided for personnel in POI environments to be aware of attempted ...', 'Training is provided for personnel in POI environments to be aware of attempted tampering or replacement of POI devices, and includes:
    Verifying the identity of any third-party persons claiming to be repair or maintenance personnel, before granting them access to modify or troubleshoot devices.
    Procedures to ensure devices are not installed, replaced, or returned without verification.
    Being aware of suspicious behavior around devices.
    Reporting suspicious behavior and indications of device tampering or substitution to appropriate personnel.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 9', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1385, '10.1', '10.1 - Processes and mechanisms for logging and monitoring all access to system compone...', 'Processes and mechanisms for logging and monitoring all access to system components and cardholder data are defined and documented.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1386, '10.1.1', '10.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 10 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1387, '10.1.2', '10.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 10 are docum...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 10 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1388, '10.2', '10.2 - Audit logs are implemented to support the detection of anomalies and suspicious ...', 'Audit logs are implemented to support the detection of anomalies and suspicious activity, and the forensic analysis of events.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1389, '10.2.1', '10.2.1 - Audit logs are enabled and active for all system components and cardholder data.', 'Audit logs are enabled and active for all system components and cardholder data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1390, '10.2.1.1', '10.2.1.1 - Audit logs capture all individual user access to cardholder data.', 'Audit logs capture all individual user access to cardholder data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1391, '10.2.1.2', '10.2.1.2 - Audit logs capture all actions taken by any individual with administrative acces...', 'Audit logs capture all actions taken by any individual with administrative access, including any interactive use of application or system accounts.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1392, '10.2.1.3', '10.2.1.3 - Audit logs capture all access to audit logs.', 'Audit logs capture all access to audit logs.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1393, '10.2.1.4', '10.2.1.4 - Audit logs capture all invalid logical access attempts.', 'Audit logs capture all invalid logical access attempts.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1394, '10.2.1.5', '10.2.1.5 - Audit logs capture all changes to identification and authentication credentials ...', 'Audit logs capture all changes to identification and authentication credentials including, but not limited to:
    Creation of new accounts.
    Elevation of privileges.
    All changes, additions, or deletions to accounts with administrative access.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1395, '10.2.1.6', '10.2.1.6 - Audit logs capture the following:     All initialization of new audit logs, an...', 'Audit logs capture the following:
    All initialization of new audit logs, and
    All starting, stopping, or pausing of the existing audit logs.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1396, '10.2.1.7', '10.2.1.7 - Audit logs capture all creation and deletion of system-level objects.', 'Audit logs capture all creation and deletion of system-level objects.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1397, '10.2.2', '10.2.2 - Audit logs record the following details for each auditable event:     User ide...', 'Audit logs record the following details for each auditable event:
    User identification.
    Type of event.
    Date and time.
    Success and failure indication.
    Origination of event.
    Identity or name of affected data, system component, resource, or service (for example, name and protocol).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1398, '10.3', '10.3 - Audit logs are protected from destruction and unauthorized modifications.', 'Audit logs are protected from destruction and unauthorized modifications.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1399, '10.3.1', '10.3.1 - Read access to audit logs files is limited to those with a job-related need.', 'Read access to audit logs files is limited to those with a job-related need.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1400, '10.3.2', '10.3.2 - Audit log files are protected to prevent modifications by individuals.', 'Audit log files are protected to prevent modifications by individuals.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1401, '10.3.3', '10.3.3 - Audit log files, including those for external- facing technologies, are promptly...', 'Audit log files, including those for external- facing technologies, are promptly backed up to a secure, central, internal log server(s) or other media that is difficult to modify.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1402, '10.3.4', '10.3.4 - File integrity monitoring or change-detection mechanisms is used on audit logs t...', 'File integrity monitoring or change-detection mechanisms is used on audit logs to ensure that existing log data cannot be changed without generating alerts.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1403, '10.4', '10.4 - Audit logs are reviewed to identify anomalies or suspicious activity.', 'Audit logs are reviewed to identify anomalies or suspicious activity.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1404, '10.4.1', '10.4.1 - The following audit logs are reviewed at least once daily:     All security ev...', 'The following audit logs are reviewed at least once daily:
    All security events.
    Logs of all system components that store, process, or transmit CHD and/or SAD.
    Logs of all critical system components.
    Logs of all servers and system components that perform security functions (for example, network security controls, intrusion-detection systems/intrusion-prevention systems (IDS/IPS), authentication servers).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1405, '10.4.1.1', '10.4.1.1 - Automated mechanisms are used to perform audit log reviews.', 'Automated mechanisms are used to perform audit log reviews.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1406, '10.4.2', '10.4.2 - Logs of all other system components (those not specified in Requirement 10.4.1) ...', 'Logs of all other system components (those not specified in Requirement 10.4.1) are reviewed periodically.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1407, '10.4.2.1', '10.4.2.1 - The frequency of periodic log reviews for all other system components (not defin...', 'The frequency of periodic log reviews for all other system components (not defined in Requirement 10.4.1) is defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1408, '10.4.3', '10.4.3 - Exceptions and anomalies identified during the review process are addressed.', 'Exceptions and anomalies identified during the review process are addressed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1409, '10.5', '10.5 - Audit log history is retained and available for analysis.', 'Audit log history is retained and available for analysis.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1410, '10.5.1', '10.5.1 - Retain audit log history for at least 12 months, with at least the most recent t...', 'Retain audit log history for at least 12 months, with at least the most recent three months immediately available for analysis.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1411, '10.6', '10.6 - Time-synchronization mechanisms support consistent time settings across all syst...', 'Time-synchronization mechanisms support consistent time settings across all systems.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1412, '10.6.1', '10.6.1 - System clocks and time are synchronized using time-synchronization technology.', 'System clocks and time are synchronized using time-synchronization technology.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1413, '10.6.2', '10.6.2 - Systems are configured to the correct and consistent time as follows:     One ...', 'Systems are configured to the correct and consistent time as follows:
    One or more designated time servers are in use.
    Only the designated central time server(s) receives time from external sources.
    Time received from external sources is based on International Atomic Time or Coordinated Universal Time (UTC).
    The designated time server(s) accept time updates only from specific industry-accepted external sources.
    Where there is more than one designated time server, the time servers peer with one another to keep accurate time.
    Internal systems receive time information only from designated central time server(s).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1414, '10.6.3', '10.6.3 - Time synchronization settings and data are protected as follows:     Access to...', 'Time synchronization settings and data are protected as follows:
    Access to time data is restricted to only personnel with a business need.
    Any changes to time settings on critical systems are logged, monitored, and reviewed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1415, '10.7', '10.7 - Failures of critical security control systems are detected, reported, and respon...', 'Failures of critical security control systems are detected, reported, and responded to promptly.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1416, '10.7.1', '10.7.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Failures of critical security...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Failures of critical security control systems are detected, alerted, and addressed promptly, including but not limited to failure of the following critical security control systems:
    Network security controls.
    IDS/IPS.
    FIM.
    Anti-malware solutions.
    Physical access controls.
    Logical access controls.
    Audit logging mechanisms.
    Segmentation controls (if used).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1417, '10.7.2', '10.7.2 - Failures of critical security control systems are detected, alerted, and address...', 'Failures of critical security control systems are detected, alerted, and addressed promptly, including but not limited to failure of the following critical security control systems:
    Network security controls.
    IDS/IPS.
    Change-detection mechanisms.
    Anti-malware solutions.
    Physical access controls.
    Logical access controls.
    Audit logging mechanisms.
    Segmentation controls (if used).
    Audit log review mechanisms.
    Automated security testing tools (if used).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1418, '10.7.3', '10.7.3 - Failures of any critical security controls systems are responded to promptly, in...', 'Failures of any critical security controls systems are responded to promptly, including but not limited to:
    Restoring security functions.
    Identifying and documenting the duration (date and time from start to end) of the security failure.
    Identifying and documenting the cause(s) of failure and documenting required remediation.
    Identifying and addressing any security issues that arose during the failure.
    Determining whether further actions are required as a result of the security failure.
    Implementing controls to prevent the cause of failure from reoccurring.
    Resuming monitoring of security controls.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 10', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1419, '11.1', '11.1 - Processes and mechanisms for regularly testing security of systems and networks ...', 'Processes and mechanisms for regularly testing security of systems and networks are defined and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1420, '11.1.1', '11.1.1 - All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirem...', 'All security policies and operational procedures that are identified in Requirement 11 are:
    Documented.
    Kept up to date.
    In use.
    Known to all affected parties.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1421, '11.1.2', '11.1.2 - Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 11 are docum...', 'Roles and responsibilities for performing activities in Requirement 11 are documented, assigned, and understood.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1422, '11.2', '11.2 - Wireless access points are identified and monitored, and unauthorized wireless a...', 'Wireless access points are identified and monitored, and unauthorized wireless access points are addressed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1423, '11.2.1', '11.2.1 - Authorized and unauthorized wireless access points are managed as follows:    ...', 'Authorized and unauthorized wireless access points are managed as follows:
    The presence of wireless (Wi-Fi) access points is tested for,
    All authorized and unauthorized wireless access points are detected and identified,
    Testing, detection, and identification occurs at least once every three months.
    If automated monitoring is used, personnel are notified via generated alerts.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1424, '11.2.2', '11.2.2 - An inventory of authorized wireless access points is maintained, including a doc...', 'An inventory of authorized wireless access points is maintained, including a documented business justification.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1425, '11.3', '11.3 - External and internal vulnerabilities are regularly identified, prioritized, and...', 'External and internal vulnerabilities are regularly identified, prioritized, and addressed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1426, '11.3.1', '11.3.1 - Internal vulnerability scans are performed as follows:     At least once every...', 'Internal vulnerability scans are performed as follows:
    At least once every three months.
    High-risk and critical vulnerabilities (per the entity’s vulnerability risk rankings defined at Requirement 6.3.1) are resolved.
      Rescans are performed that confirm all high- risk and critical vulnerabilities (as noted above) have been resolved.
    Scan tool is kept up to date with latest vulnerability information.
    Scans are performed by qualified personnel and organizational independence of the tester exists.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1427, '11.3.1.1', '11.3.1.1 - All other applicable vulnerabilities (those not ranked as high-risk or critical ...', 'All other applicable vulnerabilities (those not ranked as high-risk or critical per the entity’s vulnerability risk rankings defined at Requirement
6.3.1) are managed as follows:
      Addressed based on the risk defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1.
      Rescans are conducted as needed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1428, '11.3.1.2', '11.3.1.2 - Internal vulnerability scans are performed via authenticated scanning as follows...', 'Internal vulnerability scans are performed via authenticated scanning as follows:
    Systems that are unable to accept credentials for authenticated scanning are documented.
    Sufficient privileges are used for those systems that accept credentials for scanning.
    If accounts used for authenticated scanning can be used for interactive login, they are managed in accordance with Requirement 8.2.2.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1429, '11.3.1.3', '11.3.1.3 - Internal vulnerability scans are performed after any significant change as follo...', 'Internal vulnerability scans are performed after any significant change as follows:
    High-risk and critical vulnerabilities (per the entity’s vulnerability risk rankings defined at Requirement 6.3.1) are resolved.
    Rescans are conducted as needed.
    Scans are performed by qualified personnel and organizational independence of the tester exists (not required to be a QSA or ASV).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1430, '11.3.2', '11.3.2 - External vulnerability scans are performed as follows:       At least once eve...', 'External vulnerability scans are performed as follows:
      At least once every three months.
      By a PCI SSC Approved Scanning Vendor (ASV).
      Vulnerabilities are resolved and ASV Program Guide requirements for a passing scan are met.
      Rescans are performed as needed to confirm that vulnerabilities are resolved per the ASV Program Guide requirements for a passing scan.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
      To alert personnel to unauthorized modification (including changes, additions, and deletions) of critical files.
      To perform critical file comparisons at least once weekly.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1431, '11.3.2.1', '11.3.2.1 - External vulnerability scans are performed after any significant change as follo...', 'External vulnerability scans are performed after any significant change as follows:
    Vulnerabilities that are scored 4.0 or higher by the CVSS are resolved.
    Rescans are conducted as needed.
    Scans are performed by qualified personnel and organizational independence of the tester exists (not required to be a QSA or ASV).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1432, '11.4', '11.4 - External and internal penetration testing is regularly performed, and exploitabl...', 'External and internal penetration testing is regularly performed, and exploitable vulnerabilities and security weaknesses are corrected.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1433, '11.4.1', '11.4.1 - A penetration testing methodology is defined, documented, and implemented by the...', 'A penetration testing methodology is defined, documented, and implemented by the entity, and includes:
    Industry-accepted penetration testing approaches.
    Coverage for the entire CDE perimeter and critical systems.
    Testing from both inside and outside the network.
    Testing to validate any segmentation and scope- reduction controls.
    Application-layer penetration testing to identify, at a minimum, the vulnerabilities listed in Requirement 6.2.4.
    Network-layer penetration tests that encompass all components that support network functions as well as operating systems.
    Review and consideration of threats and vulnerabilities experienced in the last 12 months.
    Documented approach to assessing and addressing the risk posed by exploitable vulnerabilities and security weaknesses found during penetration testing.
    Retention of penetration testing results and remediation activities results for at least 12 months.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1434, '11.4.2', '11.4.2 - Internal penetration testing is performed:     Per the entity’s defined method...', 'Internal penetration testing is performed:
    Per the entity’s defined methodology,
    At least once every 12 months
    After any significant infrastructure or application upgrade or change
    By a qualified internal resource or qualified external third-party
    Organizational independence of the tester exists (not required to be a QSA or ASV).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1435, '11.4.3', '11.4.3 - External penetration testing is performed:     Per the entity’s defined method...', 'External penetration testing is performed:
    Per the entity’s defined methodology
    At least once every 12 months
    After any significant infrastructure or application upgrade or change
    By a qualified internal resource or qualified external third party
    Organizational independence of the tester exists (not required to be a QSA or ASV).
(continued on next page)', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1436, '11.4.4', '11.4.4 - Exploitable vulnerabilities and security weaknesses found during penetration tes...', 'Exploitable vulnerabilities and security weaknesses found during penetration testing are corrected as follows:
    In accordance with the entity’s assessment of the risk posed by the security issue as defined in Requirement 6.3.1.
    Penetration testing is repeated to verify the corrections.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1437, '11.4.5', '11.4.5 - If segmentation is used to isolate the CDE from other networks, penetration test...', 'If segmentation is used to isolate the CDE from other networks, penetration tests are performed on segmentation controls as follows:
    At least once every 12 months and after any changes to segmentation controls/methods
    Covering all segmentation controls/methods in use.
    According to the entity’s defined penetration testing methodology.
    Confirming that the segmentation controls/methods are operational and effective, and isolate the CDE from all out-of-scope systems.
    Confirming effectiveness of any use of isolation to separate systems with differing security levels (see Requirement 2.2.3).
    Performed by a qualified internal resource or qualified external third party.
    Organizational independence of the tester exists (not required to be a QSA or ASV).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1438, '11.4.6', '11.4.6 - Additional requirement for service providers only: If segmentation is used to is...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: If segmentation is used to isolate the CDE from other networks, penetration tests are performed on segmentation controls as follows:
    At least once every six months and after any changes to segmentation controls/methods.
    Covering all segmentation controls/methods in use.
    According to the entity’s defined penetration testing methodology.
    Confirming that the segmentation controls/methods are operational and effective, and isolate the CDE from all out-of-scope systems.
    Confirming effectiveness of any use of isolation to separate systems with differing security levels (see Requirement 2.2.3).
    Performed by a qualified internal resource or qualified external third party.
    Organizational independence of the tester exists (not required to be a QSA or ASV).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1439, '11.4.7', '11.4.7 - Additional requirement for multi-tenant service providers only: Multi-tenant ser...', 'Additional requirement for multi-tenant service providers only: Multi-tenant service providers support their customers for external penetration testing per Requirement 11.4.3 and 11.4.4.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1440, '11.5', '11.5 - Network intrusions and unexpected file changes are detected and responded to.', 'Network intrusions and unexpected file changes are detected and responded to.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1441, '11.5.1', '11.5.1 - Intrusion-detection and/or intrusion- prevention techniques are used to detect a...', 'Intrusion-detection and/or intrusion- prevention techniques are used to detect and/or prevent intrusions into the network as follows:
    All traffic is monitored at the perimeter of the CDE.
    All traffic is monitored at critical points in the CDE.
    Personnel are alerted to suspected compromises.
    All intrusion-detection and prevention engines, baselines, and signatures are kept up to date.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1442, '11.5.1.1', '11.5.1.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Intrusion-detection and/or in...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Intrusion-detection and/or intrusion-prevention techniques detect, alert on/prevent, and address covert malware communication channels.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1444, '11.6', '11.6 - Unauthorized changes on payment pages are detected and responded to.', 'Unauthorized changes on payment pages are detected and responded to.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1445, '11.6.1', '11.6.1 - A change- and tamper-detection mechanism is deployed as follows:     To alert ...', 'A change- and tamper-detection mechanism is deployed as follows:
    To alert personnel to unauthorized modification (including indicators of compromise, changes, additions, and deletions) to the HTTP headers and the contents of payment pages as received by the consumer browser.
    The mechanism is configured to evaluate the received HTTP header and payment page.
    The mechanism functions are performed as follows:
–    At least once every seven days
OR
–    Periodically (at the frequency defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 11', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1446, '12.1', '12.1 - A comprehensive information security policy that governs and provides direction ...', 'A comprehensive information security policy that governs and provides direction for protection of the entity’s information assets is known and current.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1447, '12.1.1', '12.1.1 - An overall information security policy is:     Established.     Published. ...', 'An overall information security policy is:
    Established.
    Published.
    Maintained.
    Disseminated to all relevant personnel, as well as to relevant vendors and business partners.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1448, '12.1.2', '12.1.2 - The information security policy is:     Reviewed at least once every 12 months...', 'The information security policy is:
    Reviewed at least once every 12 months.
    Updated as needed to reflect changes to business objectives or risks to the environment.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1449, '12.1.3', '12.1.3 - The security policy clearly defines information security roles and responsibilit...', 'The security policy clearly defines information security roles and responsibilities for all personnel, and all personnel are aware of and acknowledge their information security responsibilities.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1450, '12.1.4', '12.1.4 - Responsibility for information security is formally assigned to a Chief Informat...', 'Responsibility for information security is formally assigned to a Chief Information Security Officer or other information security knowledgeable member of executive management.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1451, '12.2', '12.2 - Acceptable use policies for end-user technologies are defined and implemented.', 'Acceptable use policies for end-user technologies are defined and implemented.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1452, '12.2.1', '12.2.1 - Acceptable use policies for end-user technologies are documented and implemented...', 'Acceptable use policies for end-user technologies are documented and implemented, including:
    Explicit approval by authorized parties.
    Acceptable uses of the technology.
    List of products approved by the company for employee use, including hardware and software.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1453, '12.3', '12.3 - Risks to the cardholder data environment are formally identified, evaluated, and...', 'Risks to the cardholder data environment are formally identified, evaluated, and managed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1454, '12.3.1', '12.3.1 - Each PCI DSS requirement that provides flexibility for how frequently it is perf...', 'Each PCI DSS requirement that provides flexibility for how frequently it is performed (for example, requirements to be performed periodically) is supported by a targeted risk analysis that is documented and includes:
    Identification of the assets being protected.
    Identification of the threat(s) that the requirement is protecting against.
    Identification of factors that contribute to the likelihood and/or impact of a threat being realized.
    Resulting analysis that determines, and includes justification for, how frequently the requirement must be performed to minimize the likelihood of the threat being realized.
    Review of each targeted risk analysis at least once every 12 months to determine whether the results are still valid or if an updated risk analysis is needed.
    Performance of updated risk analyses when needed, as determined by the annual review.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1455, '12.3.2', '12.3.2 - A targeted risk analysis is performed for each PCI DSS requirement that the enti...', 'A targeted risk analysis is performed for each PCI DSS requirement that the entity meets with the customized approach, to include:
    Documented evidence detailing each element specified in Appendix D: Customized Approach (including, at a minimum, a controls matrix and risk analysis).
    Approval of documented evidence by senior management.
    Performance of the targeted analysis of risk at least once every 12 months.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1456, '12.3.3', '12.3.3 - Cryptographic cipher suites and protocols in use are documented and reviewed at ...', 'Cryptographic cipher suites and protocols in use are documented and reviewed at least once every 12 months, including at least the following:
    An up-to-date inventory of all cryptographic cipher suites and protocols in use, including purpose and where used.
    Active monitoring of industry trends regarding continued viability of all cryptographic cipher suites and protocols in use.
    A documented strategy to respond to anticipated changes in cryptographic vulnerabilities.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1457, '12.3.4', '12.3.4 - Hardware and software technologies in use are reviewed at least once every 12 mo...', 'Hardware and software technologies in use are reviewed at least once every 12 months, including at least the following:
    Analysis that the technologies continue to receive security fixes from vendors promptly.
    Analysis that the technologies continue to support (and do not preclude) the entity’s PCI DSS compliance.
    Documentation of any industry announcements or trends related to a technology, such as when a vendor has announced “end of life” plans for a technology.
    Documentation of a plan, approved by senior management, to remediate outdated technologies, including those for which vendors have announced “end of life” plans.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1458, '12.4', '12.4 - PCI DSS compliance is managed.', 'PCI DSS compliance is managed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1474, '12.7.1', '12.7.1 - Potential personnel who will have access to the CDE are screened, within the con...', 'Potential personnel who will have access to the CDE are screened, within the constraints of local laws, prior to hire to minimize the risk of attacks from internal sources.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1459, '12.4.1', '12.4.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Responsibility is established...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Responsibility is established by executive management for the protection of cardholder data and a PCI DSS compliance program to include:
    Overall accountability for maintaining PCI DSS compliance.
    Defining a charter for a PCI DSS compliance program and communication to executive management.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1460, '12.4.2', '12.4.2 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Reviews are performed at leas...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Reviews are performed at least once every three months to confirm that personnel are performing their tasks in accordance with all security policies and operational procedures. Reviews are performed by personnel other than those responsible for performing the given task and include, but are not limited to, the following tasks:
    Daily log reviews.
    Configuration reviews for network security controls.
    Applying configuration standards to new systems.
    Responding to security alerts.
    Change-management processes.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1461, '12.4.2.1', '12.4.2.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Reviews conducted in accordan...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Reviews conducted in accordance with Requirement 12.4.2 are documented to include:
    Results of the reviews.
    Documented remediation actions taken for any tasks that were found to not be performed at Requirement 12.4.2.
    Review and sign-off of results by personnel assigned responsibility for the PCI DSS compliance program.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1462, '12.5', '12.5 - PCI DSS scope is documented and validated.', 'PCI DSS scope is documented and validated.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1463, '12.5.1', '12.5.1 - An inventory of system components that are in scope for PCI DSS, including a des...', 'An inventory of system components that are in scope for PCI DSS, including a description of function/use, is maintained and kept current.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1464, '12.5.2', '12.5.2 - PCI DSS scope is documented and confirmed by the entity at least once every 12 m...', 'PCI DSS scope is documented and confirmed by the entity at least once every 12 months and upon significant change to the in-scope environment. At a minimum, the scoping validation includes:
    Identifying all data flows for the various payment stages (for example, authorization, capture settlement, chargebacks, and refunds) and acceptance channels (for example, card-present, card-not-present, and e-commerce).
    Updating all data-flow diagrams per Requirement 1.2.4.
    Identifying all locations where account data is stored, processed, and transmitted, including but not limited to: 1) any locations outside of the currently defined CDE, 2) applications that process CHD, 3) transmissions between systems and networks, and 4) file backups.
    Identifying all system components in the CDE, connected to the CDE, or that could impact security of the CDE.
    Identifying all segmentation controls in use and the environment(s) from which the CDE is segmented, including justification for environments being out of scope.
    Identifying all connections from third-party entities with access to the CDE.
    Confirming that all identified data flows, account data, system components, segmentation controls, and connections from third parties with access to the CDE are included in scope.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1465, '12.5.2.1', '12.5.2.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: PCI DSS scope is documented a...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: PCI DSS scope is documented and confirmed by the entity at least once every six months and upon significant change to the in-scope environment. At a minimum, the scoping validation includes all the elements specified in Requirement 12.5.2.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1466, '12.5.3', '12.5.3 - Additional requirement for service providers only: Significant changes to organi...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: Significant changes to organizational structure result in a documented (internal) review of the impact to PCI DSS scope and applicability of controls, with results communicated to executive management.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1467, '12.6', '12.6 - Security awareness education is an ongoing activity.', 'Security awareness education is an ongoing activity.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1468, '12.6.1', '12.6.1 - A formal security awareness program is implemented to make all personnel aware o...', 'A formal security awareness program is implemented to make all personnel aware of the entity’s information security policy and procedures, and their role in protecting the cardholder data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1469, '12.6.2', '12.6.2 - The security awareness program is:     Reviewed at least once every 12 months,...', 'The security awareness program is:
    Reviewed at least once every 12 months, and
    Updated as needed to address any new threats and vulnerabilities that may impact the security of the entity’s CDE, or the information provided to personnel about their role in protecting cardholder data.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1470, '12.6.3', '12.6.3 - Personnel receive security awareness training as follows:     Upon hire and at...', 'Personnel receive security awareness training as follows:
    Upon hire and at least once every 12 months.
    Multiple methods of communication are used.
    Personnel acknowledge at least once every 12 months that they have read and understood the information security policy and procedures.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1471, '12.6.3.1', '12.6.3.1 - Security awareness training includes awareness of threats and vulnerabilities th...', 'Security awareness training includes awareness of threats and vulnerabilities that could impact the security of the CDE, including but not limited to:
    Phishing and related attacks.
    Social engineering.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1472, '12.6.3.2', '12.6.3.2 - Security awareness training includes awareness about the acceptable use of end-u...', 'Security awareness training includes awareness about the acceptable use of end-user technologies in accordance with Requirement 12.2.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1473, '12.7', '12.7 - Personnel are screened to reduce risks from insider threats.', 'Personnel are screened to reduce risks from insider threats.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1475, '12.8', '12.8 - Risk to information assets associated with third-party service provider (TPSP) r...', 'Risk to information assets associated with third-party service provider (TPSP) relationships is managed.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1476, '12.8.1', '12.8.1 - A list of all third-party service providers (TPSPs) with which account data is s...', 'A list of all third-party service providers (TPSPs) with which account data is shared or that could affect the security of account data is maintained, including a description for each of the services provided.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1477, '12.8.2', '12.8.2 - Written agreements with TPSPs are maintained as follows:     Written agreement...', 'Written agreements with TPSPs are maintained as follows:
    Written agreements are maintained with all TPSPs with which account data is shared or that could affect the security of the CDE.
    Written agreements include acknowledgments from TPSPs that they are responsible for the security of account data the TPSPs possess or otherwise store, process, or transmit on behalf of the entity, or to the extent that they could impact the security of the entity’s CDE.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1478, '12.8.3', '12.8.3 - An established process is implemented for engaging TPSPs, including proper due d...', 'An established process is implemented for engaging TPSPs, including proper due diligence prior to engagement.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1479, '12.8.4', '12.8.4 - A program is implemented to monitor TPSPs’ PCI DSS compliance status at least on...', 'A program is implemented to monitor TPSPs’ PCI DSS compliance status at least once every 12 months.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1480, '12.8.5', '12.8.5 - Information is maintained about which PCI DSS requirements are managed by each T...', 'Information is maintained about which PCI DSS requirements are managed by each TPSP, which are managed by the entity, and any that are shared between the TPSP and the entity.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1481, '12.9', '12.9 - Third-party service providers (TPSPs) support their customers’ PCI DSS complianc...', 'Third-party service providers (TPSPs) support their customers’ PCI DSS compliance.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1482, '12.9.1', '12.9.1 - Additional requirement for service providers only: TPSPs acknowledge in writing ...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: TPSPs acknowledge in writing to customers that they are responsible for the security of account data the TPSP possesses or otherwise stores, processes, or transmits on behalf of the customer, or to the extent that they could impact the security of the customer’s CDE.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1483, '12.9.2', '12.9.2 - Additional requirement for service providers only: TPSPs support their customers...', 'Additional requirement for service providers only: TPSPs support their customers’ requests for information to meet Requirements
12.8.4 and 12.8.5 by providing the following upon customer request:
    PCI DSS compliance status information for any service the TPSP performs on behalf of customers (Requirement 12.8.4).
    Information about which PCI DSS requirements are the responsibility of the TPSP and which are the responsibility of the customer, including any shared responsibilities (Requirement 12.8.5).', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1484, '12.10', '12.10 - Suspected and confirmed security incidents that could impact the CDE are respond...', 'Suspected and confirmed security incidents that could impact the CDE are responded to immediately.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1485, '12.10.1', '12.10.1 - An incident response plan exists and is ready to be activated in the event of a ...', 'An incident response plan exists and is ready to be activated in the event of a suspected or confirmed security incident. The plan includes, but is not limited to:
    Roles, responsibilities, and communication and contact strategies in the event of a suspected or confirmed security incident, including notification of payment brands and acquirers, at a minimum.
    Incident response procedures with specific containment and mitigation activities for different types of incidents.
    Business recovery and continuity procedures.
    Data backup processes.
    Analysis of legal requirements for reporting compromises.
    Coverage and responses of all critical system components.
    Reference or inclusion of incident response procedures from the payment brands.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1486, '12.10.2', '12.10.2 - At least once every 12 months, the security incident response plan is:     Rev...', 'At least once every 12 months, the security incident response plan is:
    Reviewed and the content is updated as needed.
    Tested, including all elements listed in Requirement 12.10.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1487, '12.10.3', '12.10.3 - Specific personnel are designated to be available on a 24/7 basis to respond to ...', 'Specific personnel are designated to be available on a 24/7 basis to respond to suspected or confirmed security incidents.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1488, '12.10.4', '12.10.4 - Personnel responsible for responding to suspected and confirmed security inciden...', 'Personnel responsible for responding to suspected and confirmed security incidents are appropriately and periodically trained on their incident response responsibilities.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1489, '12.10.4.1', '12.10.4.1 - The frequency of periodic training for incident response personnel is defined in...', 'The frequency of periodic training for incident response personnel is defined in the entity’s targeted risk analysis, which is performed according to all elements specified in Requirement 12.3.1.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1490, '12.10.5', '12.10.5 - The security incident response plan includes monitoring and responding to alerts...', 'The security incident response plan includes monitoring and responding to alerts from security monitoring systems, including but not limited to:
    Intrusion-detection and intrusion-prevention systems.
    Network security controls.
    Change-detection mechanisms for critical files.
    The change-and tamper-detection mechanism for payment pages. This bullet is a best practice until its effective date; refer to Applicability Notes below for details.
    Detection of unauthorized wireless access points.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1491, '12.10.6', '12.10.6 - The security incident response plan is modified and evolved according to lessons...', 'The security incident response plan is modified and evolved according to lessons learned and to incorporate industry developments.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1492, '12.10.7', '12.10.7 - Incident response procedures are in place, to be initiated upon the detection of...', 'Incident response procedures are in place, to be initiated upon the detection of stored PAN anywhere it is not expected, and include:
    Determining what to do if PAN is discovered outside the CDE, including its retrieval, secure deletion, and/or migration into the currently defined CDE, as applicable.
    Identifying whether sensitive authentication data is stored with PAN.
    Determining where the account data came from and how it ended up where it was not expected.
    Remediating data leaks or process gaps that resulted in the account data being where it was not expected.', 'PCI DSS v4.0 (Custom)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Requirement 12', NULL, '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', '2026-01-08 22:48:55.23426', 'PCI DSS', '', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1495, 'AC-2.1', 'Automated System Account Management', 'Support the management of system accounts using {{ insert: param, ac-02.01_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', '', NULL, NULL, 'active', 6, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Automated system account management includes using automated mechanisms to create, enable, modify, disable, and remove accounts; notify account managers when an account is created, enabled, modified, disabled, or removed, or when users are terminated or transferred; monitor system account usage; and report atypical system account usage. Automated mechanisms can include internal system functions and email, telephonic, and text messaging notifications.', NULL, '## 1. Implementation Guidance

**Automate Account Lifecycle Processes**
- Integrate your identity provider (IdP) with HR systems to automatically create, modify, disable, and delete accounts based on employee status changes. Use SCIM or custom scripts.
- Implement automated provisioning/deprovisioning workflows in IAM tools (e.g., Okta Workflows, Azure AD Lifecycle Workflows, Saviynt) triggered by HR events.
- For cloud environments, use Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools like Terraform or AWS CloudFormation to manage service accounts and roles, ensuring they are version-controlled and auditable.

**Enforce Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)**
- Define standardized roles with least-privilege permissions in your IdP. Use group-based assignments rather than individual permissions.
- Automatically assign users to roles/groups based on attributes (department, job code, location) synchronized from HR systems.
- For cloud platforms, use managed services like AWS IAM Identity Center or Azure PIM to automate access reviews and role assignments.

**Implement Automated Access Reviews**
- Schedule and run periodic access reviews using IAM tools. Automate reminders, escalations, and revocation of unused access.
- Configure automated deprovisioning for inactive accounts (e.g., disable after 30 days of inactivity, delete after 90 days).
- Use cloud-native tools like AWS IAM Access Analyzer or Azure AD Access Reviews to detect and remediate excessive permissions.

**Monitor and Audit Automatically**
- Send all account management events (creations, modifications, deletions) to a centralized SIEM or log management platform.
- Set up real-time alerts for suspicious activities (e.g., after-hours account creation, bulk modifications, privilege escalation).
- Use cloud-native monitoring (e.g., AWS CloudTrail, Azure Monitor, GCP Audit Logs) with automated alerting rules.

## 2. Evidence Artifacts

- **Workflow Documentation:** Screenshots or exports of automated provisioning/deprovisioning workflows from your IAM tool.
- **HR-IAM Integration Proof:** Configuration details showing synchronization between HRIS (e.g., Workday, BambooHR) and IdP.
- **Access Review Reports:** Automated reports showing review cycles, outcomes, and remediation actions taken.
- **Audit Logs:** Logs from IAM, cloud platforms, and SIEM showing automated account lifecycle events.
- **IaC Templates:** Version-controlled Terraform/CloudFormation code used to manage service accounts.
- **Alert Logs:** Records of automated alerts triggered for anomalous account management activities.

## 3. Common Pitfalls

- **Over-Privileged Service Accounts:** Failing to apply least privilege to automated service accounts, especially in cloud environments.
- **Incomplete Deprovisioning:** Automating account disablement but not removing access from all systems (e.g., cloud consoles, SaaS apps, local admin accounts).
- **Lack of Exception Handling:** Not having manual review processes for edge cases (contractors, consultants, emergency access).
- **Ignoring Inactive Accounts:** Focusing only on joiner/mover/leaver processes while neglecting dormant accounts that accumulate over time.
- **Cloud Misconfigurations:** Using root/owner accounts for automation instead of dedicated service principals with limited permissions.
- **Testing Gaps:** Not regularly testing automated workflows to ensure they function correctly during actual employee transitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1496, 'AC-2.2', 'Automated Temporary and Emergency Account Management', 'Automatically {{ insert: param, ac-02.02_odp.01 }} temporary and emergency accounts after {{ insert: param, ac-02.02_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Management of temporary and emergency accounts includes the removal or disabling of such accounts automatically after a predefined time period rather than at the convenience of the system administrator. Automatic removal or disabling of accounts provides a more consistent implementation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1498, 'AC-2.4', 'Automated Audit Actions', 'Automatically audit account creation, modification, enabling, disabling, and removal actions.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Account management audit records are defined in accordance with [AU-02](#au-2) and reviewed, analyzed, and reported in accordance with [AU-06](#au-6).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1499, 'AC-2.5', 'Inactivity Logout', 'Require that users log out when {{ insert: param, ac-02.05_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Inactivity logout is behavior- or policy-based and requires users to take physical action to log out when they are expecting inactivity longer than the defined period. Automatic enforcement of inactivity logout is addressed by [AC-11](#ac-11).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1578, 'AC-9.3', 'Notification of Account Changes', 'Notify the user, upon successful logon, of changes to {{ insert: param, ac-09.03_odp.01 }} during {{ insert: param, ac-09.03_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Information about changes to security-related account characteristics within a specified time period allows users to recognize if changes were made without their knowledge.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4416, 'SCVS-3.11', 'Authorization Enforcement', 'Verify that application build pipeline enforces authorization and defaults to deny.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:10.385803', '2026-02-06 15:18:10.385803', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Authorization Enforcement based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1497, 'AC-2.3', 'Disable Accounts', 'Disable accounts within {{ insert: param, ac-02.03_odp.01 }} when the accounts: Have expired; Are no longer associated with a user or individual; Are in violation of organizational policy; or Have been inactive for {{ insert: param, ac-02.03_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Disabling expired, inactive, or otherwise anomalous accounts supports the concepts of least privilege and least functionality which reduce the attack surface of the system.', NULL, '## AC-2.3 - Disable Accounts: Implementation Guidance

### 1. Implementation Guidance

**Define Policy Parameters First:**
- Establish organizational values for `ac-02.03_odp.01` (timeframe for disabling accounts) and `ac-02.03_odp.02` (inactivity period). Common values are 24-72 hours for disabling and 30-90 days for inactivity.
- Document specific conditions that constitute policy violations warranting immediate account disablement.

**Automate Account Lifecycle Management:**
- Integrate with HR systems to automatically disable accounts upon employee termination or role change.
- Implement automated scripts or identity governance tools to identify and flag accounts meeting disablement criteria.
- For cloud environments, leverage native capabilities (AWS IAM Access Analyzer, Azure AD Identity Protection, GCP IAM Recommender) to detect unused accounts.

**Establish Account Review Processes:**
- Conduct regular access reviews (quarterly recommended) to validate active accounts.
- Implement automated alerts for accounts approaching inactivity thresholds.
- Create exception processes for service accounts with documented business justification.

**Technical Implementation Steps:**
1. Configure identity providers to automatically disable accounts after specified inactivity periods
2. Set up SIEM alerts for failed login attempts to disabled accounts
3. Implement just-in-time access provisioning for privileged accounts
4. Use infrastructure-as-code to manage service accounts with expiration dates
5. Establish break-glass procedures for emergency access that automatically expire

### 2. Evidence Artifacts

**Policy Documentation:**
- Account management policy specifying disablement timeframes and conditions
- Risk assessment justifying chosen time parameters

**Technical Evidence:**
- Automated job logs showing account disablement actions
- Access review reports with reviewer attestations
- SIEM alerts and response logs for policy violation detection
- HR system integration logs showing termination-to-disablement workflows
- Cloud provider reports showing inactive account identification

**Monitoring Evidence:**
- Metrics dashboard showing: disabled account counts, average time to disable, exceptions granted
- Audit logs demonstrating review cycles were conducted
- Incident reports for policy violations leading to account disablement

### 3. Common Pitfalls

**Overlooking Service Accounts:**
- Failing to include non-human accounts in disablement policies
- Not implementing regular credential rotation for service accounts

**Inadequate Exception Management:**
- Allowing indefinite exceptions without periodic review
- Not documenting business justification for long-lived inactive accounts

**Cloud-Specific Challenges:**
- Assuming cloud providers automatically handle account lifecycle
- Neglecting cross-account access in AWS Organizations or Azure tenants
- Forgetting about programmatic access keys in addition to user accounts

**Process Gaps:**
- Relying solely on manual processes without automation
- Having no process for contractor or temporary employee account expiration
- Failing to test disablement procedures regularly

**Evidence Collection Issues:**
- Not maintaining chain of custody logs for forensic investigations
- Storing logs for insufficient time periods (retain for at least 90 days)
- Lack of integration between HR, IT, and security systems

**Remediation Tip:** Implement a quarterly "account cleanup" campaign where security teams manually verify automated processes are working correctly and address any exceptions or edge cases.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1502, 'AC-2.8', 'Dynamic Account Management', 'Create, activate, manage, and deactivate {{ insert: param, ac-02.08_odp }} dynamically.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Approaches for dynamically creating, activating, managing, and deactivating system accounts rely on automatically provisioning the accounts at runtime for entities that were previously unknown. Organizations plan for the dynamic management, creation, activation, and deactivation of system accounts by establishing trust relationships, business rules, and mechanisms with appropriate authorities to validate related authorizations and privileges.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1503, 'AC-2.9', 'Restrictions on Use of Shared and Group Accounts', 'Only permit the use of shared and group accounts that meet {{ insert: param, ac-02.09_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Before permitting the use of shared or group accounts, organizations consider the increased risk due to the lack of accountability with such accounts.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1504, 'AC-2.10', 'Shared and Group Account Credential Change', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1505, 'AC-2.11', 'Usage Conditions', 'Enforce {{ insert: param, ac-02.11_odp.01 }} for {{ insert: param, ac-02.11_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Specifying and enforcing usage conditions helps to enforce the principle of least privilege, increase user accountability, and enable effective account monitoring. Account monitoring includes alerts generated if the account is used in violation of organizational parameters. Organizations can describe specific conditions or circumstances under which system accounts can be used, such as by restricting usage to certain days of the week, time of day, or specific durations of time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1506, 'AC-2.12', 'Account Monitoring for Atypical Usage', 'Monitor system accounts for {{ insert: param, ac-02.12_odp.01 }} ; and Report atypical usage of system accounts to {{ insert: param, ac-02.12_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Atypical usage includes accessing systems at certain times of the day or from locations that are not consistent with the normal usage patterns of individuals. Monitoring for atypical usage may reveal rogue behavior by individuals or an attack in progress. Account monitoring may inadvertently create privacy risks since data collected to identify atypical usage may reveal previously unknown information about the behavior of individuals. Organizations assess and document privacy risks from monitoring accounts for atypical usage in their privacy impact assessment and make determinations that are in alignment with their privacy program plan.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1507, 'AC-2.13', 'Disable Accounts for High-risk Individuals', 'Disable accounts of individuals within {{ insert: param, ac-02.13_odp.01 }} of discovery of {{ insert: param, ac-02.13_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Users who pose a significant security and/or privacy risk include individuals for whom reliable evidence indicates either the intention to use authorized access to systems to cause harm or through whom adversaries will cause harm. Such harm includes adverse impacts to organizational operations, organizational assets, individuals, other organizations, or the Nation. Close coordination among system administrators, legal staff, human resource managers, and authorizing officials is essential when disabling system accounts for high-risk individuals.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1509, 'AC-3.1', 'Restricted Access to Privileged Functions', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1510, 'AC-3.2', 'Dual Authorization', 'Enforce dual authorization for {{ insert: param, ac-03.02_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Dual authorization, also known as two-person control, reduces risk related to insider threats. Dual authorization mechanisms require the approval of two authorized individuals to execute. To reduce the risk of collusion, organizations consider rotating dual authorization duties. Organizations consider the risk associated with implementing dual authorization mechanisms when immediate responses are necessary to ensure public and environmental safety.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1543, 'AC-4.19', 'Validation of Metadata', 'When transferring information between different security domains, implement {{ insert: param, ac-4.19_prm_1 }} on metadata.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'All information (including metadata and the data to which the metadata applies) is subject to filtering and inspection. Some organizations distinguish between metadata and data payloads (i.e., only the data to which the metadata is bound). Other organizations do not make such distinctions and consider metadata and the data to which the metadata applies to be part of the payload.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1579, 'AC-9.4', 'Additional Logon Information', 'Notify the user, upon successful logon, of the following additional information: {{ insert: param, ac-09.04_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Organizations can specify additional information to be provided to users upon logon, including the location of the last logon. User location is defined as information that can be determined by systems, such as Internet Protocol (IP) addresses from which network logons occurred, notifications of local logons, or device identifiers.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3677, '13.1.3', '**Verify that** rollback procedures can revert to previous model versions or safe-mode operations.', '**Verify that** rollback procedures can revert to previous model versions or safe-mode operations.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:23.359845', '2026-02-04 23:49:23.359845', NULL, '**C13.1 Kill-Switch & Override Mechanisms**

Provide shutdown or rollback paths when unsafe behavior of the AI system is observed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3678, '13.1.4', '**Verify that** override mechanisms are tested regularly.', '**Verify that** override mechanisms are tested regularly.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:23.580913', '2026-02-04 23:49:23.580913', NULL, '**C13.1 Kill-Switch & Override Mechanisms**

Provide shutdown or rollback paths when unsafe behavior of the AI system is observed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1512, 'AC-3.4', 'Discretionary Access Control', 'Enforce {{ insert: param, ac-3.4_prm_1 }} over the set of covered subjects and objects specified in the policy, and where the policy specifies that a subject that has been granted access to information can do one or more of the following: Pass the information to any other subjects or objects; Grant its privileges to other subjects; Change security attributes on subjects, objects, the system, or the system’s components; Choose the security attributes to be associated with newly created or revised objects; or Change the rules governing access control.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'When discretionary access control policies are implemented, subjects are not constrained with regard to what actions they can take with information for which they have already been granted access. Thus, subjects that have been granted access to information are not prevented from passing the information to other subjects or objects (i.e., subjects have the discretion to pass). Discretionary access control can operate in conjunction with mandatory access control as described in [AC-3(3)](#ac-3.3) and [AC-3(15)](#ac-3.15) . A subject that is constrained in its operation by mandatory access control policies can still operate under the less rigorous constraints of discretionary access control. Therefore, while [AC-3(3)](#ac-3.3) imposes constraints that prevent a subject from passing information to another subject operating at a different impact or classification level, [AC-3(4)](#ac-3.4) permits the subject to pass the information to any subject at the same impact or classification level. The policy is bounded by the system. Once the information is passed outside of system control, additional means may be required to ensure that the constraints remain in effect. While traditional definitions of discretionary access control require identity-based access control, that limitation is not required for this particular use of discretionary access control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1513, 'AC-3.5', 'Security-relevant Information', 'Prevent access to {{ insert: param, ac-03.05_odp }} except during secure, non-operable system states.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Security-relevant information is information within systems that can potentially impact the operation of security functions or the provision of security services in a manner that could result in failure to enforce system security and privacy policies or maintain the separation of code and data. Security-relevant information includes access control lists, filtering rules for routers or firewalls, configuration parameters for security services, and cryptographic key management information. Secure, non-operable system states include the times in which systems are not performing mission or business-related processing, such as when the system is offline for maintenance, boot-up, troubleshooting, or shut down.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1514, 'AC-3.6', 'Protection of User and System Information', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1515, 'AC-3.7', 'Role-based Access Control', 'Enforce a role-based access control policy over defined subjects and objects and control access based upon {{ insert: param, ac-3.7_prm_1 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Role-based access control (RBAC) is an access control policy that enforces access to objects and system functions based on the defined role (i.e., job function) of the subject. Organizations can create specific roles based on job functions and the authorizations (i.e., privileges) to perform needed operations on the systems associated with the organization-defined roles. When users are assigned to specific roles, they inherit the authorizations or privileges defined for those roles. RBAC simplifies privilege administration for organizations because privileges are not assigned directly to every user (which can be a large number of individuals) but are instead acquired through role assignments. RBAC can also increase privacy and security risk if individuals assigned to a role are given access to information beyond what they need to support organizational missions or business functions. RBAC can be implemented as a mandatory or discretionary form of access control. For organizations implementing RBAC with mandatory access controls, the requirements in [AC-3(3)](#ac-3.3) define the scope of the subjects and objects covered by the policy.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1516, 'AC-3.8', 'Revocation of Access Authorizations', 'Enforce the revocation of access authorizations resulting from changes to the security attributes of subjects and objects based on {{ insert: param, ac-03.08_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Revocation of access rules may differ based on the types of access revoked. For example, if a subject (i.e., user or process acting on behalf of a user) is removed from a group, access may not be revoked until the next time the object is opened or the next time the subject attempts to access the object. Revocation based on changes to security labels may take effect immediately. Organizations provide alternative approaches on how to make revocations immediate if systems cannot provide such capability and immediate revocation is necessary.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1544, 'AC-4.20', 'Approved Solutions', 'Employ {{ insert: param, ac-04.20_odp.01 }} to control the flow of {{ insert: param, ac-04.20_odp.02 }} across security domains.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Organizations define approved solutions and configurations in cross-domain policies and guidance in accordance with the types of information flows across classification boundaries. The National Security Agency (NSA) National Cross Domain Strategy and Management Office provides a listing of approved cross-domain solutions. Contact [ncdsmo@nsa.gov](mailto:ncdsmo@nsa.gov) for more information.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1678, 'AU-6.3', 'Correlate Audit Record Repositories', 'Analyze and correlate audit records across different repositories to gain organization-wide situational awareness.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Audit and Accountability', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Audit and Accountability', 'Organization-wide situational awareness includes awareness across all three levels of risk management (i.e., organizational level, mission/business process level, and information system level) and supports cross-organization awareness.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4419, 'SCVS-3.14', 'Job Audit Log', 'Verify that application build pipeline maintains a verifiable audit log of all build job changes.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:11.134894', '2026-02-06 15:18:11.134894', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Job Audit Log based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4420, 'SCVS-3.15', 'Maintenance Cadence', 'Verify that application build pipeline has required maintenance cadence where the entire stack is updated, patched, and re-certified for use.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:11.381061', '2026-02-06 15:18:11.381061', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Maintenance Cadence based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4422, 'SCVS-3.17', 'Manipulation Awareness', 'Verify that all build-time manipulations to source or binaries are known and well defined.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:11.875211', '2026-02-06 15:18:11.875211', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Manipulation Awareness based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1518, 'AC-3.10', 'Audited Override of Access Control Mechanisms', 'Employ an audited override of automated access control mechanisms under {{ insert: param, ac-03.10_odp.01 }} by {{ insert: param, ac-03.10_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'In certain situations, such as when there is a threat to human life or an event that threatens the organization’s ability to carry out critical missions or business functions, an override capability for access control mechanisms may be needed. Override conditions are defined by organizations and used only in those limited circumstances. Audit events are defined in [AU-2](#au-2) . Audit records are generated in [AU-12](#au-12).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1519, 'AC-3.11', 'Restrict Access to Specific Information Types', 'Restrict access to data repositories containing {{ insert: param, ac-03.11_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Restricting access to specific information is intended to provide flexibility regarding access control of specific information types within a system. For example, role-based access could be employed to allow access to only a specific type of personally identifiable information within a database rather than allowing access to the database in its entirety. Other examples include restricting access to cryptographic keys, authentication information, and selected system information.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1520, 'AC-3.12', 'Assert and Enforce Application Access', 'Require applications to assert, as part of the installation process, the access needed to the following system applications and functions: {{ insert: param, ac-03.12_odp }}; Provide an enforcement mechanism to prevent unauthorized access; and Approve access changes after initial installation of the application.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Asserting and enforcing application access is intended to address applications that need to access existing system applications and functions, including user contacts, global positioning systems, cameras, keyboards, microphones, networks, phones, or other files.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1522, 'AC-3.14', 'Individual Access', 'Provide {{ insert: param, ac-03.14_odp.01 }} to enable individuals to have access to the following elements of their personally identifiable information: {{ insert: param, ac-03.14_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Individual access affords individuals the ability to review personally identifiable information about them held within organizational records, regardless of format. Access helps individuals to develop an understanding about how their personally identifiable information is being processed. It can also help individuals ensure that their data is accurate. Access mechanisms can include request forms and application interfaces. For federal agencies, [PRIVACT](#18e71fec-c6fd-475a-925a-5d8495cf8455) processes can be located in systems of record notices and on agency websites. Access to certain types of records may not be appropriate (e.g., for federal agencies, law enforcement records within a system of records may be exempt from disclosure under the [PRIVACT](#18e71fec-c6fd-475a-925a-5d8495cf8455) ) or may require certain levels of authentication assurance. Organizational personnel consult with the senior agency official for privacy and legal counsel to determine appropriate mechanisms and access rights or limitations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1523, 'AC-3.15', 'Discretionary and Mandatory Access Control', 'Enforce {{ insert: param, ac-3.15_prm_1 }} over the set of covered subjects and objects specified in the policy; and Enforce {{ insert: param, ac-3.15_prm_2 }} over the set of covered subjects and objects specified in the policy.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Simultaneously implementing a mandatory access control policy and a discretionary access control policy can provide additional protection against the unauthorized execution of code by users or processes acting on behalf of users. This helps prevent a single compromised user or process from compromising the entire system.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1679, 'AU-6.4', 'Central Review and Analysis', 'Provide and implement the capability to centrally review and analyze audit records from multiple components within the system.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Audit and Accountability', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Audit and Accountability', 'Automated mechanisms for centralized reviews and analyses include Security Information and Event Management products.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4425, 'SCVS-3.20', 'Unused Component ID', 'Verify that unused direct and transitive components have been identified.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:12.617216', '2026-02-06 15:18:12.617216', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Unused Component ID based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4426, 'SCVS-3.21', 'Unused Component Removal', 'Verify that unused direct and transitive components have been removed from the application.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:12.862218', '2026-02-06 15:18:12.862218', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Unused Component Removal based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1525, 'AC-4.1', 'Object Security and Privacy Attributes', 'Use {{ insert: param, ac-4.1_prm_1 }} associated with {{ insert: param, ac-4.1_prm_2 }} to enforce {{ insert: param, ac-04.01_odp.09 }} as a basis for flow control decisions.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'Access Control', 'Information flow enforcement mechanisms compare security and privacy attributes associated with information (i.e., data content and structure) and source and destination objects and respond appropriately when the enforcement mechanisms encounter information flows not explicitly allowed by information flow policies. For example, an information object labeled Secret would be allowed to flow to a destination object labeled Secret, but an information object labeled Top Secret would not be allowed to flow to a destination object labeled Secret. A dataset of personally identifiable information may be tagged with restrictions against combining with other types of datasets and, thus, would not be allowed to flow to the restricted dataset. Security and privacy attributes can also include source and destination addresses employed in traffic filter firewalls. Flow enforcement using explicit security or privacy attributes can be used, for example, to control the release of certain types of information.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

Implement zero-trust networking with default-deny policies and encrypted communications.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4433, 'SCVS-4.10', 'Version Correlation', 'Verify that package repository provides a verifiable way of correlating component versions to specific source codes in version control.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V4: Package Management Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:14.840771', '2026-02-06 15:18:14.840771', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Version Correlation based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1558, 'AC-6', 'Least Privilege', 'Employ the principle of least privilege, allowing only authorized accesses for users (or processes acting on behalf of users) that are necessary to accomplish assigned organizational tasks.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Organizations employ least privilege for specific duties and systems. The principle of least privilege is also applied to system processes, ensuring that the processes have access to systems and operate at privilege levels no higher than necessary to accomplish organizational missions or business functions. Organizations consider the creation of additional processes, roles, and accounts as necessary to achieve least privilege. Organizations apply least privilege to the development, implementation, and operation of organizational systems.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1559, 'AC-6.1', 'Authorize Access to Security Functions', 'Authorize access for {{ insert: param, ac-06.01_odp.01 }} to: {{ insert: param, ac-6.1_prm_2 }} ; and {{ insert: param, ac-06.01_odp.05 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Security functions include establishing system accounts, configuring access authorizations (i.e., permissions, privileges), configuring settings for events to be audited, and establishing intrusion detection parameters. Security-relevant information includes filtering rules for routers or firewalls, configuration parameters for security services, cryptographic key management information, and access control lists. Authorized personnel include security administrators, system administrators, system security officers, system programmers, and other privileged users.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1560, 'AC-6.2', 'Non-privileged Access for Nonsecurity Functions', 'Require that users of system accounts (or roles) with access to {{ insert: param, ac-06.02_odp }} use non-privileged accounts or roles, when accessing nonsecurity functions.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Requiring the use of non-privileged accounts when accessing nonsecurity functions limits exposure when operating from within privileged accounts or roles. The inclusion of roles addresses situations where organizations implement access control policies, such as role-based access control, and where a change of role provides the same degree of assurance in the change of access authorizations for the user and the processes acting on behalf of the user as would be provided by a change between a privileged and non-privileged account.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1561, 'AC-6.3', 'Network Access to Privileged Commands', 'Authorize network access to {{ insert: param, ac-06.03_odp.01 }} only for {{ insert: param, ac-06.03_odp.02 }} and document the rationale for such access in the security plan for the system.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Network access is any access across a network connection in lieu of local access (i.e., user being physically present at the device).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1562, 'AC-6.4', 'Separate Processing Domains', 'Provide separate processing domains to enable finer-grained allocation of user privileges.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Providing separate processing domains for finer-grained allocation of user privileges includes using virtualization techniques to permit additional user privileges within a virtual machine while restricting privileges to other virtual machines or to the underlying physical machine, implementing separate physical domains, and employing hardware or software domain separation mechanisms.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1563, 'AC-6.5', 'Privileged Accounts', 'Restrict privileged accounts on the system to {{ insert: param, ac-06.05_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Privileged accounts, including super user accounts, are typically described as system administrator for various types of commercial off-the-shelf operating systems. Restricting privileged accounts to specific personnel or roles prevents day-to-day users from accessing privileged information or privileged functions. Organizations may differentiate in the application of restricting privileged accounts between allowed privileges for local accounts and for domain accounts provided that they retain the ability to control system configurations for key parameters and as otherwise necessary to sufficiently mitigate risk.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1564, 'AC-6.6', 'Privileged Access by Non-organizational Users', 'Prohibit privileged access to the system by non-organizational users.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'An organizational user is an employee or an individual considered by the organization to have the equivalent status of an employee. Organizational users include contractors, guest researchers, or individuals detailed from other organizations. A non-organizational user is a user who is not an organizational user. Policies and procedures for granting equivalent status of employees to individuals include a need-to-know, citizenship, and the relationship to the organization.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1565, 'AC-6.7', 'Review of User Privileges', 'Review {{ insert: param, ac-06.07_odp.01 }} the privileges assigned to {{ insert: param, ac-06.07_odp.02 }} to validate the need for such privileges; and Reassign or remove privileges, if necessary, to correctly reflect organizational mission and business needs.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'The need for certain assigned user privileges may change over time to reflect changes in organizational mission and business functions, environments of operation, technologies, or threats. A periodic review of assigned user privileges is necessary to determine if the rationale for assigning such privileges remains valid. If the need cannot be revalidated, organizations take appropriate corrective actions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1566, 'AC-6.8', 'Privilege Levels for Code Execution', 'Prevent the following software from executing at higher privilege levels than users executing the software: {{ insert: param, ac-06.08_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'In certain situations, software applications or programs need to execute with elevated privileges to perform required functions. However, depending on the software functionality and configuration, if the privileges required for execution are at a higher level than the privileges assigned to organizational users invoking such applications or programs, those users may indirectly be provided with greater privileges than assigned.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4435, 'SCVS-4.12', 'Code Signing', 'Verify that package repository requires code signing to publish packages to production repositories.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V4: Package Management Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:15.34043', '2026-02-06 15:18:15.34043', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Code Signing based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4436, 'SCVS-4.13', 'Remote Integrity Verification', 'Verify that package manager verifies the integrity of packages when they are retrieved from remote repository.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V4: Package Management Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:15.586716', '2026-02-06 15:18:15.586716', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Remote Integrity Verification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1570, 'AC-7.1', 'Automatic Account Lock', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1571, 'AC-7.2', 'Purge or Wipe Mobile Device', 'Purge or wipe information from {{ insert: param, ac-07.02_odp.01 }} based on {{ insert: param, ac-07.02_odp.02 }} after {{ insert: param, ac-07.02_odp.03 }} consecutive, unsuccessful device logon attempts.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'A mobile device is a computing device that has a small form factor such that it can be carried by a single individual; is designed to operate without a physical connection; possesses local, non-removable or removable data storage; and includes a self-contained power source. Purging or wiping the device applies only to mobile devices for which the organization-defined number of unsuccessful logons occurs. The logon is to the mobile device, not to any one account on the device. Successful logons to accounts on mobile devices reset the unsuccessful logon count to zero. Purging or wiping may be unnecessary if the information on the device is protected with sufficiently strong encryption mechanisms.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1572, 'AC-7.3', 'Biometric Attempt Limiting', 'Limit the number of unsuccessful biometric logon attempts to {{ insert: param, ac-07.03_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Biometrics are probabilistic in nature. The ability to successfully authenticate can be impacted by many factors, including matching performance and presentation attack detection mechanisms. Organizations select the appropriate number of attempts for users based on organizationally-defined factors.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1573, 'AC-7.4', 'Use of Alternate Authentication Factor', 'Allow the use of {{ insert: param, ac-07.04_odp.01 }} that are different from the primary authentication factors after the number of organization-defined consecutive invalid logon attempts have been exceeded; and Enforce a limit of {{ insert: param, ac-07.04_odp.02 }} consecutive invalid logon attempts through use of the alternative factors by a user during a {{ insert: param, ac-07.04_odp.03 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'The use of alternate authentication factors supports the objective of availability and allows a user who has inadvertently been locked out to use additional authentication factors to bypass the lockout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1575, 'AC-9', 'Previous Logon Notification', 'Notify the user, upon successful logon to the system, of the date and time of the last logon.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Previous logon notification is applicable to system access via human user interfaces and access to systems that occurs in other types of architectures. Information about the last successful logon allows the user to recognize if the date and time provided is not consistent with the user’s last access.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1576, 'AC-9.1', 'Unsuccessful Logons', 'Notify the user, upon successful logon, of the number of unsuccessful logon attempts since the last successful logon.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Information about the number of unsuccessful logon attempts since the last successful logon allows the user to recognize if the number of unsuccessful logon attempts is consistent with the user’s actual logon attempts.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1577, 'AC-9.2', 'Successful and Unsuccessful Logons', 'Notify the user, upon successful logon, of the number of {{ insert: param, ac-09.02_odp.01 }} during {{ insert: param, ac-09.02_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Information about the number of successful and unsuccessful logon attempts within a specified time period allows the user to recognize if the number and type of logon attempts are consistent with the user’s actual logon attempts.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3266, '1.1.2', '**Verify that** training data processes exclude unnecessary features, attributes, or fields (e.g., unused metadata, sensitive PII, leaked test data).', '**Verify that** training data processes exclude unnecessary features, attributes, or fields (e.g., unused metadata, sensitive PII, leaked test data).', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:43:25.531556', '2026-02-04 23:43:25.531556', NULL, '**C1.1 Training Data Provenance**

Maintain a verifiable inventory of all datasets, accept only trusted sources, and log every change for auditability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3269, '1.2.1', '**Verify that** access controls protect training data storage and pipelines.', '**Verify that** access controls protect training data storage and pipelines.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:43:26.259891', '2026-02-04 23:43:26.259891', NULL, '**C1.2 Training Data Security & Integrity**

Restrict access to training data, encrypt it at rest and in transit, and validate its integrity to prevent tampering, theft, or data poisoning.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4438, 'SCVS-4.15', 'TLS Enforcement', 'Verify that package repository enforces use of TLS for all interactions.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V4: Package Management Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:16.083816', '2026-02-06 15:18:16.083816', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for TLS Enforcement based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4439, 'SCVS-4.16', 'TLS Validation', 'Verify that package manager validates TLS certificate chain to repository and fails securely when validation fails.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V4: Package Management Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:16.338643', '2026-02-06 15:18:16.338643', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for TLS Validation based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4440, 'SCVS-4.17', 'Static Analysis', 'Verify that package repository requires and/or performs static code analysis prior to publishing a component and makes results available for others to consume.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V4: Package Management Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:16.588978', '2026-02-06 15:18:16.588978', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Static Analysis based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4441, 'SCVS-4.18', 'No Execution', 'Verify that package manager does not execute component code.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V4: Package Management Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:16.835272', '2026-02-06 15:18:16.835272', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for No Execution based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4442, 'SCVS-4.19', 'Installation Documentation', 'Verify that package manager documents package installation in machine-readable form.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V4: Package Management Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:17.0798', '2026-02-06 15:18:17.0798', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Installation Documentation based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4444, 'SCVS-5.5', 'Exploitability Identification', 'Verify that an automated process of identifying confirmed dataflow exploitability is used.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V5: Component Analysis Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:17.569274', '2026-02-06 15:18:17.569274', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Exploitability Identification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1582, 'AC-11.1', 'Pattern-hiding Displays', 'Conceal, via the device lock, information previously visible on the display with a publicly viewable image.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'The pattern-hiding display can include static or dynamic images, such as patterns used with screen savers, photographic images, solid colors, clock, battery life indicator, or a blank screen with the caveat that controlled unclassified information is not displayed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1583, 'AC-12', 'Session Termination', 'Automatically terminate a user session after {{ insert: param, ac-12_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Session termination addresses the termination of user-initiated logical sessions (in contrast to [SC-10](#sc-10) , which addresses the termination of network connections associated with communications sessions (i.e., network disconnect)). A logical session (for local, network, and remote access) is initiated whenever a user (or process acting on behalf of a user) accesses an organizational system. Such user sessions can be terminated without terminating network sessions. Session termination ends all processes associated with a user’s logical session except for those processes that are specifically created by the user (i.e., session owner) to continue after the session is terminated. Conditions or trigger events that require automatic termination of the session include organization-defined periods of user inactivity, targeted responses to certain types of incidents, or time-of-day restrictions on system use.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1584, 'AC-12.1', 'User-initiated Logouts', 'Provide a logout capability for user-initiated communications sessions whenever authentication is used to gain access to {{ insert: param, ac-12.01_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Information resources to which users gain access via authentication include local workstations, databases, and password-protected websites or web-based services.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1585, 'AC-12.2', 'Termination Message', 'Display an explicit logout message to users indicating the termination of authenticated communications sessions.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Logout messages for web access can be displayed after authenticated sessions have been terminated. However, for certain types of sessions, including file transfer protocol (FTP) sessions, systems typically send logout messages as final messages prior to terminating sessions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1586, 'AC-12.3', 'Timeout Warning Message', 'Display an explicit message to users indicating that the session will end in {{ insert: param, ac-12.03_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'To increase usability, notify users of pending session termination and prompt users to continue the session. The pending session termination time period is based on the parameters defined in the [AC-12](#ac-12) base control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1587, 'AC-13', 'Supervision and Review — Access Control', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1589, 'AC-14.1', 'Necessary Uses', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1590, 'AC-15', 'Automated Marking', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1591, 'AC-16', 'Security and Privacy Attributes', 'Provide the means to associate {{ insert: param, ac-16_prm_1 }} with {{ insert: param, ac-16_prm_2 }} for information in storage, in process, and/or in transmission; Ensure that the attribute associations are made and retained with the information; Establish the following permitted security and privacy attributes from the attributes defined in [AC-16a](#ac-16_smt.a) for {{ insert: param, ac-16_prm_3 }}: {{ insert: param, ac-16_prm_4 }}; Determine the following permitted attribute values or ranges for each of the established attributes: {{ insert: param, ac-16_odp.09 }}; Audit changes to attributes; and Review {{ insert: param, ac-16_prm_6 }} for applicability {{ insert: param, ac-16_prm_7 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.577168', 'Access Control', 'Information is represented internally within systems using abstractions known as data structures. Internal data structures can represent different types of entities, both active and passive. Active entities, also known as subjects, are typically associated with individuals, devices, or processes acting on behalf of individuals. Passive entities, also known as objects, are typically associated with data structures, such as records, buffers, tables, files, inter-process pipes, and communications ports. Security attributes, a form of metadata, are abstractions that represent the basic properties or characteristics of active and passive entities with respect to safeguarding information. Privacy attributes, which may be used independently or in conjunction with security attributes, represent the basic properties or characteristics of active or passive entities with respect to the management of personally identifiable information. Attributes can be either explicitly or implicitly associated with the information contained in organizational systems or system components.

Attributes may be associated with active entities (i.e., subjects) that have the potential to send or receive information, cause information to flow among objects, or change the system state. These attributes may also be associated with passive entities (i.e., objects) that contain or receive information. The association of attributes to subjects and objects by a system is referred to as binding and is inclusive of setting the attribute value and the attribute type. Attributes, when bound to data or information, permit the enforcement of security and privacy policies for access control and information flow control, including data retention limits, permitted uses of personally identifiable information, and identification of personal information within data objects. Such enforcement occurs through organizational processes or system functions or mechanisms. The binding techniques implemented by systems affect the strength of attribute binding to information. Binding strength and the assurance associated with binding techniques play important parts in the trust that organizations have in the information flow enforcement process. The binding techniques affect the number and degree of additional reviews required by organizations. The content or assigned values of attributes can directly affect the ability of individuals to access organizational information.

Organizations can define the types of attributes needed for systems to support missions or business functions. There are many values that can be assigned to a security attribute. By specifying the permitted attribute ranges and values, organizations ensure that attribute values are meaningful and relevant. Labeling refers to the association of attributes with the subjects and objects represented by the internal data structures within systems. This facilitates system-based enforcement of information security and privacy policies. Labels include classification of information in accordance with legal and compliance requirements (e.g., top secret, secret, confidential, controlled unclassified), information impact level; high value asset information, access authorizations, nationality; data life cycle protection (i.e., encryption and data expiration), personally identifiable information processing permissions, including individual consent to personally identifiable information processing, and contractor affiliation. A related term to labeling is marking. Marking refers to the association of attributes with objects in a human-readable form and displayed on system media. Marking enables manual, procedural, or process-based enforcement of information security and privacy policies. Security and privacy labels may have the same value as media markings (e.g., top secret, secret, confidential). See [MP-3](#mp-3) (Media Marking).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3267, '1.1.3', '**Verify that** all dataset changes are subject to a logged approval workflow.', '**Verify that** all dataset changes are subject to a logged approval workflow.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:43:25.770051', '2026-02-04 23:43:25.770051', NULL, '**C1.1 Training Data Provenance**

Maintain a verifiable inventory of all datasets, accept only trusted sources, and log every change for auditability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3268, '1.1.4', '**Verify that** datasets or subsets are watermarked or fingerprinted where feasible.', '**Verify that** datasets or subsets are watermarked or fingerprinted where feasible.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:43:26.016522', '2026-02-04 23:43:26.016522', NULL, '**C1.1 Training Data Provenance**

Maintain a verifiable inventory of all datasets, accept only trusted sources, and log every change for auditability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4446, 'SCVS-5.7', 'Outdated Component Identification', 'Verify that an automated process of identifying out-of-date components is used.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V5: Component Analysis Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:18.063871', '2026-02-06 15:18:18.063871', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Outdated Component Identification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4447, 'SCVS-5.8', 'EOL Identification', 'Verify that an automated process of identifying end-of-life / end-of-support components is used.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V5: Component Analysis Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:18.310949', '2026-02-06 15:18:18.310949', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for EOL Identification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4448, 'SCVS-5.9', 'Type Identification', 'Verify that an automated process of identifying component type is used.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V5: Component Analysis Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:18.558883', '2026-02-06 15:18:18.558883', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Type Identification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4450, 'SCVS-5.11', 'Quantity Identification', 'Verify that an automated process of identifying component quantity is used.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V5: Component Analysis Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:19.065521', '2026-02-06 15:18:19.065521', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Quantity Identification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4451, 'SCVS-5.12', 'License Identification', 'Verify that an automated process of identifying component license is used.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V5: Component Analysis Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:19.315389', '2026-02-06 15:18:19.315389', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for License Identification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4452, 'SCVS-6.4', 'Pedigree Documentation', 'Verify that pedigree of component modification is documented and verifiable.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V6: Pedigree and Provenance Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:19.565922', '2026-02-06 15:18:19.565922', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Pedigree Documentation based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1593, 'AC-16.2', 'Attribute Value Changes by Authorized Individuals', 'Provide authorized individuals (or processes acting on behalf of individuals) the capability to define or change the value of associated security and privacy attributes.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'The content or assigned values of attributes can directly affect the ability of individuals to access organizational information. Therefore, it is important for systems to be able to limit the ability to create or modify attributes to authorized individuals.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1594, 'AC-16.3', 'Maintenance of Attribute Associations by System', 'Maintain the association and integrity of {{ insert: param, ac-16.3_prm_1 }} to {{ insert: param, ac-16.3_prm_2 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Maintaining the association and integrity of security and privacy attributes to subjects and objects with sufficient assurance helps to ensure that the attribute associations can be used as the basis of automated policy actions. The integrity of specific items, such as security configuration files, may be maintained through the use of an integrity monitoring mechanism that detects anomalies and changes that deviate from "known good" baselines. Automated policy actions include retention date expirations, access control decisions, information flow control decisions, and information disclosure decisions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1596, 'AC-16.5', 'Attribute Displays on Objects to Be Output', 'Display security and privacy attributes in human-readable form on each object that the system transmits to output devices to identify {{ insert: param, ac-16.05_odp.01 }} using {{ insert: param, ac-16.05_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'System outputs include printed pages, screens, or equivalent items. System output devices include printers, notebook computers, video displays, smart phones, and tablets. To mitigate the risk of unauthorized exposure of information (e.g., shoulder surfing), the outputs display full attribute values when unmasked by the subscriber.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1597, 'AC-16.6', 'Maintenance of Attribute Association', 'Require personnel to associate and maintain the association of {{ insert: param, ac-16.6_prm_1 }} with {{ insert: param, ac-16.6_prm_2 }} in accordance with {{ insert: param, ac-16.6_prm_3 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Maintaining attribute association requires individual users (as opposed to the system) to maintain associations of defined security and privacy attributes with subjects and objects.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1598, 'AC-16.7', 'Consistent Attribute Interpretation', 'Provide a consistent interpretation of security and privacy attributes transmitted between distributed system components.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'To enforce security and privacy policies across multiple system components in distributed systems, organizations provide a consistent interpretation of security and privacy attributes employed in access enforcement and flow enforcement decisions. Organizations can establish agreements and processes to help ensure that distributed system components implement attributes with consistent interpretations in automated access enforcement and flow enforcement actions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1599, 'AC-16.8', 'Association Techniques and Technologies', 'Implement {{ insert: param, ac-16.8_prm_1 }} in associating security and privacy attributes to information.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'The association of security and privacy attributes to information within systems is important for conducting automated access enforcement and flow enforcement actions. The association of such attributes to information (i.e., binding) can be accomplished with technologies and techniques that provide different levels of assurance. For example, systems can cryptographically bind attributes to information using digital signatures that support cryptographic keys protected by hardware devices (sometimes known as hardware roots of trust).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1600, 'AC-16.9', 'Attribute Reassignment — Regrading Mechanisms', 'Change security and privacy attributes associated with information only via regrading mechanisms validated using {{ insert: param, ac-16.9_prm_1 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'A regrading mechanism is a trusted process authorized to re-classify and re-label data in accordance with a defined policy exception. Validated regrading mechanisms are used by organizations to provide the requisite levels of assurance for attribute reassignment activities. The validation is facilitated by ensuring that regrading mechanisms are single purpose and of limited function. Since security and privacy attribute changes can directly affect policy enforcement actions, implementing trustworthy regrading mechanisms is necessary to help ensure that such mechanisms perform in a consistent and correct mode of operation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1613, 'AC-18', 'Wireless Access', 'Establish configuration requirements, connection requirements, and implementation guidance for each type of wireless access; and Authorize each type of wireless access to the system prior to allowing such connections.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Wireless technologies include microwave, packet radio (ultra-high frequency or very high frequency), 802.11x, and Bluetooth. Wireless networks use authentication protocols that provide authenticator protection and mutual authentication.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4066, 'SCVS-6.3', 'Provenance Documentation', 'Verify that provenance of modified components is known and documented.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V6: Pedigree and Provenance Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:40:50.790542', '2026-02-06 13:40:50.790542', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for End-of-Life Management based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4454, 'SCVS-6.6', 'Modification Analysis', 'Verify that modified components are analyzed with the same level of precision as unmodified components.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V6: Pedigree and Provenance Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:20.072915', '2026-02-06 15:18:20.072915', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Modification Analysis based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4455, 'SCVS-6.7', 'Unique Risk Analysis', 'Verify that risk unique to modified components can be analyzed and associated specifically to modified variant.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V6: Pedigree and Provenance Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:20.321487', '2026-02-06 15:18:20.321487', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Unique Risk Analysis based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3270, '1.2.2', '**Verify that** all access to training data is logged, including user, time, and action.', '**Verify that** all access to training data is logged, including user, time, and action.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:43:26.507495', '2026-02-04 23:43:26.507495', NULL, '**C1.2 Training Data Security & Integrity**

Restrict access to training data, encrypt it at rest and in transit, and validate its integrity to prevent tampering, theft, or data poisoning.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4387, 'SCVS-2.6', 'Signature Verification Performance', 'Verify that SBOM signature verification is performed.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V2: Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:01.184596', '2026-02-06 15:18:01.184596', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Signature Verification Performance based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4388, 'SCVS-3.7', 'Version Control Source', 'Verify that application build pipeline may only perform builds of source code maintained in version control systems.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:01.439226', '2026-02-06 15:18:01.439226', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Version Control Source based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1603, 'AC-17.1', 'Monitoring and Control', 'Employ automated mechanisms to monitor and control remote access methods.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Monitoring and control of remote access methods allows organizations to detect attacks and help ensure compliance with remote access policies by auditing the connection activities of remote users on a variety of system components, including servers, notebook computers, workstations, smart phones, and tablets. Audit logging for remote access is enforced by [AU-2](#au-2) . Audit events are defined in [AU-2a](#au-2_smt.a).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1604, 'AC-17.2', 'Protection of Confidentiality and Integrity Using Encryption', 'Implement cryptographic mechanisms to protect the confidentiality and integrity of remote access sessions.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Virtual private networks can be used to protect the confidentiality and integrity of remote access sessions. Transport Layer Security (TLS) is an example of a cryptographic protocol that provides end-to-end communications security over networks and is used for Internet communications and online transactions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1605, 'AC-17.3', 'Managed Access Control Points', 'Route remote accesses through authorized and managed network access control points.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Organizations consider the Trusted Internet Connections (TIC) initiative [DHS TIC](#4f42ee6e-86cc-403b-a51f-76c2b4f81b54) requirements for external network connections since limiting the number of access control points for remote access reduces attack surfaces.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1606, 'AC-17.4', 'Privileged Commands and Access', 'Authorize the execution of privileged commands and access to security-relevant information via remote access only in a format that provides assessable evidence and for the following needs: {{ insert: param, ac-17.4_prm_1 }} ; and Document the rationale for remote access in the security plan for the system.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Remote access to systems represents a significant potential vulnerability that can be exploited by adversaries. As such, restricting the execution of privileged commands and access to security-relevant information via remote access reduces the exposure of the organization and the susceptibility to threats by adversaries to the remote access capability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1607, 'AC-17.5', 'Monitoring for Unauthorized Connections', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1608, 'AC-17.6', 'Protection of Mechanism Information', 'Protect information about remote access mechanisms from unauthorized use and disclosure.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Remote access to organizational information by non-organizational entities can increase the risk of unauthorized use and disclosure about remote access mechanisms. The organization considers including remote access requirements in the information exchange agreements with other organizations, as applicable. Remote access requirements can also be included in rules of behavior (see [PL-4](#pl-4) ) and access agreements (see [PS-6](#ps-6)).', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1609, 'AC-17.7', 'Additional Protection for Security Function Access', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1610, 'AC-17.8', 'Disable Nonsecure Network Protocols', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1611, 'AC-17.9', 'Disconnect or Disable Access', 'Provide the capability to disconnect or disable remote access to the system within {{ insert: param, ac-17.09_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'The speed of system disconnect or disablement varies based on the criticality of missions or business functions and the need to eliminate immediate or future remote access to systems.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1612, 'AC-17.10', 'Authenticate Remote Commands', 'Implement {{ insert: param, ac-17.10_odp.01 }} to authenticate {{ insert: param, ac-17.10_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Authenticating remote commands protects against unauthorized commands and the replay of authorized commands. The ability to authenticate remote commands is important for remote systems for which loss, malfunction, misdirection, or exploitation would have immediate or serious consequences, such as injury, death, property damage, loss of high value assets, failure of mission or business functions, or compromise of classified or controlled unclassified information. Authentication mechanisms for remote commands ensure that systems accept and execute commands in the order intended, execute only authorized commands, and reject unauthorized commands. Cryptographic mechanisms can be used, for example, to authenticate remote commands.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4390, 'SCVS-2.15', 'SPDX Licenses', 'Verify that components defined in SBOM have valid SPDX license ID''s or expressions (if applicable).', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V2: Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:01.948682', '2026-02-06 15:18:01.948682', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for SPDX Licenses based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4398, 'SCVS-2.16', 'Copyright Statements', 'Verify that components defined in SBOM have valid copyright statements.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V2: Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:03.935085', '2026-02-06 15:18:03.935085', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Copyright Statements based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

Restrict access to training data, encrypt it at rest and in transit, and validate its integrity to prevent tampering, theft, or data poisoning.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3275, '1.2.7', '**Verify that** all training dataset versions are uniquely identified, stored immutably, and auditable to support rollback and forensic analysis.', '**Verify that** all training dataset versions are uniquely identified, stored immutably, and auditable to support rollback and forensic analysis.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:43:27.719523', '2026-02-04 23:43:27.719523', NULL, '**C1.2 Training Data Security & Integrity**

Restrict access to training data, encrypt it at rest and in transit, and validate its integrity to prevent tampering, theft, or data poisoning.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4400, 'SCVS-2.18', 'File Hashes', 'Verify that components defined in SBOM have one or more file hashes (SHA-256, SHA-512, etc).', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V2: Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:04.429244', '2026-02-06 15:18:04.429244', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for File Hashes based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4401, 'SCVS-3.4', 'Build Integrity', 'Verify that application build pipeline prohibits alteration of build outside of the job performing the build.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:04.675692', '2026-02-06 15:18:04.675692', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Build Integrity based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4402, 'SCVS-3.5', 'Package Settings Integrity', 'Verify that application build pipeline prohibits alteration of package management settings.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:04.921401', '2026-02-06 15:18:04.921401', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Package Settings Integrity based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1615, 'AC-18.2', 'Monitoring Unauthorized Connections', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1616, 'AC-18.3', 'Disable Wireless Networking', 'Disable, when not intended for use, wireless networking capabilities embedded within system components prior to issuance and deployment.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Wireless networking capabilities that are embedded within system components represent a significant potential vulnerability that can be exploited by adversaries. Disabling wireless capabilities when not needed for essential organizational missions or functions can reduce susceptibility to threats by adversaries involving wireless technologies.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1617, 'AC-18.4', 'Restrict Configurations by Users', 'Identify and explicitly authorize users allowed to independently configure wireless networking capabilities.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Organizational authorizations to allow selected users to configure wireless networking capabilities are enforced, in part, by the access enforcement mechanisms employed within organizational systems.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1620, 'AC-19.1', 'Use of Writable and Portable Storage Devices', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1621, 'AC-19.2', 'Use of Personally Owned Portable Storage Devices', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1622, 'AC-19.3', 'Use of Portable Storage Devices with No Identifiable Owner', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1623, 'AC-19.4', 'Restrictions for Classified Information', 'Prohibit the use of unclassified mobile devices in facilities containing systems processing, storing, or transmitting classified information unless specifically permitted by the authorizing official; and Enforce the following restrictions on individuals permitted by the authorizing official to use unclassified mobile devices in facilities containing systems processing, storing, or transmitting classified information: Connection of unclassified mobile devices to classified systems is prohibited; Connection of unclassified mobile devices to unclassified systems requires approval from the authorizing official; Use of internal or external modems or wireless interfaces within the unclassified mobile devices is prohibited; and Unclassified mobile devices and the information stored on those devices are subject to random reviews and inspections by {{ insert: param, ac-19.04_odp.01 }} , and if classified information is found, the incident handling policy is followed.Restrict the connection of classified mobile devices to classified systems in accordance with {{ insert: param, ac-19.04_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'None.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1624, 'AC-19.5', 'Full Device or Container-based Encryption', 'Employ {{ insert: param, ac-19.05_odp.01 }} to protect the confidentiality and integrity of information on {{ insert: param, ac-19.05_odp.02 }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Container-based encryption provides a more fine-grained approach to data and information encryption on mobile devices, including encrypting selected data structures such as files, records, or fields.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1644, 'AT-2.3', 'Social Engineering and Mining', 'Provide literacy training on recognizing and reporting potential and actual instances of social engineering and social mining.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Awareness and Training', 'Social engineering is an attempt to trick an individual into revealing information or taking an action that can be used to breach, compromise, or otherwise adversely impact a system. Social engineering includes phishing, pretexting, impersonation, baiting, quid pro quo, thread-jacking, social media exploitation, and tailgating. Social mining is an attempt to gather information about the organization that may be used to support future attacks. Literacy training includes information on how to communicate the concerns of employees and management regarding potential and actual instances of social engineering and data mining through organizational channels based on established policies and procedures.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4403, 'SCVS-3.6', 'Code Execution Limits', 'Verify that application build pipeline prohibits the execution of arbitrary code outside of the context of a jobs build script.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:05.168681', '2026-02-06 15:18:05.168681', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Code Execution Limits based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4407, 'SCVS-1.7', 'Component Identification', 'Verify that components are uniquely identified in a consistent, machine-readable format.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V1: Inventory Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:06.411206', '2026-02-06 15:18:06.411206', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Component Identification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4409, 'SCVS-1.9', 'Component Function', 'Verify that the component function is known throughout inventory.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V1: Inventory Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:06.915715', '2026-02-06 15:18:06.915715', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Component Function based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3273, '1.2.5', '**Verify that** that automated detection techniques are applied to guard against unauthorized modifications or corruption of training data.', '**Verify that** that automated detection techniques are applied to guard against unauthorized modifications or corruption of training data.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:43:27.244976', '2026-02-04 23:43:27.244976', NULL, '**C1.2 Training Data Security & Integrity**

Restrict access to training data, encrypt it at rest and in transit, and validate its integrity to prevent tampering, theft, or data poisoning.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3274, '1.2.6', '**Verify that** obsolete training data is securely purged or anonymized.', '**Verify that** obsolete training data is securely purged or anonymized.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:43:27.483465', '2026-02-04 23:43:27.483465', NULL, '**C1.2 Training Data Security & Integrity**

Restrict access to training data, encrypt it at rest and in transit, and validate its integrity to prevent tampering, theft, or data poisoning.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3587, '10.2.2', '**Verify that** adversarial-example detection raises blocking alerts in production pipelines.', '**Verify that** adversarial-example detection raises blocking alerts in production pipelines.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:03.380602', '2026-02-04 23:49:03.380602', NULL, '**10.2 Adversarial-Example Hardening**

Increase resilience to manipulated inputs. Robust adversarial-training and benchmark scoring are the current best practice.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1626, 'AC-20.1', 'Limits on Authorized Use', 'Permit authorized individuals to use an external system to access the system or to process, store, or transmit organization-controlled information only after: Verification of the implementation of controls on the external system as specified in the organization’s security and privacy policies and security and privacy plans; or Retention of approved system connection or processing agreements with the organizational entity hosting the external system.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Limiting authorized use recognizes circumstances where individuals using external systems may need to access organizational systems. Organizations need assurance that the external systems contain the necessary controls so as not to compromise, damage, or otherwise harm organizational systems. Verification that the required controls have been implemented can be achieved by external, independent assessments, attestations, or other means, depending on the confidence level required by organizations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1627, 'AC-20.2', 'Portable Storage Devices — Restricted Use', 'Restrict the use of organization-controlled portable storage devices by authorized individuals on external systems using {{ insert: param, ac-20.02_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Limits on the use of organization-controlled portable storage devices in external systems include restrictions on how the devices may be used and under what conditions the devices may be used.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1628, 'AC-20.3', 'Non-organizationally Owned Systems — Restricted Use', 'Restrict the use of non-organizationally owned systems or system components to process, store, or transmit organizational information using {{ insert: param, ac-20.03_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Non-organizationally owned systems or system components include systems or system components owned by other organizations as well as personally owned devices. There are potential risks to using non-organizationally owned systems or components. In some cases, the risk is sufficiently high as to prohibit such use (see [AC-20 b.](#ac-20_smt.b) ). In other cases, the use of such systems or system components may be allowed but restricted in some way. Restrictions include requiring the implementation of approved controls prior to authorizing the connection of non-organizationally owned systems and components; limiting access to types of information, services, or applications; using virtualization techniques to limit processing and storage activities to servers or system components provisioned by the organization; and agreeing to the terms and conditions for usage. Organizations consult with the Office of the General Counsel regarding legal issues associated with using personally owned devices, including requirements for conducting forensic analyses during investigations after an incident.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1629, 'AC-20.4', 'Network Accessible Storage Devices — Prohibited Use', 'Prohibit the use of {{ insert: param, ac-20.04_odp }} in external systems.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Network-accessible storage devices in external systems include online storage devices in public, hybrid, or community cloud-based systems.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1630, 'AC-20.5', 'Portable Storage Devices — Prohibited Use', 'Prohibit the use of organization-controlled portable storage devices by authorized individuals on external systems.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Limits on the use of organization-controlled portable storage devices in external systems include a complete prohibition of the use of such devices. Prohibiting such use is enforced using technical methods and/or nontechnical (i.e., process-based) methods.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1632, 'AC-21.1', 'Automated Decision Support', 'Employ {{ insert: param, ac-21.01_odp }} to enforce information-sharing decisions by authorized users based on access authorizations of sharing partners and access restrictions on information to be shared.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Automated mechanisms are used to enforce information sharing decisions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1633, 'AC-21.2', 'Information Search and Retrieval', 'Implement information search and retrieval services that enforce {{ insert: param, ac-21.02_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Information search and retrieval services identify information system resources relevant to an information need.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3043, '0201.02c1Var1', 'Media Encryption', 'Portable media containing sensitive information shall be encrypted.', 'HITRUST-Aligned (Representative)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Portable Media Security', NULL, '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', 'HITRUST', '', 701, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3044, '0301.03d1Var1', 'Mobile Device Management', 'Mobile devices accessing corporate data shall be managed via MDM.', 'HITRUST-Aligned (Representative)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Mobile Device Security', NULL, '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', 'HITRUST', '', 701, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3045, '0401.04e1Var1', 'Wireless Encryption', 'Wireless networks shall use strong encryption (e.g., WPA2/3 Enterprise).', 'HITRUST-Aligned (Representative)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Wireless Security', NULL, '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', 'HITRUST', '', 701, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3046, '0501.05f1Var1', 'Configuration Standards', 'Baseline configurations shall be established and maintained for all system components.', 'HITRUST-Aligned (Representative)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Configuration Management', NULL, '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', 'HITRUST', '', 701, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3047, '0601.06g1Var1', 'Vulnerability Scanning', 'Vulnerability scans shall be performed at regular intervals.', 'HITRUST-Aligned (Representative)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Vulnerability Management', NULL, '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', 'HITRUST', '', 701, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3048, '0602.06g2Var1', 'Patch Management', 'Security patches shall be applied within established timeframes based on severity.', 'HITRUST-Aligned (Representative)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Vulnerability Management', NULL, '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', 'HITRUST', '', 701, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3049, '0701.07h1Var1', 'Network Segmentation', 'Network segmentation shall be used to isolate sensitive systems and data.', 'HITRUST-Aligned (Representative)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Network Protection', NULL, '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', 'HITRUST', '', 701, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3050, '0702.07h2Var1', 'Firewall Configuration', 'Firewall rules shall be reviewed regularly and follow the principle of least privilege.', 'HITRUST-Aligned (Representative)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Network Protection', NULL, '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', 'HITRUST', '', 701, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3051, '0801.08i1Var1', 'Encryption in Transit', 'Sensitive data transmitted over public networks shall be encrypted.', 'HITRUST-Aligned (Representative)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Transmission Protection', NULL, '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', '2026-01-31 15:44:03.689418', 'HITRUST', '', 701, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3588, '10.2.4', '**Verify that** certified‐robustness proofs or interval-bound certificates cover at least the top critical classes.', '**Verify that** certified‐robustness proofs or interval-bound certificates cover at least the top critical classes.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:03.603027', '2026-02-04 23:49:03.603027', NULL, '**10.2 Adversarial-Example Hardening**

Increase resilience to manipulated inputs. Robust adversarial-training and benchmark scoring are the current best practice.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4070, 'SCVS-2.3', 'Unique Identifier', 'Verify that each SBOM has a unique identifier.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V2: Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:40:51.731265', '2026-02-06 13:40:51.731265', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for License Compliance based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4411, 'SCVS-2.4', 'SBOM Signing', 'Verify that SBOM has been signed by publisher, supplier, or certifying authority.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V2: Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:08.158247', '2026-02-06 15:18:08.158247', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for SBOM Signing based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1635, 'AC-23', 'Data Mining Protection', 'Employ {{ insert: param, ac-23_odp.01 }} for {{ insert: param, ac-23_odp.02 }} to detect and protect against unauthorized data mining.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Data mining is an analytical process that attempts to find correlations or patterns in large data sets for the purpose of data or knowledge discovery. Data storage objects include database records and database fields. Sensitive information can be extracted from data mining operations. When information is personally identifiable information, it may lead to unanticipated revelations about individuals and give rise to privacy risks. Prior to performing data mining activities, organizations determine whether such activities are authorized. Organizations may be subject to applicable laws, executive orders, directives, regulations, or policies that address data mining requirements. Organizational personnel consult with the senior agency official for privacy and legal counsel regarding such requirements.

Data mining prevention and detection techniques include limiting the number and frequency of database queries to increase the work factor needed to determine the contents of databases, limiting types of responses provided to database queries, applying differential privacy techniques or homomorphic encryption, and notifying personnel when atypical database queries or accesses occur. Data mining protection focuses on protecting information from data mining while such information resides in organizational data stores. In contrast, [AU-13](#au-13) focuses on monitoring for organizational information that may have been mined or otherwise obtained from data stores and is available as open-source information residing on external sites, such as social networking or social media websites.

[EO 13587](#0af071a6-cf8e-48ee-8c82-fe91efa20f94) requires the establishment of an insider threat program for deterring, detecting, and mitigating insider threats, including the safeguarding of sensitive information from exploitation, compromise, or other unauthorized disclosure. Data mining protection requires organizations to identify appropriate techniques to prevent and detect unnecessary or unauthorized data mining. Data mining can be used by an insider to collect organizational information for the purpose of exfiltration.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1636, 'AC-24', 'Access Control Decisions', '{{ insert: param, ac-24_odp.01 }} to ensure {{ insert: param, ac-24_odp.02 }} are applied to each access request prior to access enforcement.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'Access control decisions (also known as authorization decisions) occur when authorization information is applied to specific accesses. In contrast, access enforcement occurs when systems enforce access control decisions. While it is common to have access control decisions and access enforcement implemented by the same entity, it is not required, and it is not always an optimal implementation choice. For some architectures and distributed systems, different entities may make access control decisions and enforce access.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1638, 'AC-24.2', 'No User or Process Identity', 'Enforce access control decisions based on {{ insert: param, ac-24.2_prm_1 }} that do not include the identity of the user or process acting on behalf of the user.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Access Control', 'In certain situations, it is important that access control decisions can be made without information regarding the identity of the users issuing the requests. These are generally instances where preserving individual privacy is of paramount importance. In other situations, user identification information is simply not needed for access control decisions, and especially in the case of distributed systems, transmitting such information with the needed degree of assurance may be very expensive or difficult to accomplish. MAC, RBAC, ABAC, and label-based control policies, for example, might not include user identity as an attribute.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1645, 'AT-2.4', 'Suspicious Communications and Anomalous System Behavior', 'Provide literacy training on recognizing suspicious communications and anomalous behavior in organizational systems using {{ insert: param, at-02.04_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Awareness and Training', 'A well-trained workforce provides another organizational control that can be employed as part of a defense-in-depth strategy to protect against malicious code coming into organizations via email or the web applications. Personnel are trained to look for indications of potentially suspicious email (e.g., receiving an unexpected email, receiving an email containing strange or poor grammar, or receiving an email from an unfamiliar sender that appears to be from a known sponsor or contractor). Personnel are also trained on how to respond to suspicious email or web communications. For this process to work effectively, personnel are trained and made aware of what constitutes suspicious communications. Training personnel on how to recognize anomalous behaviors in systems can provide organizations with early warning for the presence of malicious code. Recognition of anomalous behavior by organizational personnel can supplement malicious code detection and protection tools and systems employed by organizations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1795, 'CM-7.3', 'Registration Compliance', 'Ensure compliance with {{ insert: param, cm-07.03_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Configuration Management', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:06.23121', '2026-01-09 09:38:06.23121', 'Configuration Management', 'Organizations use the registration process to manage, track, and provide oversight for systems and implemented functions, ports, protocols, and services.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4412, 'SCVS-2.5', 'Signature Verification', 'Verify that SBOM signature verification exists.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V2: Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:08.408198', '2026-02-06 15:18:08.408198', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Signature Verification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4071, 'SCVS-3.2', 'Build Documentation', 'Verify that documentation exists on how the application is built and instructions for repeating the build.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:40:51.959757', '2026-02-06 13:40:51.959757', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Component Vetting based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4413, 'SCVS-3.8', 'Network Settings Integrity', 'Verify that application build pipeline prohibits alteration of DNS and network settings during build.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:09.641208', '2026-02-06 15:18:09.641208', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Network Settings Integrity based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3277, '11.4.3', '**Verify that** policy-as-code gates block redeployment of models to new domains without DPIA review.', '**Verify that** policy-as-code gates block redeployment of models to new domains without DPIA review.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:43:28.199039', '2026-02-04 23:43:28.199039', NULL, '**11.4 Purpose-Limitation & Scope-Creep Protection**

', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3278, '1.3.2', '**Verify that** labeling interfaces and platforms enforce strong access controls, maintain tamper-evident audit logs of all labeling activities, and protect against unauthorized modifications.', '**Verify that** labeling interfaces and platforms enforce strong access controls, maintain tamper-evident audit logs of all labeling activities, and protect against unauthorized modifications.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:43:28.437547', '2026-02-04 23:43:28.437547', NULL, '**C1.3 Training Data Labeling Quality, Integrity, and Security**

Protect labels and require technical review for critical data.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4415, 'SCVS-3.10', 'Authentication Enforcement', 'Verify that application build pipeline enforces authentication and defaults to deny.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:10.138249', '2026-02-06 15:18:10.138249', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Authentication Enforcement based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1641, 'AT-2', 'Literacy Training and Awareness', 'The organization provides basic security awareness training to information system users (including managers, senior executives, and contractors)...', 'NIST 800-53', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-02-13 12:42:38.908', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'AT', 'Organizations provide basic and advanced levels of literacy training to system users, including measures to test the knowledge level of users. Organizations determine the content of literacy training and awareness based on specific organizational requirements, the systems to which personnel have authorized access, and work environments (e.g., telework). The content includes an understanding of the need for security and privacy as well as actions by users to maintain security and personal privacy and to respond to suspected incidents. The content addresses the need for operations security and the handling of personally identifiable information.

Awareness techniques include displaying posters, offering supplies inscribed with security and privacy reminders, displaying logon screen messages, generating email advisories or notices from organizational officials, and conducting awareness events. Literacy training after the initial training described in [AT-2a.1](#at-2_smt.a.1) is conducted at a minimum frequency consistent with applicable laws, directives, regulations, and policies. Subsequent literacy training may be satisfied by one or more short ad hoc sessions and include topical information on recent attack schemes, changes to organizational security and privacy policies, revised security and privacy expectations, or a subset of topics from the initial training. Updating literacy training and awareness content on a regular basis helps to ensure that the content remains relevant. Events that may precipitate an update to literacy training and awareness content include, but are not limited to, assessment or audit findings, security incidents or breaches, or changes in applicable laws, executive orders, directives, regulations, policies, standards, and guidelines.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1642, 'AT-2.1', 'Practical Exercises', 'Provide practical exercises in literacy training that simulate events and incidents.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.706627', 'Awareness and Training', 'Practical exercises include no-notice social engineering attempts to collect information, gain unauthorized access, or simulate the adverse impact of opening malicious email attachments or invoking, via spear phishing attacks, malicious web links.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1643, 'AT-2.2', 'Insider Threat', 'Provide literacy training on recognizing and reporting potential indicators of insider threat.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Awareness and Training', 'Potential indicators and possible precursors of insider threat can include behaviors such as inordinate, long-term job dissatisfaction; attempts to gain access to information not required for job performance; unexplained access to financial resources; bullying or harassment of fellow employees; workplace violence; and other serious violations of policies, procedures, directives, regulations, rules, or practices. Literacy training includes how to communicate the concerns of employees and management regarding potential indicators of insider threat through channels established by the organization and in accordance with established policies and procedures. Organizations may consider tailoring insider threat awareness topics to the role. For example, training for managers may be focused on changes in the behavior of team members, while training for employees may be focused on more general observations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1676, 'AU-6.1', 'Automated Process Integration', 'Integrate audit record review, analysis, and reporting processes using {{ insert: param, au-06.01_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Audit and Accountability', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Audit and Accountability', 'Organizational processes that benefit from integrated audit record review, analysis, and reporting include incident response, continuous monitoring, contingency planning, investigation and response to suspicious activities, and Inspector General audits.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4417, 'SCVS-3.12', 'Separation of Concerns', 'Verify that application build pipeline requires separation of concerns for the modification of system settings.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:10.633972', '2026-02-06 15:18:10.633972', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Separation of Concerns based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4418, 'SCVS-3.13', 'System Audit Log', 'Verify that application build pipeline maintains a verifiable audit log of all system changes.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:10.885376', '2026-02-06 15:18:10.885376', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for System Audit Log based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3279, '1.3.3', '**Verify that** sensitive information in labels is redacted, anonymized, or encrypted at the data field level at rest and in transit.', '**Verify that** sensitive information in labels is redacted, anonymized, or encrypted at the data field level at rest and in transit.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:43:28.678047', '2026-02-04 23:43:28.678047', NULL, '**C1.3 Training Data Labeling Quality, Integrity, and Security**

Protect labels and require technical review for critical data.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4421, 'SCVS-3.16', 'Tool Analysis', 'Verify that compilers, version control clients, development utilities, and software development kits are analyzed and monitored for tampering, trojans, or malicious code.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:11.629812', '2026-02-06 15:18:11.629812', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Tool Analysis based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4423, 'SCVS-3.18', 'Component Checksums', 'Verify that checksums of all first-party and third-party components are documented for every build.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:12.119814', '2026-02-06 15:18:12.119814', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Component Checksums based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1647, 'AT-2.6', 'Cyber Threat Environment', 'Provide literacy training on the cyber threat environment; and Reflect current cyber threat information in system operations.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Awareness and Training', 'Since threats continue to change over time, threat literacy training by the organization is dynamic. Moreover, threat literacy training is not performed in isolation from the system operations that support organizational mission and business functions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1649, 'AT-3.1', 'Environmental Controls', 'Provide {{ insert: param, at-03.01_odp.01 }} with initial and {{ insert: param, at-03.01_odp.02 }} training in the employment and operation of environmental controls.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Awareness and Training', 'Environmental controls include fire suppression and detection devices or systems, sprinkler systems, handheld fire extinguishers, fixed fire hoses, smoke detectors, temperature or humidity, heating, ventilation, air conditioning, and power within the facility.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1650, 'AT-3.2', 'Physical Security Controls', 'Provide {{ insert: param, at-03.02_odp.01 }} with initial and {{ insert: param, at-03.02_odp.02 }} training in the employment and operation of physical security controls.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Awareness and Training', 'Physical security controls include physical access control devices, physical intrusion and detection alarms, operating procedures for facility security guards, and monitoring or surveillance equipment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1651, 'AT-3.3', 'Practical Exercises', 'Provide practical exercises in security and privacy training that reinforce training objectives.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Awareness and Training', 'Practical exercises for security include training for software developers that addresses simulated attacks that exploit common software vulnerabilities or spear or whale phishing attacks targeted at senior leaders or executives. Practical exercises for privacy include modules with quizzes on identifying and processing personally identifiable information in various scenarios or scenarios on conducting privacy impact assessments.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1652, 'AT-3.4', 'Suspicious Communications and Anomalous System Behavior', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Awareness and Training', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1653, 'AT-3.5', 'Processing Personally Identifiable Information', 'Provide {{ insert: param, at-03.05_odp.01 }} with initial and {{ insert: param, at-03.05_odp.02 }} training in the employment and operation of personally identifiable information processing and transparency controls.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Awareness and Training', 'Personally identifiable information processing and transparency controls include the organization’s authority to process personally identifiable information and personally identifiable information processing purposes. Role-based training for federal agencies addresses the types of information that may constitute personally identifiable information and the risks, considerations, and obligations associated with its processing. Such training also considers the authority to process personally identifiable information documented in privacy policies and notices, system of records notices, computer matching agreements and notices, privacy impact assessments, [PRIVACT](#18e71fec-c6fd-475a-925a-5d8495cf8455) statements, contracts, information sharing agreements, memoranda of understanding, and/or other documentation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1654, 'AT-4', 'Training Records', 'Document and monitor information security and privacy training activities, including security and privacy awareness training and specific role-based security and privacy training; and Retain individual training records for {{ insert: param, at-04_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Awareness and Training', 'Documentation for specialized training may be maintained by individual supervisors at the discretion of the organization. The National Archives and Records Administration provides guidance on records retention for federal agencies.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1655, 'AT-5', 'Contacts with Security Groups and Associations', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Awareness and Training', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Awareness and Training', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1677, 'AU-6.2', 'Automated Security Alerts', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Audit and Accountability', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Audit and Accountability', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2223, 'RA-5.6', 'Automated Trend Analyses', 'Compare the results of multiple vulnerability scans using {{ insert: param, ra-05.06_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Risk Assessment', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:07.252102', '2026-01-09 09:38:07.252102', 'Risk Assessment', 'Using automated mechanisms to analyze multiple vulnerability scans over time can help determine trends in system vulnerabilities and identify patterns of attack.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4424, 'SCVS-3.19', 'Checksum Delivery', 'Verify that checksums of all components are accessible and delivered out-of-band whenever those components are packaged or distributed.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:12.370832', '2026-02-06 15:18:12.370832', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Checksum Delivery based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4427, 'SCVS-4.4', 'MFA Publishing Support', 'Verify that package repository supports multi-factor authentication component publishing.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V4: Package Management Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:13.354282', '2026-02-06 15:18:13.354282', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for MFA Publishing Support based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4431, 'SCVS-4.8', 'Publisher Notification', 'Verify that package repository notifies publishers of security issues.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V4: Package Management Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:14.343962', '2026-02-06 15:18:14.343962', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Publisher Notification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4434, 'SCVS-4.11', 'Update Auditability', 'Verify that package repository provides auditability when components are updated.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V4: Package Management Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:15.087842', '2026-02-06 15:18:15.087842', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Update Auditability based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4437, 'SCVS-4.14', 'Local Integrity Verification', 'Verify that package manager verifies the integrity of packages when they are retrieved from file system.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V4: Package Management Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:15.832785', '2026-02-06 15:18:15.832785', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Local Integrity Verification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4443, 'SCVS-5.4', 'Vulnerability Identification', 'Verify that an automated process of identifying all publicly disclosed vulnerabilities in third-party and open source components is used.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V5: Component Analysis Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:17.324566', '2026-02-06 15:18:17.324566', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Vulnerability Identification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4445, 'SCVS-5.6', 'Version Identification', 'Verify that an automated process of identifying non-specified component versions is used.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V5: Component Analysis Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:17.816412', '2026-02-06 15:18:17.816412', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Version Identification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4449, 'SCVS-5.10', 'Function Identification', 'Verify that an automated process of identifying component function is used.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V5: Component Analysis Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:18.813432', '2026-02-06 15:18:18.813432', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Function Identification based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1659, 'AU-2.1', 'Compilation of Audit Records from Multiple Sources', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Audit and Accountability', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Audit and Accountability', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1660, 'AU-2.2', 'Selection of Audit Events by Component', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Audit and Accountability', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Audit and Accountability', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1661, 'AU-2.3', 'Reviews and Updates', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Audit and Accountability', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Audit and Accountability', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1662, 'AU-2.4', 'Privileged Functions', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Audit and Accountability', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Audit and Accountability', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1664, 'AU-3.1', 'Additional Audit Information', 'Generate audit records containing the following additional information: {{ insert: param, au-03.01_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Audit and Accountability', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Audit and Accountability', 'The ability to add information generated in audit records is dependent on system functionality to configure the audit record content. Organizations may consider additional information in audit records including, but not limited to, access control or flow control rules invoked and individual identities of group account users. Organizations may also consider limiting additional audit record information to only information that is explicitly needed for audit requirements. This facilitates the use of audit trails and audit logs by not including information in audit records that could potentially be misleading, make it more difficult to locate information of interest, or increase the risk to individuals'' privacy.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1665, 'AU-3.2', 'Centralized Management of Planned Audit Record Content', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Audit and Accountability', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Audit and Accountability', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1666, 'AU-3.3', 'Limit Personally Identifiable Information Elements', 'Limit personally identifiable information contained in audit records to the following elements identified in the privacy risk assessment: {{ insert: param, au-03.03_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Audit and Accountability', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Audit and Accountability', 'Limiting personally identifiable information in audit records when such information is not needed for operational purposes helps reduce the level of privacy risk created by a system.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1667, 'AU-4', 'Audit Log Storage Capacity', 'Allocate audit log storage capacity to accommodate {{ insert: param, au-04_odp }}.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Audit and Accountability', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.83833', 'Audit and Accountability', 'Organizations consider the types of audit logging to be performed and the audit log processing requirements when allocating audit log storage capacity. Allocating sufficient audit log storage capacity reduces the likelihood of such capacity being exceeded and resulting in the potential loss or reduction of audit logging capability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2224, 'RA-5.7', 'Automated Detection and Notification of Unauthorized Components', '', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Risk Assessment', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:07.252102', '2026-01-09 09:38:07.252102', 'Risk Assessment', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4453, 'SCVS-6.5', 'Unique Modification ID', 'Verify that modified components are uniquely identified and distinct from origin component.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V6: Pedigree and Provenance Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:19.818929', '2026-02-06 15:18:19.818929', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Unique Modification ID based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4414, 'SCVS-3.9', 'Trust Store Integrity', 'Verify that application build pipeline prohibits alteration of certificate trust stores.', 'SCVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'V3: Build Environment Requirements', NULL, '2026-02-06 15:18:09.88915', '2026-02-06 15:18:09.88915', NULL, 'Implementation guidance for Trust Store Integrity based on OWASP Software Component Verification Standard v1.0.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
