	(3423, '6.3.5', '**Verify that** expired dependencies trigger automated PRs to update or fork pinned versions.', '**Verify that** expired dependencies trigger automated PRs to update or fork pinned versions.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:48:26.736634', '2026-02-04 23:48:26.736634', NULL, '**C6.3 Dependency Pinning & Verification**

Pin every dependency to immutable digests and reproduce builds to guarantee identical, tamper‑free artifacts.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3424, '6.4.1', '**Verify that** model weights, datasets, and containers are downloaded only from approved domains or internal registries.', '**Verify that** model weights, datasets, and containers are downloaded only from approved domains or internal registries.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:48:26.957575', '2026-02-04 23:48:26.957575', NULL, '**C6.4 Trusted Source Enforcement**

Allow artifact downloads only from cryptographically verified, organization‑approved sources and block everything else.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4292, '9.2.1', 'Verify that connections to and from the server use trusted TLS certificates. Where internally generated or self-signed certificates are used, the server must be configured to only trust specific internal CAs and specific self-signed certificates. All othe', 'Verify that connections to and from the server use trusted TLS certificates. Where internally generated or self-signed certificates are used, the server must be configured to only trust specific internal CAs and specific self-signed certificates. All others should be rejected.', 'ASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'ASVS, L1, L2', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:06.717524', '2026-02-06 13:43:06.717524', NULL, '**V9.2 Server Communication Security**

Server communications are more than just HTTP. Secure connections to and from other systems, such as monitoring systems, management tools, remote access and ssh, middleware, database, mainframes, partner or external source systems &mdash; must be in place. All of these must be encrypted to prevent "hard on the outside, trivially easy to intercept on the inside".', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4491, '5.1', 'Policies for information security', 'Information security policy and topic-specific policies should be defined, approved by management, published, communicated to and acknowledged by relevant personnel and relevant interested parties.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2746, '3.4.6', 'Verify that the web application uses the frame-ancestors directive of the Content-Security-Policy header field for every HTTP response to ensure that it cannot be embedded by default and that embedding of specific resources is allowed only when neces', 'Verify that the web application uses the frame-ancestors directive of the Content-Security-Policy header field for every HTTP response to ensure that it cannot be embedded by default and that embedding of specific resources is allowed only when necessary. Note that the X-Frame-Options header field, although supported by browsers, is obsolete and may not be relied upon.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:36.768', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.4: Browser Security Mechanism Headers', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2747, '3.4.7', 'Verify that the Content-Security-Policy header field specifies a location to report violations.', 'Verify that the Content-Security-Policy header field specifies a location to report violations.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:36.768', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.4: Browser Security Mechanism Headers', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4492, '5.2', 'Information security roles and responsibilities', 'Information security roles and responsibilities should be defined and allocated according to the organization needs.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2748, '3.4.8', 'Verify that all HTTP responses that initiate a document rendering (such as responses with Content-Type text/html), include the Cross‑Origin‑Opener‑Policy header field with the same-origin directive or the same-origin-allow-popups directive as require', 'Verify that all HTTP responses that initiate a document rendering (such as responses with Content-Type text/html), include the Cross‑Origin‑Opener‑Policy header field with the same-origin directive or the same-origin-allow-popups directive as required. This prevents attacks that abuse shared access to Window objects, such as tabnabbing and frame counting.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:36.768', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.4: Browser Security Mechanism Headers', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4493, '5.3', 'Segregation of duties', 'Conflicting duties and areas of responsibility should be segregated to reduce opportunities for unauthorized or unintentional modification or misuse of the organization''s assets.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4494, '5.4', 'Management responsibilities', 'Management should require all personnel to apply information security in accordance with the established information security policy, topic-specific policies and procedures of the organization.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4495, '5.5', 'Contact with authorities', 'The organization should establish and maintain contact with appropriate authorities.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4496, '5.6', 'Contact with special interest groups', 'The organization should establish and maintain contact with appropriate special interest groups or other specialist security forums and professional associations.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4497, '5.7', 'Threat intelligence', 'Information relating to information security threats should be collected and analyzed to produce threat intelligence.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4498, '5.8', 'Information security in project management', 'Information security should be integrated into project management.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4499, '5.9', 'Inventory of information and other associated assets', 'An inventory of information and other associated assets, including owners, should be developed and maintained.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4500, '5.10', 'Acceptable use of information and other associated assets', 'Rules for the acceptable use and procedures for handling information and other associated assets should be defined, documented and implemented.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4501, '5.15', 'Access control', 'Rules to control physical and logical access to information and other associated assets should be established and implemented based on business and information security requirements.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4502, '5.16', 'Identity management', 'The full lifecycle of digital identities should be managed.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4503, '5.17', 'Authentication information', 'Allocation and management of authentication information should be controlled by a management process, including advising personnel on the appropriate handling of authentication information.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4504, '5.18', 'Access rights', 'Access rights to information and other associated assets should be provisioned, reviewed, modified and removed in accordance with the organization''s topic-specific policy on and rules for access control.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4505, '6.1', 'Screening', 'Background verification checks on all candidates to become personnel should be carried out prior to joining the organization.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'People Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4506, '6.2', 'Terms and conditions of employment', 'The contractual agreements with personnel should state their and the organization''s responsibilities for information security.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'People Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4507, '6.3', 'Information security awareness, education and training', 'Personnel of the organization and relevant interested parties should receive appropriate information security awareness, education and training.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'People Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2752, '3.5.4', 'Verify that separate applications are hosted on different hostnames to leverage the restrictions provided by same-origin policy, including how documents or scripts loaded by one origin can interact with resources from another origin and hostname-base', 'Verify that separate applications are hosted on different hostnames to leverage the restrictions provided by same-origin policy, including how documents or scripts loaded by one origin can interact with resources from another origin and hostname-based restrictions on cookies.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.032', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.5: Browser Origin Separation', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4508, '6.4', 'Disciplinary process', 'A disciplinary process should be formalized and communicated to take action against personnel and other relevant interested parties who have committed an information security policy violation.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'People Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4509, '7.1', 'Physical security perimeters', 'Security perimeters should be defined and used to protect areas that contain information and other associated assets.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Physical Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4510, '7.2', 'Physical entry', 'Secure areas should be protected by appropriate entry controls and points of access.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Physical Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4511, '7.3', 'Securing offices, rooms and facilities', 'Physical security for offices, rooms and facilities should be designed and implemented.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Physical Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4512, '7.10', 'Storage media', 'Storage media should be managed through their life cycle of acquisition, use, transportation and disposal in accordance with the organization''s topic-specific policy on and rules for storage media.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Physical Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4513, '8.1', 'User endpoint devices', 'Information held on, processed by or accessible via user endpoint devices should be protected.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4514, '8.2', 'Privileged access rights', 'The allocation and use of privileged access rights should be restricted and managed.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4515, '8.3', 'Information access restriction', 'Access to information and other associated assets should be restricted in accordance with the established topic-specific policy on access control.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4516, '8.4', 'Access to source code', 'Read and write access to source code, development tools and software libraries should be appropriately managed.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4517, '8.5', 'Secure authentication', 'Secure authentication technologies and procedures should be implemented based on information access restrictions and the topic-specific policy on access control.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4518, '8.8', 'Management of technical vulnerabilities', 'Information about technical vulnerabilities of information systems in use should be obtained, the organization''s exposure to such vulnerabilities should be evaluated and appropriate measures should be taken.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2753, '3.5.5', 'Verify that messages received by the postMessage interface are discarded if the origin of the message is not trusted, or if the syntax of the message is invalid.', 'Verify that messages received by the postMessage interface are discarded if the origin of the message is not trusted, or if the syntax of the message is invalid.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.032', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.5: Browser Origin Separation', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2754, '3.5.6', 'Verify that JSONP functionality is not enabled anywhere across the application to avoid Cross-Site Script Inclusion (XSSI) attacks.', 'Verify that JSONP functionality is not enabled anywhere across the application to avoid Cross-Site Script Inclusion (XSSI) attacks.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.032', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.5: Browser Origin Separation', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2756, '3.5.8', 'Verify that authenticated resources (such as images, videos, scripts, and other documents) can be loaded or embedded on behalf of the user only when intended. This can be accomplished by strict validation of the Sec-Fetch-* HTTP request header fields', 'Verify that authenticated resources (such as images, videos, scripts, and other documents) can be loaded or embedded on behalf of the user only when intended. This can be accomplished by strict validation of the Sec-Fetch-* HTTP request header fields to ensure that the request did not originate from an inappropriate cross-origin call, or by setting a restrictive Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy HTTP response header field to instruct the browser to block returned content.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.032', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.5: Browser Origin Separation', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2755, '3.5.7', 'Verify that data requiring authorization is not included in script resource responses, like JavaScript files, to prevent Cross-Site Script Inclusion (XSSI) attacks.', 'Verify that data requiring authorization is not included in script resource responses, like JavaScript files, to prevent Cross-Site Script Inclusion (XSSI) attacks.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.032', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.5: Browser Origin Separation', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2759, '3.7.2', 'Verify that the application will only automatically redirect the user to a different hostname or domain (which is not controlled by the application) where the destination appears on an allowlist.', 'Verify that the application will only automatically redirect the user to a different hostname or domain (which is not controlled by the application) where the destination appears on an allowlist.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.032', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.7: Other Browser Security Considerations', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2760, '3.7.3', 'Verify that the application shows a notification when the user is being redirected to a URL outside of the application''s control, with an option to cancel the navigation.', 'Verify that the application shows a notification when the user is being redirected to a URL outside of the application''s control, with an option to cancel the navigation.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.032', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.7: Other Browser Security Considerations', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3630, '11.4.2', '**Verify that** runtime monitors detect queries inconsistent with declared purpose and trigger soft refusal.', '**Verify that** runtime monitors detect queries inconsistent with declared purpose and trigger soft refusal.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:12.910692', '2026-02-04 23:49:12.910692', NULL, '**11.4 Purpose-Limitation & Scope-Creep Protection**

', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3631, '11.5.1', '**Verify that** a Consent-Management Platform (CMP) records opt-in status, purpose, and retention period per data-subject.', '**Verify that** a Consent-Management Platform (CMP) records opt-in status, purpose, and retention period per data-subject.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:13.129702', '2026-02-04 23:49:13.129702', NULL, '**11.5 Consent Management & Lawful-Basis Tracking**

', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4293, '9.2.2', 'Verify that encrypted communications such as TLS is used for all inbound and outbound connections, including for management ports, monitoring, authentication, API, or web service calls, database, cloud, serverless, mainframe, external, and partner connect', 'Verify that encrypted communications such as TLS is used for all inbound and outbound connections, including for management ports, monitoring, authentication, API, or web service calls, database, cloud, serverless, mainframe, external, and partner connections. The server must not fall back to insecure or unencrypted protocols.', 'ASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'ASVS, L1, L2', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:06.943515', '2026-02-06 13:43:06.943515', NULL, '**V9.2 Server Communication Security**

Server communications are more than just HTTP. Secure connections to and from other systems, such as monitoring systems, management tools, remote access and ssh, middleware, database, mainframes, partner or external source systems &mdash; must be in place. All of these must be encrypted to prevent "hard on the outside, trivially easy to intercept on the inside".', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4294, '9.2.3', 'Verify that all encrypted connections to external systems that involve sensitive information or functions are authenticated.', 'Verify that all encrypted connections to external systems that involve sensitive information or functions are authenticated.', 'ASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'ASVS, L1, L2', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:07.172156', '2026-02-06 13:43:07.172156', NULL, '**V9.2 Server Communication Security**

Server communications are more than just HTTP. Secure connections to and from other systems, such as monitoring systems, management tools, remote access and ssh, middleware, database, mainframes, partner or external source systems &mdash; must be in place. All of these must be encrypted to prevent "hard on the outside, trivially easy to intercept on the inside".', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4519, '8.9', 'Configuration management', 'Configurations, including security configurations, of hardware, software, services and networks should be established, documented, implemented, monitored and reviewed.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2770, '4.2.3', 'Verify that the application does not send nor accept HTTP/2 or HTTP/3 messages with connection-specific header fields such as Transfer-Encoding to prevent response splitting and header injection attacks.', 'Verify that the application does not send nor accept HTTP/2 or HTTP/3 messages with connection-specific header fields such as Transfer-Encoding to prevent response splitting and header injection attacks.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V4: API and Web Service', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.292', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V4.2: HTTP Message Structure Validation', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4520, '8.10', 'Information deletion', 'Information stored in information systems, devices or on any other storage media should be deleted when no longer required.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4521, '8.11', 'Data masking', 'Data masking should be used in accordance with the organization''s topic-specific policy on access control and other related topic-specific policies, and business requirements, taking into consideration applicable legislation.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological Controls', NULL, '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', '2026-02-14 06:48:34.84279', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

Server communications are more than just HTTP. Secure connections to and from other systems, such as monitoring systems, management tools, remote access and ssh, middleware, database, mainframes, partner or external source systems &mdash; must be in place. All of these must be encrypted to prevent "hard on the outside, trivially easy to intercept on the inside".', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4296, '13.2.2', 'Verify that JSON schema validation is in place and verified before accepting input.', 'Verify that JSON schema validation is in place and verified before accepting input.', 'ASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'ASVS, L1, L2, L3, CWE-20', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:07.628019', '2026-02-06 13:43:07.628019', NULL, '**V13.2 RESTful Web Service**

JSON schema validation is in a draft stage of standardization (see references). When considering using JSON schema validation, which is best practice for RESTful web services, consider using these additional data validation strategies in combination with JSON schema validation:

* Parsing validation of the JSON object, such as if there are missing or extra elements.
* Validation of the JSON object values using standard input validation methods, such as data type, data format, length, etc.
* and formal JSON schema validation.

Once the JSON schema validation standard is formalized, ASVS will update its advice in this area. Carefully monitor any JSON schema validation libraries in use, as they will need to be updated regularly until the standard is formalized and bugs are ironed out of reference implementations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3425, '6.4.2', '**Verify that** Sigstore/Cosign signatures validate publisher identity before artifacts are cached locally.', '**Verify that** Sigstore/Cosign signatures validate publisher identity before artifacts are cached locally.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:48:27.179556', '2026-02-04 23:48:27.179556', NULL, '**C6.4 Trusted Source Enforcement**

Allow artifact downloads only from cryptographically verified, organization‑approved sources and block everything else.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3426, '6.4.3', '**Verify that** egress proxies block unauthenticated artifact downloads to enforce trusted‑source policy.', '**Verify that** egress proxies block unauthenticated artifact downloads to enforce trusted‑source policy.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:48:27.400579', '2026-02-04 23:48:27.400579', NULL, '**C6.4 Trusted Source Enforcement**

Allow artifact downloads only from cryptographically verified, organization‑approved sources and block everything else.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3427, '6.4.4', '**Verify that** repository allow‑lists are reviewed quarterly with evidence of business justification for each entry.', '**Verify that** repository allow‑lists are reviewed quarterly with evidence of business justification for each entry.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:48:27.620157', '2026-02-04 23:48:27.620157', NULL, '**C6.4 Trusted Source Enforcement**

Allow artifact downloads only from cryptographically verified, organization‑approved sources and block everything else.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(490, 'GV.OC-04', 'Organizational Context', 'Critical objectives, capabilities, and services that the organization provides and those upon which it depends are understood and prioritized.', 'NIST CSF 2.0', 'Unassigned', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Govern', NULL, '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', 'Organizational Context', 'Ex1: Establish criteria for determining the criticality of capabilities and services as viewed by internal and external stakeholders
Ex2: Determine (e.g., from a business impact analysis) assets and business operations that are vital to achieving mission objectives and the potential impact of a loss (or partial loss) of such operations
Ex3: Establish and communicate resilience objectives (e.g., recovery time objectives) for delivering critical capabilities and services in various operating states (e.g., under attack, during recovery, normal operation)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(499, 'GV.RR-01', 'Roles, Responsibilities, and Authorities', 'Organizational cybersecurity roles and responsibilities are established and communicated.', 'NIST CSF 2.0', 'Unassigned', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Govern', NULL, '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', 'Roles, Responsibilities, and Authorities', 'Ex1: Leaders (e.g., directors) agree on their roles and responsibilities in developing, implementing, and assessing the organization''s cybersecurity strategy
Ex2: Share leaders'' expectations regarding a secure and ethical culture, especially when current events present the opportunity to highlight positive or negative examples of cybersecurity risk management
Ex3: Leaders direct the CISO to maintain a comprehensive cybersecurity risk strategy and review and update it at least annually and after major events
Ex4: Conduct reviews to ensure adequate authority and coordination among those responsible for managing cybersecurity risk', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(516, 'GV.SC-09', 'Cybersecurity Supply Chain Risk Management', 'Supply chain risk management roles and responsibilities are established and communicated.', 'NIST CSF 2.0', 'Unassigned', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Govern', NULL, '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', 'Cybersecurity Supply Chain Risk Management', 'Ex1: Policies and procedures require provenance records for all acquired technology products and services
Ex2: Periodically provide risk reporting to leaders about how acquired components are proven to be untampered and authentic
Ex3: Communicate regularly among cybersecurity risk managers and operations personnel about the need to acquire software patches, updates, and upgrades only from authenticated and trustworthy software providers
Ex4: Review policies to ensure that they require approved supplier personnel to perform maintenance on supplier products
Ex5: Policies and procedure require checking upgrades to critical hardware for unauthorized changes', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(526, 'ID.RA-02', 'Risk Assessment', 'Cybersecurity risks (technical, operational, and strategic) are evaluated and prioritized.', 'NIST CSF 2.0', 'Unassigned', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Identify', NULL, '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', 'Risk Assessment', 'Ex1: Configure cybersecurity tools and technologies with detection or response capabilities to securely ingest cyber threat intelligence feeds
Ex2: Receive and review advisories from reputable third parties on current threat actors and their tactics, techniques, and procedures (TTPs)
Ex3: Monitor sources of cyber threat intelligence for information on the types of vulnerabilities that emerging technologies may have', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(538, 'ID.IM-04', 'Improvement', 'Cybersecurity objectives are updated as needed.', 'NIST CSF 2.0', 'Unassigned', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Identify', NULL, '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', 'Improvement', 'Ex1: Establish contingency plans (e.g., incident response, business continuity, disaster recovery) for responding to and recovering from adverse events that can interfere with operations, expose confidential information, or otherwise endanger the organization''s mission and viability
Ex2: Include contact and communication information, processes for handling common scenarios, and criteria for prioritization, escalation, and elevation in all contingency plans
Ex3: Create a vulnerability management plan to identify and assess all types of vulnerabilities and to prioritize, test, and implement risk responses
Ex4: Communicate cybersecurity plans (including updates) to those responsible for carrying them out and to affected parties
Ex5: Review and update all cybersecurity plans annually or when a need for significant improvements is identified', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2812, '6.3.6', 'Verify that email is not used as either a single-factor or multi-factor authentication mechanism.', 'Verify that email is not used as either a single-factor or multi-factor authentication mechanism.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.3: General Authentication Security', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3428, '6.4.5', '**Verify that** policy violations trigger quarantining of artifacts and rollback of dependent pipeline runs.', '**Verify that** policy violations trigger quarantining of artifacts and rollback of dependent pipeline runs.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:48:27.839699', '2026-02-04 23:48:27.839699', NULL, '**C6.4 Trusted Source Enforcement**

Allow artifact downloads only from cryptographically verified, organization‑approved sources and block everything else.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(568, 'DE.AE-04', 'Adverse Event Analysis', 'Impact of events is determined and documented.', 'NIST CSF 2.0', 'Unassigned', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Detect', 'Incident Response Policy', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', 'Adverse Event Analysis', 'Ex1: Use SIEMs or other tools to estimate impact and scope, and review and refine the estimates
Ex2: A person creates their own estimates of impact and scope', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(562, 'DE.CM-02', 'Continuous Monitoring', 'The physical environment is monitored to find potentially adverse events.', 'NIST CSF 2.0', 'Unassigned', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Detect', NULL, '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', 'Continuous Monitoring', 'Ex1: Monitor logs from physical access control systems (e.g., badge readers) to find unusual access patterns (e.g., deviations from the norm) and failed access attempts
Ex2: Review and monitor physical access records (e.g., from visitor registration, sign-in sheets)
Ex3: Monitor physical access controls (e.g., locks, latches, hinge pins, alarms) for signs of tampering
Ex4: Monitor the physical environment using alarm systems, cameras, and security guards', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2813, '6.3.7', 'Verify that users are notified after updates to authentication details, such as credential resets or modification of the username or email address.', 'Verify that users are notified after updates to authentication details, such as credential resets or modification of the username or email address.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.3: General Authentication Security', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2814, '6.3.8', 'Verify that valid users cannot be deduced from failed authentication challenges, such as by basing on error messages, HTTP response codes, or different response times. Registration and forgot password functionality must also have this protection.', 'Verify that valid users cannot be deduced from failed authentication challenges, such as by basing on error messages, HTTP response codes, or different response times. Registration and forgot password functionality must also have this protection.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.3: General Authentication Security', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2818, '6.4.4', 'Verify that if a multi-factor authentication factor is lost, evidence of identity proofing is performed at the same level as during enrollment.', 'Verify that if a multi-factor authentication factor is lost, evidence of identity proofing is performed at the same level as during enrollment.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.4: Authentication Factor Lifecycle and Recovery', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2817, '6.4.3', 'Verify that a secure process for resetting a forgotten password is implemented, that does not bypass any enabled multi-factor authentication mechanisms.', 'Verify that a secure process for resetting a forgotten password is implemented, that does not bypass any enabled multi-factor authentication mechanisms.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.4: Authentication Factor Lifecycle and Recovery', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2819, '6.4.5', 'Verify that renewal instructions for authentication mechanisms which expire are sent with enough time to be carried out before the old authentication mechanism expires, configuring automated reminders if necessary.', 'Verify that renewal instructions for authentication mechanisms which expire are sent with enough time to be carried out before the old authentication mechanism expires, configuring automated reminders if necessary.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.4: Authentication Factor Lifecycle and Recovery', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2820, '6.4.6', 'Verify that administrative users can initiate the password reset process for the user, but that this does not allow them to change or choose the user''s password. This prevents a situation where they know the user''s password.', 'Verify that administrative users can initiate the password reset process for the user, but that this does not allow them to change or choose the user''s password. This prevents a situation where they know the user''s password.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.4: Authentication Factor Lifecycle and Recovery', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2821, '6.5.1', 'Verify that lookup secrets, out-of-band authentication requests or codes, and time-based one-time passwords (TOTPs) are only successfully usable once.', 'Verify that lookup secrets, out-of-band authentication requests or codes, and time-based one-time passwords (TOTPs) are only successfully usable once.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.5: General Multi-factor authentication requirements', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3429, '6.5.1', '**Verify that** external datasets undergo poisoning risk scoring (e.g., data fingerprinting, outlier detection).', '**Verify that** external datasets undergo poisoning risk scoring (e.g., data fingerprinting, outlier detection).', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:48:28.062564', '2026-02-04 23:48:28.062564', NULL, '**C6.5 Third‑Party Dataset Risk Assessment**

Evaluate external datasets for poisoning, bias, and legal compliance, and monitor them throughout their lifecycle.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3430, '6.5.2', '**Verify that** bias metrics (demographic parity, equal opportunity) are calculated before dataset approval.', '**Verify that** bias metrics (demographic parity, equal opportunity) are calculated before dataset approval.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:48:28.282042', '2026-02-04 23:48:28.282042', NULL, '**C6.5 Third‑Party Dataset Risk Assessment**

Evaluate external datasets for poisoning, bias, and legal compliance, and monitor them throughout their lifecycle.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2825, '6.5.5', 'Verify that out-of-band authentication requests, codes, or tokens, as well as time-based one-time passwords (TOTPs) have a defined lifetime. Out of band requests must have a maximum lifetime of 10 minutes and for TOTP a maximum lifetime of 30 seconds', 'Verify that out-of-band authentication requests, codes, or tokens, as well as time-based one-time passwords (TOTPs) have a defined lifetime. Out of band requests must have a maximum lifetime of 10 minutes and for TOTP a maximum lifetime of 30 seconds.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.5: General Multi-factor authentication requirements', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2826, '6.5.6', 'Verify that any authentication factor (including physical devices) can be revoked in case of theft or other loss.', 'Verify that any authentication factor (including physical devices) can be revoked in case of theft or other loss.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.5: General Multi-factor authentication requirements', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3632, '11.5.2', '**Verify that** APIs expose consent tokens; models must validate token scope before inference.', '**Verify that** APIs expose consent tokens; models must validate token scope before inference.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:13.349747', '2026-02-04 23:49:13.349747', NULL, '**11.5 Consent Management & Lawful-Basis Tracking**

', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2827, '6.5.7', 'Verify that biometric authentication mechanisms are only used as secondary factors together with either something you have or something you know.', 'Verify that biometric authentication mechanisms are only used as secondary factors together with either something you have or something you know.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.5: General Multi-factor authentication requirements', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2828, '6.5.8', 'Verify that time-based one-time passwords (TOTPs) are checked based on a time source from a trusted service and not from an untrusted or client provided time.', 'Verify that time-based one-time passwords (TOTPs) are checked based on a time source from a trusted service and not from an untrusted or client provided time.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.5: General Multi-factor authentication requirements', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2829, '6.6.1', 'Verify that authentication mechanisms using the Public Switched Telephone Network (PSTN) to deliver One-time Passwords (OTPs) via phone or SMS are offered only when the phone number has previously been validated, alternate stronger methods (such as T', 'Verify that authentication mechanisms using the Public Switched Telephone Network (PSTN) to deliver One-time Passwords (OTPs) via phone or SMS are offered only when the phone number has previously been validated, alternate stronger methods (such as Time based One-time Passwords) are also offered, and the service provides information on their security risks to users. For L3 applications, phone and SMS must not be available as options.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.082', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.6: Out-of-Band authentication mechanisms', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2830, '6.6.2', 'Verify that out-of-band authentication requests, codes, or tokens are bound to the original authentication request for which they were generated and are not usable for a previous or subsequent one.', 'Verify that out-of-band authentication requests, codes, or tokens are bound to the original authentication request for which they were generated and are not usable for a previous or subsequent one.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.082', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.6: Out-of-Band authentication mechanisms', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2831, '6.6.3', 'Verify that a code based out-of-band authentication mechanism is protected against brute force attacks by using rate limiting. Consider also using a code with at least 64 bits of entropy.', 'Verify that a code based out-of-band authentication mechanism is protected against brute force attacks by using rate limiting. Consider also using a code with at least 64 bits of entropy.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.082', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.6: Out-of-Band authentication mechanisms', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2832, '6.6.4', 'Verify that, where push notifications are used for multi-factor authentication, rate limiting is used to prevent push bombing attacks. Number matching may also mitigate this risk.', 'Verify that, where push notifications are used for multi-factor authentication, rate limiting is used to prevent push bombing attacks. Number matching may also mitigate this risk.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.082', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.6: Out-of-Band authentication mechanisms', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2833, '6.7.1', 'Verify that the certificates used to verify cryptographic authentication assertions are stored in a way protects them from modification.', 'Verify that the certificates used to verify cryptographic authentication assertions are stored in a way protects them from modification.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.082', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.7: Cryptographic authentication mechanism', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2834, '6.7.2', 'Verify that the challenge nonce is at least 64 bits in length, and statistically unique or unique over the lifetime of the cryptographic device.', 'Verify that the challenge nonce is at least 64 bits in length, and statistically unique or unique over the lifetime of the cryptographic device.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.082', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.7: Cryptographic authentication mechanism', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3633, '11.5.3', '**Verify that** denied or withdrawn consent halts processing pipelines within 24 hours.', '**Verify that** denied or withdrawn consent halts processing pipelines within 24 hours.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:13.568723', '2026-02-04 23:49:13.568723', NULL, '**11.5 Consent Management & Lawful-Basis Tracking**

', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3634, '11.6.1', '**Verify that** client updates employ local differential privacy noise addition before aggregation.', '**Verify that** client updates employ local differential privacy noise addition before aggregation.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:13.789733', '2026-02-04 23:49:13.789733', NULL, '**11.6 Federated Learning with Privacy Controls**

', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3635, '11.6.2', '**Verify that** training metrics are differentially private and never reveal single-client loss.', '**Verify that** training metrics are differentially private and never reveal single-client loss.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:14.028756', '2026-02-04 23:49:14.028756', NULL, '**11.6 Federated Learning with Privacy Controls**

', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4297, '13.2.3', 'Verify that RESTful web services that utilize cookies are protected from Cross-Site Request Forgery via the use of at least one or more of the following: double submit cookie pattern, CSRF nonces, or Origin request header checks.', 'Verify that RESTful web services that utilize cookies are protected from Cross-Site Request Forgery via the use of at least one or more of the following: double submit cookie pattern, CSRF nonces, or Origin request header checks.', 'ASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'ASVS, L1, L2, L3, CWE-352', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:07.856048', '2026-02-06 13:43:07.856048', NULL, '**V13.2 RESTful Web Service**

JSON schema validation is in a draft stage of standardization (see references). When considering using JSON schema validation, which is best practice for RESTful web services, consider using these additional data validation strategies in combination with JSON schema validation:

* Parsing validation of the JSON object, such as if there are missing or extra elements.
* Validation of the JSON object values using standard input validation methods, such as data type, data format, length, etc.
* and formal JSON schema validation.

Once the JSON schema validation standard is formalized, ASVS will update its advice in this area. Carefully monitor any JSON schema validation libraries in use, as they will need to be updated regularly until the standard is formalized and bugs are ironed out of reference implementations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2844, '7.2.3', 'Verify that if reference tokens are used to represent user sessions, they are unique and generated using a cryptographically secure pseudo-random number generator (CSPRNG) and possess at least 128 bits of entropy.', 'Verify that if reference tokens are used to represent user sessions, they are unique and generated using a cryptographically secure pseudo-random number generator (CSPRNG) and possess at least 128 bits of entropy.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V7: Session Management', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.083', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V7.2: Fundamental Session Management Security', 'Applicable Levels: L1, L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(577, 'RS.AN-03', 'Incident Analysis', 'Forensics are performed as needed.', 'NIST CSF 2.0', 'Unassigned', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Respond', NULL, '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', 'Incident Analysis', 'Ex1: Determine the sequence of events that occurred during the incident and which assets and resources were involved in each event
Ex2: Attempt to determine what vulnerabilities, threats, and threat actors were directly or indirectly involved in the incident
Ex3: Analyze the incident to find the underlying, systemic root causes
Ex4: Check any cyber deception technology for additional information on attacker behavior', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(591, 'RC.CO-03', 'Recovery Communication', 'Recovery activities are updated based on lessons learned.', 'NIST CSF 2.0', 'Unassigned', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Recover', NULL, '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', 'Incident Recovery Communication', 'Ex1: Securely share recovery information, including restoration progress, consistent with response plans and information sharing agreements
Ex2: Regularly update senior leadership on recovery status and restoration progress for major incidents
Ex3: Follow the rules and protocols defined in contracts for incident information sharing between the organization and its suppliers
Ex4: Coordinate crisis communication between the organization and its critical suppliers', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2845, '7.2.4', 'Verify that the application generates a new session token on user authentication, including re-authentication, and terminates the current session token.', 'Verify that the application generates a new session token on user authentication, including re-authentication, and terminates the current session token.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V7: Session Management', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.083', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V7.2: Fundamental Session Management Security', 'Applicable Levels: L1, L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4298, '13.2.4', '[DELETED, DUPLICATE OF 11.1.4]', '[DELETED, DUPLICATE OF 11.1.4]', 'ASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'ASVS', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:08.086037', '2026-02-06 13:43:08.086037', NULL, '**V13.2 RESTful Web Service**

JSON schema validation is in a draft stage of standardization (see references). When considering using JSON schema validation, which is best practice for RESTful web services, consider using these additional data validation strategies in combination with JSON schema validation:

* Parsing validation of the JSON object, such as if there are missing or extra elements.
* Validation of the JSON object values using standard input validation methods, such as data type, data format, length, etc.
* and formal JSON schema validation.

Once the JSON schema validation standard is formalized, ASVS will update its advice in this area. Carefully monitor any JSON schema validation libraries in use, as they will need to be updated regularly until the standard is formalized and bugs are ironed out of reference implementations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(488, 'GV.OC-02', 'Organizational Context', 'Internal and external stakeholders are understood, and their needs and expectations regarding cybersecurity risk management are understood and considered.', 'NIST CSF 2.0', 'Unassigned', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Govern', NULL, '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', 'Organizational Context', 'Ex1: Identify relevant internal stakeholders and their cybersecurity-related expectations (e.g., performance and risk expectations of officers, directors, and advisors; cultural expectations of employees)
Ex2: Identify relevant external stakeholders and their cybersecurity-related expectations (e.g., privacy expectations of customers, business expectations of partnerships, compliance expectations of regulators, ethics expectations of society)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2851, '7.4.4', 'Verify that all pages that require authentication have easy and visible access to logout functionality.', 'Verify that all pages that require authentication have easy and visible access to logout functionality.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V7: Session Management', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.336', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V7.4: Session Termination', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2852, '7.4.5', 'Verify that application administrators are able to terminate active sessions for an individual user or for all users.', 'Verify that application administrators are able to terminate active sessions for an individual user or for all users.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V7: Session Management', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.336', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V7.4: Session Termination', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2853, '7.5.1', 'Verify that the application requires full re-authentication before allowing modifications to sensitive account attributes which may affect authentication such as email address, phone number, MFA configuration, or other information used in account rec', 'Verify that the application requires full re-authentication before allowing modifications to sensitive account attributes which may affect authentication such as email address, phone number, MFA configuration, or other information used in account recovery.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V7: Session Management', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.336', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V7.5: Defenses Against Session Abuse', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2855, '7.5.3', 'Verify that the application requires further authentication with at least one factor or secondary verification before performing highly sensitive transactions or operations.', 'Verify that the application requires further authentication with at least one factor or secondary verification before performing highly sensitive transactions or operations.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V7: Session Management', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.336', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V7.5: Defenses Against Session Abuse', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2854, '7.5.2', 'Verify that users are able to view and (having authenticated again with at least one factor) terminate any or all currently active sessions.', 'Verify that users are able to view and (having authenticated again with at least one factor) terminate any or all currently active sessions.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V7: Session Management', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.336', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V7.5: Defenses Against Session Abuse', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2857, '7.6.2', 'Verify that creation of a session requires either the user''s consent or an explicit action, preventing the creation of new application sessions without user interaction.', 'Verify that creation of a session requires either the user''s consent or an explicit action, preventing the creation of new application sessions without user interaction.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V7: Session Management', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.336', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V7.6: Federated Re-authentication', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4299, '13.2.5', 'Verify that REST services explicitly check the incoming Content-Type to be the expected one, such as application/xml or application/json.', 'Verify that REST services explicitly check the incoming Content-Type to be the expected one, such as application/xml or application/json.', 'ASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'ASVS, L1, L2', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:08.311059', '2026-02-06 13:43:08.311059', NULL, '**V13.2 RESTful Web Service**

JSON schema validation is in a draft stage of standardization (see references). When considering using JSON schema validation, which is best practice for RESTful web services, consider using these additional data validation strategies in combination with JSON schema validation:

* Parsing validation of the JSON object, such as if there are missing or extra elements.
* Validation of the JSON object values using standard input validation methods, such as data type, data format, length, etc.
* and formal JSON schema validation.

Once the JSON schema validation standard is formalized, ASVS will update its advice in this area. Carefully monitor any JSON schema validation libraries in use, as they will need to be updated regularly until the standard is formalized and bugs are ironed out of reference implementations.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2865, '8.2.4', 'Verify that adaptive security controls based on a consumer''s environmental and contextual attributes (such as time of day, location, IP address, or device) are implemented for authentication and authorization decisions, as defined in the application''', 'Verify that adaptive security controls based on a consumer''s environmental and contextual attributes (such as time of day, location, IP address, or device) are implemented for authentication and authorization decisions, as defined in the application''s documentation. These controls must be applied when the consumer tries to start a new session and also during an existing session.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V8: Authorization', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.336', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V8.2: General Authorization Design', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2869, '8.4.1', 'Verify that multi-tenant applications use cross-tenant controls to ensure consumer operations will never affect tenants with which they do not have permissions to interact.', 'Verify that multi-tenant applications use cross-tenant controls to ensure consumer operations will never affect tenants with which they do not have permissions to interact.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V8: Authorization', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.593', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V8.4: Other Authorization Considerations', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2870, '8.4.2', 'Verify that access to administrative interfaces incorporates multiple layers of security, including continuous consumer identity verification, device security posture assessment, and contextual risk analysis, ensuring that network location or trusted', 'Verify that access to administrative interfaces incorporates multiple layers of security, including continuous consumer identity verification, device security posture assessment, and contextual risk analysis, ensuring that network location or trusted endpoints are not the sole factors for authorization even though they may reduce the likelihood of unauthorized access.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V8: Authorization', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.593', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V8.4: Other Authorization Considerations', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2883, '10.3.1', 'Verify that the resource server only accepts access tokens that are intended for use with that service (audience). The audience may be included in a structured access token (such as the ''aud'' claim in JWT), or it can be checked using the token intros', 'Verify that the resource server only accepts access tokens that are intended for use with that service (audience). The audience may be included in a structured access token (such as the ''aud'' claim in JWT), or it can be checked using the token introspection endpoint.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.593', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V10.3: OAuth Resource Server', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2878, '10.1.1', 'Verify that tokens are only sent to components that strictly need them. For example, when using a backend-for-frontend pattern for browser-based JavaScript applications, access and refresh tokens shall only be accessible for the backend.', 'Verify that tokens are only sent to components that strictly need them. For example, when using a backend-for-frontend pattern for browser-based JavaScript applications, access and refresh tokens shall only be accessible for the backend.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.593', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V10.1: Generic OAuth and OIDC Security', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2879, '10.1.2', 'Verify that the client only accepts values from the authorization server (such as the authorization code or ID Token) if these values result from an authorization flow that was initiated by the same user agent session and transaction. This requires t', 'Verify that the client only accepts values from the authorization server (such as the authorization code or ID Token) if these values result from an authorization flow that was initiated by the same user agent session and transaction. This requires that client-generated secrets, such as the proof key for code exchange (PKCE) ''code_verifier'', ''state'' or OIDC ''nonce'', are not guessable, are specific to the transaction, and are securely bound to both the client and the user agent session in which the transaction was started.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.593', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V10.1: Generic OAuth and OIDC Security', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2880, '10.2.1', 'Verify that, if the code flow is used, the OAuth client has protection against browser-based request forgery attacks, commonly known as cross-site request forgery (CSRF), which trigger token requests, either by using proof key for code exchange (PKCE', 'Verify that, if the code flow is used, the OAuth client has protection against browser-based request forgery attacks, commonly known as cross-site request forgery (CSRF), which trigger token requests, either by using proof key for code exchange (PKCE) functionality or checking the ''state'' parameter that was sent in the authorization request.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.593', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V10.2: OAuth Client', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(566, 'DE.AE-02', 'Adverse Event Analysis', 'Potentially adverse events are analyzed to better understand associated activities.', 'NIST CSF 2.0', 'Unassigned', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Detect', 'Incident Response Policy', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', '2025-12-20 09:07:31.20323', 'Adverse Event Analysis', 'Ex1: Use security information and event management (SIEM) or other tools to continuously monitor log events for known malicious and suspicious activity
Ex2: Utilize up-to-date cyber threat intelligence in log analysis tools to improve detection accuracy and characterize threat actors, their methods, and indicators of compromise
Ex3: Regularly conduct manual reviews of log events for technologies that cannot be sufficiently monitored through automation
Ex4: Use log analysis tools to generate reports on their findings', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2881, '10.2.2', 'Verify that, if the OAuth client can interact with more than one authorization server, it has a defense against mix-up attacks. For example, it could require that the authorization server return the ''iss'' parameter value and validate it in the author', 'Verify that, if the OAuth client can interact with more than one authorization server, it has a defense against mix-up attacks. For example, it could require that the authorization server return the ''iss'' parameter value and validate it in the authorization response and the token response.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.593', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V10.2: OAuth Client', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2882, '10.2.3', 'Verify that the OAuth client only requests the required scopes (or other authorization parameters) in requests to the authorization server.', 'Verify that the OAuth client only requests the required scopes (or other authorization parameters) in requests to the authorization server.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.593', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V10.2: OAuth Client', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3431, '6.5.3', '**Verify that** origin, lineage, and license terms for datasets are captured in ML‑BOM entries.', '**Verify that** origin, lineage, and license terms for datasets are captured in ML‑BOM entries.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:48:28.503576', '2026-02-04 23:48:28.503576', NULL, '**C6.5 Third‑Party Dataset Risk Assessment**

Evaluate external datasets for poisoning, bias, and legal compliance, and monitor them throughout their lifecycle.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3432, '6.5.4', '**Verify that** periodic monitoring detects drift or corruption in hosted datasets.', '**Verify that** periodic monitoring detects drift or corruption in hosted datasets.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:48:28.727564', '2026-02-04 23:48:28.727564', NULL, '**C6.5 Third‑Party Dataset Risk Assessment**

Evaluate external datasets for poisoning, bias, and legal compliance, and monitor them throughout their lifecycle.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2884, '10.3.2', 'Verify that the resource server enforces authorization decisions based on claims from the access token that define delegated authorization. If claims such as ''sub'', ''scope'', and ''authorization_details'' are present, they must be part of the decision.', 'Verify that the resource server enforces authorization decisions based on claims from the access token that define delegated authorization. If claims such as ''sub'', ''scope'', and ''authorization_details'' are present, they must be part of the decision.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.593', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V10.3: OAuth Resource Server', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2887, '10.3.5', 'Verify that the resource server prevents the use of stolen access tokens or replay of access tokens (from unauthorized parties) by requiring sender-constrained access tokens, either Mutual TLS for OAuth 2 or OAuth 2 Demonstration of Proof of Possessi', 'Verify that the resource server prevents the use of stolen access tokens or replay of access tokens (from unauthorized parties) by requiring sender-constrained access tokens, either Mutual TLS for OAuth 2 or OAuth 2 Demonstration of Proof of Possession (DPoP).', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.593', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V10.3: OAuth Resource Server', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2888, '10.4.1', 'Verify that the authorization server validates redirect URIs based on a client-specific allowlist of pre-registered URIs using exact string comparison.', 'Verify that the authorization server validates redirect URIs based on a client-specific allowlist of pre-registered URIs using exact string comparison.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.593', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.593089', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L1, L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2889, '10.4.2', 'Verify that, if the authorization server returns the authorization code in the authorization response, it can be used only once for a token request. For the second valid request with an authorization code that has already been used to issue an access', 'Verify that, if the authorization server returns the authorization code in the authorization response, it can be used only once for a token request. For the second valid request with an authorization code that has already been used to issue an access token, the authorization server must reject a token request and revoke any issued tokens related to the authorization code.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L1, L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2890, '10.4.3', 'Verify that the authorization code is short-lived. The maximum lifetime can be up to 10 minutes for L1 and L2 applications and up to 1 minute for L3 applications.', 'Verify that the authorization code is short-lived. The maximum lifetime can be up to 10 minutes for L1 and L2 applications and up to 1 minute for L3 applications.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L1, L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2891, '10.4.4', 'Verify that for a given client, the authorization server only allows the usage of grants that this client needs to use. Note that the grants ''token'' (Implicit flow) and ''password'' (Resource Owner Password Credentials flow) must no longer be used.', 'Verify that for a given client, the authorization server only allows the usage of grants that this client needs to use. Note that the grants ''token'' (Implicit flow) and ''password'' (Resource Owner Password Credentials flow) must no longer be used.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L1, L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2892, '10.4.5', 'Verify that the authorization server mitigates refresh token replay attacks for public clients, preferably using sender-constrained refresh tokens, i.e., Demonstrating Proof of Possession (DPoP) or Certificate-Bound Access Tokens using mutual TLS (mT', 'Verify that the authorization server mitigates refresh token replay attacks for public clients, preferably using sender-constrained refresh tokens, i.e., Demonstrating Proof of Possession (DPoP) or Certificate-Bound Access Tokens using mutual TLS (mTLS). For L1 and L2 applications, refresh token rotation may be used. If refresh token rotation is used, the authorization server must invalidate the refresh token after usage, and revoke all refresh tokens for that authorization if an already used and invalidated refresh token is provided.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L1, L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2893, '10.4.6', 'Verify that, if the code grant is used, the authorization server mitigates authorization code interception attacks by requiring proof key for code exchange (PKCE). For authorization requests, the authorization server must require a valid ''code_challe', 'Verify that, if the code grant is used, the authorization server mitigates authorization code interception attacks by requiring proof key for code exchange (PKCE). For authorization requests, the authorization server must require a valid ''code_challenge'' value and must not accept a ''code_challenge_method'' value of ''plain''. For a token request, it must require validation of the ''code_verifier'' parameter.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2894, '10.4.7', 'Verify that if the authorization server supports unauthenticated dynamic client registration, it mitigates the risk of malicious client applications. It must validate client metadata such as any registered URIs, ensure the user''s consent, and warn th', 'Verify that if the authorization server supports unauthenticated dynamic client registration, it mitigates the risk of malicious client applications. It must validate client metadata such as any registered URIs, ensure the user''s consent, and warn the user before processing an authorization request with an untrusted client application.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2897, '10.4.10', 'Verify that confidential client is authenticated for client-to-authorized server backchannel requests such as token requests, pushed authorization requests (PAR), and token revocation requests.', 'Verify that confidential client is authenticated for client-to-authorized server backchannel requests such as token requests, pushed authorization requests (PAR), and token revocation requests.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2899, '10.4.12', 'Verify that for a given client, the authorization server only allows the ''response_mode'' value that this client needs to use. For example, by having the authorization server validate this value against the expected values or by using pushed authoriza', 'Verify that for a given client, the authorization server only allows the ''response_mode'' value that this client needs to use. For example, by having the authorization server validate this value against the expected values or by using pushed authorization request (PAR) or JWT-secured Authorization Request (JAR).', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2900, '10.4.13', 'Verify that grant type ''code'' is always used together with pushed authorization requests (PAR).', 'Verify that grant type ''code'' is always used together with pushed authorization requests (PAR).', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2901, '10.4.14', 'Verify that the authorization server issues only sender-constrained (Proof-of-Possession) access tokens, either with certificate-bound access tokens using mutual TLS (mTLS) or DPoP-bound access tokens (Demonstration of Proof of Possession).', 'Verify that the authorization server issues only sender-constrained (Proof-of-Possession) access tokens, either with certificate-bound access tokens using mutual TLS (mTLS) or DPoP-bound access tokens (Demonstration of Proof of Possession).', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2902, '10.4.15', 'Verify that, for a server-side client (which is not executed on the end-user device), the authorization server ensures that the ''authorization_details'' parameter value is from the client backend and that the user has not tampered with it. For example', 'Verify that, for a server-side client (which is not executed on the end-user device), the authorization server ensures that the ''authorization_details'' parameter value is from the client backend and that the user has not tampered with it. For example, by requiring the usage of pushed authorization request (PAR) or JWT-secured Authorization Request (JAR).', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2903, '10.4.16', 'Verify that the client is confidential and the authorization server requires the use of strong client authentication methods (based on public-key cryptography and resistant to replay attacks), such as mutual TLS (''tls_client_auth'', ''self_signed_tls_c', 'Verify that the client is confidential and the authorization server requires the use of strong client authentication methods (based on public-key cryptography and resistant to replay attacks), such as mutual TLS (''tls_client_auth'', ''self_signed_tls_client_auth'') or private key JWT (''private_key_jwt'').', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2904, '10.5.1', 'Verify that the client (as the relying party) mitigates ID Token replay attacks. For example, by ensuring that the ''nonce'' claim in the ID Token matches the ''nonce'' value sent in the authentication request to the OpenID Provider (in OAuth2 refereed t', 'Verify that the client (as the relying party) mitigates ID Token replay attacks. For example, by ensuring that the ''nonce'' claim in the ID Token matches the ''nonce'' value sent in the authentication request to the OpenID Provider (in OAuth2 refereed to as the authorization request sent to the authorization server).', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.5: OIDC Client', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2905, '10.5.2', 'Verify that the client uniquely identifies the user from ID Token claims, usually the ''sub'' claim, which cannot be reassigned to other users (for the scope of an identity provider).', 'Verify that the client uniquely identifies the user from ID Token claims, usually the ''sub'' claim, which cannot be reassigned to other users (for the scope of an identity provider).', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.5: OIDC Client', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2906, '10.5.3', 'Verify that the client rejects attempts by a malicious authorization server to impersonate another authorization server through authorization server metadata. The client must reject authorization server metadata if the issuer URL in the authorization', 'Verify that the client rejects attempts by a malicious authorization server to impersonate another authorization server through authorization server metadata. The client must reject authorization server metadata if the issuer URL in the authorization server metadata does not exactly match the pre-configured issuer URL expected by the client.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.856', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.5: OIDC Client', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2907, '10.5.4', 'Verify that the client validates that the ID Token is intended to be used for that client (audience) by checking that the ''aud'' claim from the token is equal to the ''client_id'' value for the client.', 'Verify that the client validates that the ID Token is intended to be used for that client (audience) by checking that the ''aud'' claim from the token is equal to the ''client_id'' value for the client.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.856', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.5: OIDC Client', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2932, '11.5.1', 'Verify that all random numbers and strings which are intended to be non-guessable must be generated using a cryptographically secure pseudo-random number generator (CSPRNG) and have at least 128 bits of entropy. Note that UUIDs do not respect this co', 'Verify that all random numbers and strings which are intended to be non-guessable must be generated using a cryptographically secure pseudo-random number generator (CSPRNG) and have at least 128 bits of entropy. Note that UUIDs do not respect this condition.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V11: Cryptography', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.365', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V11.5: Random Values', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2909, '10.6.1', 'Verify that the OpenID Provider only allows values ''code'', ''ciba'', ''id_token'', or ''id_token code'' for response mode. Note that ''code'' is preferred over ''id_token code'' (the OIDC Hybrid flow), and ''token'' (any Implicit flow) must not be used.', 'Verify that the OpenID Provider only allows values ''code'', ''ciba'', ''id_token'', or ''id_token code'' for response mode. Note that ''code'' is preferred over ''id_token code'' (the OIDC Hybrid flow), and ''token'' (any Implicit flow) must not be used.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.111', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.6: OpenID Provider', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2910, '10.6.2', 'Verify that the OpenID Provider mitigates denial of service through forced logout. By obtaining explicit confirmation from the end-user or, if present, validating parameters in the logout request (initiated by the relying party), such as the ''id_toke', 'Verify that the OpenID Provider mitigates denial of service through forced logout. By obtaining explicit confirmation from the end-user or, if present, validating parameters in the logout request (initiated by the relying party), such as the ''id_token_hint''.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.111', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.6: OpenID Provider', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2912, '10.7.2', 'Verify that when the authorization server prompts for user consent, it presents sufficient and clear information about what is being consented to. When applicable, this should include the nature of the requested authorizations (typically based on sco', 'Verify that when the authorization server prompts for user consent, it presents sufficient and clear information about what is being consented to. When applicable, this should include the nature of the requested authorizations (typically based on scope, resource server, Rich Authorization Requests (RAR) authorization details), the identity of the authorized application, and the lifetime of these authorizations.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.111', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.7: Consent Management', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2913, '10.7.3', 'Verify that the user can review, modify, and revoke consents which the user has granted through the authorization server.', 'Verify that the user can review, modify, and revoke consents which the user has granted through the authorization server.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.111', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.7: Consent Management', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2914, '11.1.1', 'Verify that there is a documented policy for management of cryptographic keys and a cryptographic key lifecycle that follows a key management standard such as NIST SP 800-57. This should include ensuring that keys are not overshared (for example, wit', 'Verify that there is a documented policy for management of cryptographic keys and a cryptographic key lifecycle that follows a key management standard such as NIST SP 800-57. This should include ensuring that keys are not overshared (for example, with more than two entities for shared secrets and more than one entity for private keys).', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V11: Cryptography', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.111', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V11.1: Cryptographic Inventory and Documentation', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2915, '11.1.2', 'Verify that a cryptographic inventory is performed, maintained, regularly updated, and includes all cryptographic keys, algorithms, and certificates used by the application. It must also document where keys can and cannot be used in the system, and t', 'Verify that a cryptographic inventory is performed, maintained, regularly updated, and includes all cryptographic keys, algorithms, and certificates used by the application. It must also document where keys can and cannot be used in the system, and the types of data that can and cannot be protected using the keys.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V11: Cryptography', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.111', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V11.1: Cryptographic Inventory and Documentation', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2916, '11.1.3', 'Verify that cryptographic discovery mechanisms are employed to identify all instances of cryptography in the system, including encryption, hashing, and signing operations.', 'Verify that cryptographic discovery mechanisms are employed to identify all instances of cryptography in the system, including encryption, hashing, and signing operations.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V11: Cryptography', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.111', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V11.1: Cryptographic Inventory and Documentation', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2917, '11.1.4', 'Verify that a cryptographic inventory is maintained. This must include a documented plan that outlines the migration path to new cryptographic standards, such as post-quantum cryptography, in order to react to future threats.', 'Verify that a cryptographic inventory is maintained. This must include a documented plan that outlines the migration path to new cryptographic standards, such as post-quantum cryptography, in order to react to future threats.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V11: Cryptography', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.111', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V11.1: Cryptographic Inventory and Documentation', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

Isolate tool interactions to prevent unauthorized system access or code execution.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3504, '9.2.3', '**Verify that** tool binaries or descriptors are digitally signed; signatures are validated before loading.', '**Verify that** tool binaries or descriptors are digitally signed; signatures are validated before loading.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:48:44.786801', '2026-02-04 23:48:44.786801', NULL, '**9.2 Tool Plugin Sandboxing**

Isolate tool interactions to prevent unauthorized system access or code execution.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1825, 'CP-2', 'Contingency Plan', 'Develop a contingency plan for the system that: Identifies essential mission and business functions and associated contingency requirements; Provides recovery objectives, restoration priorities, and metrics; Addresses contingency roles, responsibilities, assigned individuals with contact information; Addresses maintaining essential mission and business functions despite a system disruption, compromise, or failure; Addresses eventual, full system restoration without deterioration of the controls originally planned and implemented; Addresses the sharing of contingency information; and Is reviewed and approved by {{ insert: param, cp-2_prm_1 }};Distribute copies of the contingency plan to {{ insert: param, cp-2_prm_2 }}; Coordinate contingency planning activities with incident handling activities; Review the contingency plan for the system {{ insert: param, cp-02_odp.05 }}; Update the contingency plan to address changes to the organization, system, or environment of operation and problems encountered during contingency plan implementation, execution, or testing; Communicate contingency plan changes to {{ insert: param, cp-2_prm_4 }}; Incorporate lessons learned from contingency plan testing, training, or actual contingency activities into contingency testing and training; and Protect the contingency plan from unauthorized disclosure and modification.', 'NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'Contingency Planning', NULL, '2026-01-09 09:38:06.23121', '2026-01-09 09:38:06.23121', 'Contingency Planning', 'Contingency planning for systems is part of an overall program for achieving continuity of operations for organizational mission and business functions. Contingency planning addresses system restoration and implementation of alternative mission or business processes when systems are compromised or breached. Contingency planning is considered throughout the system development life cycle and is a fundamental part of the system design. Systems can be designed for redundancy, to provide backup capabilities, and for resilience. Contingency plans reflect the degree of restoration required for organizational systems since not all systems need to fully recover to achieve the level of continuity of operations desired. System recovery objectives reflect applicable laws, executive orders, directives, regulations, policies, standards, guidelines, organizational risk tolerance, and system impact level.

Actions addressed in contingency plans include orderly system degradation, system shutdown, fallback to a manual mode, alternate information flows, and operating in modes reserved for when systems are under attack. By coordinating contingency planning with incident handling activities, organizations ensure that the necessary planning activities are in place and activated in the event of an incident. Organizations consider whether continuity of operations during an incident conflicts with the capability to automatically disable the system, as specified in [IR-4(5)](#ir-4.5) . Incident response planning is part of contingency planning for organizations and is addressed in the [IR](#ir) (Incident Response) family.', NULL, '## **CP-2 Contingency Plan Implementation Guidance**

### **1. Implementation Guidance**

**Phase 1: Plan Development & Scope Definition**
*   **Conduct a Business Impact Analysis (BIA):** Identify and document essential mission/business functions, their Recovery Time Objectives (RTOs), Recovery Point Objectives (RPOs), and maximum tolerable downtime. Prioritize systems (e.g., cloud-native apps, databases, identity services).
*   **Define Clear Recovery Strategies:** For each priority tier, specify the technical recovery approach (e.g., failover to AWS Region B, restore from immutable backups in Azure Blob Storage, spin up containerized services in Kubernetes).
*   **Establish Roles & Communication:** Create a RACI matrix for the contingency team (e.g., Incident Commander, Cloud Infrastructure Lead, App Owner, Comms Lead). Include primary/backup contact details and define external stakeholder notification procedures.
*   **Integrate with Incident Response:** Ensure the CP-2 plan''s activation criteria and procedures are documented in your Incident Response Plan (IR-4). Use a common playbook format (e.g., in Jira, ServiceNow, or dedicated IR platform) to avoid conflict.

**Phase 2: Plan Distribution, Maintenance & Protection**
*   **Secure Distribution & Access:** Store the approved plan in a secure, accessible location (e.g., encrypted S3 bucket with limited IAM roles, password manager like 1Password for Teams). Define `cp-2_prm_2` as contingency team members and key management.
*   **Implement a Formal Review Cycle:** Define `cp-2_prm_1` (approving officials) and `cp-02_odp.05` (review frequency, e.g., annually or after significant changes). Trigger reviews after major cloud architecture changes, mergers, or new regulatory requirements.
*   **Manage Changes Systematically:** Maintain a change log for the plan. Define `cp-2_prm_4` as all plan holders and stakeholders. Communicate updates via a controlled channel (e.g., a dedicated Teams/Slack channel, or a notification from your GRC platform).
*   **Protect Plan Integrity:** Classify the plan as "Confidential" or "Contingency Plan - Sensitive." Apply access controls (e.g., least-privilege IAM policies, require VPN for access, disable printing/downloading).

**Phase 3: Integration with Testing & Operations**
*   **Incorporate Lessons Learned:** After any test (tabletop or technical DR drill) or actual event, conduct a formal after-action review. Update recovery runbooks, contact lists, and cloud configurations based on findings.
*   **Automate Where Possible:** Use Infrastructure as Code (IaC) templates (Terraform, CloudFormation) to document and automate recovery environments. Embed restoration priorities and steps into runbooks.

### **2. Evidence Artifacts**

*   **Approved Contingency Plan Document:** Version-controlled document showing approval by `cp-2_prm_1` (e.g., CISO, System Owner).
*   **Business Impact Analysis (BIA) Report:** Documents essential functions, RTOs, RPOs, and system priorities.
*   **Contingency Team RACI Matrix & Contact List:** Dated roster with roles, responsibilities, and verified contact information.
*   **Distribution Records:** Logs or receipts showing the plan was provided to `cp-2_prm_2` (e.g., email receipts, access logs from secure repository).
*   **Plan Review & Update Records:** Minutes from annual review meetings, change logs showing updates triggered by system/environment changes.
*   **Communication Records:** Notices sent to `cp-2_prm_4` informing them of plan updates.
*   **Integration Evidence:** Documented procedures or playbook excerpts showing coordination between contingency and incident handling teams.
*   **Protection Mechanisms:** Configuration screenshots of access controls (IAM policies, SharePoint permissions) protecting the plan.

### **3. Common Pitfalls**

*   **"Shelfware" Plan:** Creating a plan that is not integrated with daily operations or incident response. **Mitigation:** Design recovery steps as executable runbooks, not just prose.
*   **Outdated Contacts & Dependencies:** Failing to update contact lists and overlooking critical third-party dependencies (e.g., SaaS providers, cloud regions). **Mitigation:** Review and verify contacts quarterly. Map and document external dependencies in the BIA.
*   **Ignoring Cloud Shared Responsibility Model:** Assuming the cloud provider (AWS, Azure, GCP) handles all recovery aspects. **Mitigation:** Clearly document in the plan which recovery tasks are your responsibility (e.g., data restoration, application failover) vs. the provider''s.
*   **Lack of Measurable Objectives:** Defining vague recovery goals instead of specific, measurable RTOs/RPOs. **Mitigation:** Base objectives on the BIA and validate them through testing.
*   **Poor Change Management:** Updating the live system without considering contingency plan impacts. **Mitigation:** Integrate contingency plan review as a checkpoint in your change management process for significant system modifications.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2934, '11.6.1', 'Verify that only approved cryptographic algorithms and modes of operation are used for key generation and seeding, and digital signature generation and verification. Key generation algorithms must not generate insecure keys vulnerable to known attack', 'Verify that only approved cryptographic algorithms and modes of operation are used for key generation and seeding, and digital signature generation and verification. Key generation algorithms must not generate insecure keys vulnerable to known attacks, for example, RSA keys which are vulnerable to Fermat factorization.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V11: Cryptography', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.365', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V11.6: Public Key Cryptography', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2937, '11.7.2', 'Verify that data minimization ensures the minimal amount of data is exposed during processing, and ensure that data is encrypted immediately after use or as soon as feasible.', 'Verify that data minimization ensures the minimal amount of data is exposed during processing, and ensure that data is encrypted immediately after use or as soon as feasible.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V11: Cryptography', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.365', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V11.7: In-Use Data Cryptography', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2941, '12.1.4', 'Verify that proper certification revocation, such as Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) Stapling, is enabled and configured.', 'Verify that proper certification revocation, such as Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) Stapling, is enabled and configured.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V12: Secure Communication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.365', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.843074', 'V12.1: General TLS Security Guidance', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2942, '12.1.5', 'Verify that Encrypted Client Hello (ECH) is enabled in the application''s TLS settings to prevent exposure of sensitive metadata, such as the Server Name Indication (SNI), during TLS handshake processes.', 'Verify that Encrypted Client Hello (ECH) is enabled in the application''s TLS settings to prevent exposure of sensitive metadata, such as the Server Name Indication (SNI), during TLS handshake processes.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V12: Secure Communication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.365', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.843074', 'V12.1: General TLS Security Guidance', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2944, '12.2.2', 'Verify that external facing services use publicly trusted TLS certificates.', 'Verify that external facing services use publicly trusted TLS certificates.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V12: Secure Communication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.365', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.843074', 'V12.2: HTTPS Communication with External Facing Services', 'Applicable Levels: L1, L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4300, '14.1.2', 'Verify that compiler flags are configured to enable all available buffer overflow protections and warnings, including stack randomization, data execution prevention, and to break the build if an unsafe pointer, memory, format string, integer, or string op', 'Verify that compiler flags are configured to enable all available buffer overflow protections and warnings, including stack randomization, data execution prevention, and to break the build if an unsafe pointer, memory, format string, integer, or string operations are found.', 'ASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'ASVS, L1, L2', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:08.538012', '2026-02-06 13:43:08.538012', NULL, '**V14.1 Build and Deploy**

Build pipelines are the basis for repeatable security - every time something insecure is discovered, it can be resolved in the source code, build or deployment scripts, and tested automatically. We are strongly encouraging the use of build pipelines with automatic security and dependency checks that warn or break the build to prevent known security issues being deployed into production. Manual steps performed irregularly directly leads to avoidable security mistakes.

As the industry moves to a DevSecOps model, it is important to ensure the continued availability and integrity of deployment and configuration to achieve a "known good" state. In the past, if a system was hacked, it would take days to months to prove that no further intrusions had taken place. Today, with the advent of software defined infrastructure, rapid A/B deployments with zero downtime, and automated containerized builds, it is possible to automatically and continuously build, harden, and deploy a "known good" replacement for any compromised system.

If traditional models are still in place, then manual steps must be taken to harden and back up that configuration to allow the compromised systems to be quickly replaced with high integrity, uncompromised systems in a timely fashion.

Compliance with this section requires an automated build system, and access to build and deployment scripts.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
