	(94, 'A.8.28', 'Secure application development', 'Applications shall be developed securely.', 'ISO/IEC 27001:2022', '', '', NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological', NULL, '2025-12-19 06:15:44.072337', '2025-12-19 06:15:44.072337', 'Technological', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(95, 'A.8.29', 'Security testing in development and acceptance', 'Security testing shall be conducted during development and acceptance.', 'ISO/IEC 27001:2022', '', '', NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological', NULL, '2025-12-19 06:15:44.278336', '2025-12-19 06:15:44.278336', 'Technological', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(96, 'A.8.30', 'Outsourced development', 'Outsourced development shall be managed securely.', 'ISO/IEC 27001:2022', '', '', NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological', NULL, '2025-12-19 06:15:44.486392', '2025-12-19 06:15:44.486392', 'Technological', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(97, 'A.8.31', 'Separation of development, test and production environments', 'Development, test and production environments shall be separated.', 'ISO/IEC 27001:2022', '', '', NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological', NULL, '2025-12-19 06:15:44.698369', '2025-12-19 06:15:44.698369', 'Technological', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(98, 'A.8.32', 'Change management for cryptographic controls', 'Changes to cryptographic controls shall be managed.', 'ISO/IEC 27001:2022', '', '', NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological', NULL, '2025-12-19 06:15:44.906915', '2025-12-19 06:15:44.906915', 'Technological', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(99, 'A.8.33', 'Test information', 'Test information shall be protected and controlled.', 'ISO/IEC 27001:2022', '', '', NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological', NULL, '2025-12-19 06:15:45.115378', '2025-12-19 06:15:45.115378', 'Technological', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4359, '14.1.1', 'Verify that the application build and deployment processes are performed in a secure and repeatable way, such as CI / CD automation, automated configuration management, and automated deployment scripts.', 'Verify that the application build and deployment processes are performed in a secure and repeatable way, such as CI / CD automation, automated configuration management, and automated deployment scripts.', 'ASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'ASVS, L1, L2', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:21.979727', '2026-02-06 13:43:21.979727', NULL, '**V14.1 Build and Deploy**

Build pipelines are the basis for repeatable security - every time something insecure is discovered, it can be resolved in the source code, build or deployment scripts, and tested automatically. We are strongly encouraging the use of build pipelines with automatic security and dependency checks that warn or break the build to prevent known security issues being deployed into production. Manual steps performed irregularly directly leads to avoidable security mistakes.

As the industry moves to a DevSecOps model, it is important to ensure the continued availability and integrity of deployment and configuration to achieve a "known good" state. In the past, if a system was hacked, it would take days to months to prove that no further intrusions had taken place. Today, with the advent of software defined infrastructure, rapid A/B deployments with zero downtime, and automated containerized builds, it is possible to automatically and continuously build, harden, and deploy a "known good" replacement for any compromised system.

If traditional models are still in place, then manual steps must be taken to harden and back up that configuration to allow the compromised systems to be quickly replaced with high integrity, uncompromised systems in a timely fashion.

Compliance with this section requires an automated build system, and access to build and deployment scripts.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4360, '14.1.3', 'Verify that server configuration is hardened as per the recommendations of the application server and frameworks in use.', 'Verify that server configuration is hardened as per the recommendations of the application server and frameworks in use.', 'ASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'ASVS, L1, L2', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:22.208184', '2026-02-06 13:43:22.208184', NULL, '**V14.1 Build and Deploy**

Build pipelines are the basis for repeatable security - every time something insecure is discovered, it can be resolved in the source code, build or deployment scripts, and tested automatically. We are strongly encouraging the use of build pipelines with automatic security and dependency checks that warn or break the build to prevent known security issues being deployed into production. Manual steps performed irregularly directly leads to avoidable security mistakes.

As the industry moves to a DevSecOps model, it is important to ensure the continued availability and integrity of deployment and configuration to achieve a "known good" state. In the past, if a system was hacked, it would take days to months to prove that no further intrusions had taken place. Today, with the advent of software defined infrastructure, rapid A/B deployments with zero downtime, and automated containerized builds, it is possible to automatically and continuously build, harden, and deploy a "known good" replacement for any compromised system.

If traditional models are still in place, then manual steps must be taken to harden and back up that configuration to allow the compromised systems to be quickly replaced with high integrity, uncompromised systems in a timely fashion.

Compliance with this section requires an automated build system, and access to build and deployment scripts.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(100, 'A.8.34', 'Protection of information systems from misuse', 'Information systems shall be protected from misuse.', 'ISO/IEC 27001:2022', '', '', NULL, 'active', 1, 'Technological', NULL, '2025-12-19 06:15:45.321391', '2025-12-19 06:15:45.321391', 'Technological', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(8, 'A.5.1', 'Policies for information security', 'Information security policy and topic-specific policies shall be defined, approved by management, published, communicated to and acknowledged by relevant personnel.', 'ISO/IEC 27001:2022', '', '', NULL, 'active', 3, 'Organisational', 'Information Security Policy', '2025-12-19 06:15:25.91783', '2025-12-19 06:15:25.91783', 'Organisational', '- **Define Information Security Policy:**
  - Identify the organization''s information security objectives and scope.
  - Develop a comprehensive information security policy that aligns with business goals and regulatory requirements.
  - Include key elements such as risk management, access control, data protection, and incident response.

- **Develop Topic-Specific Policies:**
  - Identify specific areas requiring detailed policies (e.g., data classification, mobile device management, remote access).
  - Draft policies addressing each specific topic, ensuring they support the overarching information security policy.

- **Approval by Management:**
  - Present the drafted policies to senior management for review.
  - Obtain formal approval from management, ensuring they understand and support the policies.

- **Publication of Policies:**
  - Store the approved policies in a centralized, accessible location (e.g., intranet, document management system).
  - Ensure that the policies are version-controlled and regularly updated.

- **Communication to Relevant Personnel:**
  - Develop a communication plan to inform all relevant personnel about the policies.
  - Use multiple channels (e.g., emails, meetings, training sessions) to disseminate the information.

- **Acknowledgment by Personnel:**
  - Implement a process for personnel to acknowledge their understanding and acceptance of the policies (e.g., electronic acknowledgment, signed documents).
  - Maintain records of acknowledgments for audit and compliance purposes.

- **Regular Review and Updates:**
  - Schedule regular reviews of the policies to ensure they remain relevant and effective.
  - Update the policies as necessary to reflect changes in the organization, technology, or regulatory environment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(17, 'A.5.10', 'Acceptable use of information and other associated assets', 'Rules for the acceptable use and procedures for handling information and other associated assets shall be identified and documented.', 'ISO/IEC 27001:2022', '', '', NULL, 'active', 2, 'Organisational', 'Information Security Policy', '2025-12-19 06:15:27.829153', '2025-12-19 06:15:27.829153', 'Organisational', '- **Identify Assets**:
  - Inventory all information and associated assets, including hardware, software, data, and communication devices.
  - Classify assets based on sensitivity, value, and criticality to the organization.

- **Define Acceptable Use**:
  - Develop a clear acceptable use policy (AUP) outlining permitted and prohibited actions for each type of asset.
  - Include guidelines on personal use, access controls, data sharing, and internet usage.

- **Document Procedures**:
  - Create detailed procedures for handling information, including data entry, processing, storage, transmission, and disposal.
  - Establish protocols for secure use of mobile devices and remote access.

- **Communicate and Train**:
  - Distribute the AUP and handling procedures to all employees and relevant third parties.
  - Conduct regular training sessions to ensure understanding and compliance with the policies.

- **Monitor and Enforce**:
  - Implement monitoring mechanisms to detect and respond to policy violations.
  - Define disciplinary actions for non-compliance and ensure they are consistently applied.

- **Review and Update**:
  - Regularly review the AUP and handling procedures to ensure they remain relevant and effective.
  - Update the policies and procedures in response to technological changes, new threats, or organizational changes.

- **Obtain Acknowledgment**:
  - Require employees and third parties to formally acknowledge their understanding and acceptance of the AUP and procedures.
  - Maintain records of acknowledgments for compliance verification.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4361, '14.1.5', 'Verify that authorized administrators can verify the integrity of all security-relevant configurations to detect tampering.', 'Verify that authorized administrators can verify the integrity of all security-relevant configurations to detect tampering.', 'ASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'ASVS, L1', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:22.434748', '2026-02-06 13:43:22.434748', NULL, '**V14.1 Build and Deploy**

