As the industry moves to a DevSecOps model, it is important to ensure the continued availability and integrity of deployment and configuration to achieve a "known good" state. In the past, if a system was hacked, it would take days to months to prove that no further intrusions had taken place. Today, with the advent of software defined infrastructure, rapid A/B deployments with zero downtime, and automated containerized builds, it is possible to automatically and continuously build, harden, and deploy a "known good" replacement for any compromised system.

If traditional models are still in place, then manual steps must be taken to harden and back up that configuration to allow the compromised systems to be quickly replaced with high integrity, uncompromised systems in a timely fashion.

Compliance with this section requires an automated build system, and access to build and deployment scripts.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4362, '14.3.2', 'Verify that web or application server and application framework debug modes are disabled in production to eliminate debug features, developer consoles, and unintended security disclosures.', 'Verify that web or application server and application framework debug modes are disabled in production to eliminate debug features, developer consoles, and unintended security disclosures.', 'ASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'ASVS, L1, L2, L3, CWE-497', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:22.660227', '2026-02-06 13:43:22.660227', NULL, '**V14.3 Unintended Security Disclosure**

Configurations for production should be hardened to protect against common attacks, such as debug consoles, raise the bar for Cross-site Scripting (XSS) and Remote File Inclusion (RFI) attacks, and to eliminate trivial information discovery "vulnerabilities" that are the unwelcome hallmark of many penetration testing reports. Many of these issues are rarely rated as a significant risk, but they are chained together with other vulnerabilities. If these issues are not present by default, it raises the bar before most attacks can succeed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4363, 'MASVS-AUTH-3', 'The app secures sensitive operations with additional authentication.', 'Some additional form of authentication is often desirable for sensitive actions inside the app. This can be done in different ways (biometric, pin, MFA code generator, email, deep links, etc) and they all need to be implemented securely.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Authentication and Authorization', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:25.912755', '2026-02-06 13:43:25.912755', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4364, 'MASVS-STORAGE-1', 'Sensitive Data Storage', 'Verify that sensitive data is not stored insecurely on the device.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Storage', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:26.149718', '2026-02-06 13:43:26.149718', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4365, 'MASVS-STORAGE-2', 'Log Sanitization', 'Verify that sensitive data is not leaked through system logs.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Storage', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:26.38524', '2026-02-06 13:43:26.38524', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4366, 'MASVS-CRYPTO-1', 'Key Management', 'Verify that cryptographic keys are managed securely using platform features (Keystore/Keychain).', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Cryptography', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:26.619253', '2026-02-06 13:43:26.619253', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4367, 'MASVS-CRYPTO-2', 'Strong Algorithms', 'Verify that only industry-standard, strong cryptographic algorithms are used.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Cryptography', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:26.876761', '2026-02-06 13:43:26.876761', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4368, 'MASVS-AUTH-1', 'Secure Authentication', 'Verify that authentication is performed securely and follows best practices.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Authentication and Authorization', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:27.108836', '2026-02-06 13:43:27.108836', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4369, 'MASVS-AUTH-2', 'Biometric Authentication', 'Verify that biometric authentication is implemented using platform-recommended APIs.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Authentication and Authorization', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:27.340817', '2026-02-06 13:43:27.340817', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4370, 'MASVS-NETWORK-1', 'TLS Configuration', 'Verify that all network communication is performed over a secure, up-to-date TLS connection.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Network Communication', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:27.577329', '2026-02-06 13:43:27.577329', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(9, 'A.5.2', 'Information security roles and responsibilities', 'Information security roles and responsibilities shall be defined and allocated according to the organization needs.', 'ISO/IEC 27001:2022', '', '', NULL, 'active', 2, 'Organisational', 'Information Security Policy', '2025-12-19 06:15:26.136156', '2025-12-19 06:15:26.136156', 'Organisational', '- **Conduct a Needs Assessment:**
  - Analyze the organization''s structure and operations to determine specific information security needs.
  - Identify critical areas where information security roles are essential.

- **Define Roles and Responsibilities:**
  - Develop a comprehensive list of information security roles required within the organization.
  - Clearly define the responsibilities and expectations for each role, ensuring alignment with organizational objectives.

- **Establish a RACI Matrix:**
  - Create a RACI (Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, Informed) matrix to map out roles and responsibilities for key information security activities.
  - Ensure that each activity has a designated responsible and accountable person.

- **Document Roles and Responsibilities:**
  - Formalize the defined roles and responsibilities in official documentation, such as job descriptions, policy documents, or an information security manual.
  - Ensure documentation is accessible to all relevant personnel.

- **Assign Roles:**
  - Allocate roles to qualified personnel, considering their skills, experience, and capacity.
  - Ensure that individuals understand their responsibilities and have the authority to perform their roles effectively.

- **Communicate and Train:**
  - Communicate the defined roles and responsibilities to all employees and relevant stakeholders.
  - Provide training to ensure that personnel understand their roles and how they contribute to the organization''s information security.

- **Review and Update Regularly:**
  - Periodically review roles and responsibilities to ensure they remain relevant to the organization''s evolving needs and external changes.
  - Update documentation and communicate changes as necessary.

- **Monitor and Evaluate:**
  - Implement mechanisms to monitor the effectiveness of the assigned roles and responsibilities.
  - Conduct regular evaluations and adjust roles or responsibilities if gaps or overlaps are identified.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3639, '12.1.2', '**Verify that** logs are stored in secure, access-controlled repositories with appropriate retention policies and backup procedures.', '**Verify that** logs are stored in secure, access-controlled repositories with appropriate retention policies and backup procedures.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:14.932729', '2026-02-04 23:49:14.932729', NULL, '**C12.1 Request & Response Logging**

', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3640, '12.1.3', '**Verify that** log storage systems implement encryption at rest and in transit to protect sensitive information contained in logs.', '**Verify that** log storage systems implement encryption at rest and in transit to protect sensitive information contained in logs.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:15.155788', '2026-02-04 23:49:15.155788', NULL, '**C12.1 Request & Response Logging**

', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4371, 'MASVS-PLATFORM-1', 'The app uses IPC mechanisms securely.', 'Apps typically use platform provided IPC mechanisms to intentionally expose data or functionality. Both installed apps and the user are able to interact with the app in many different ways. This control ensures that all interactions involving IPC mechanisms happen securely.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Platform Interaction', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:27.813024', '2026-02-06 13:43:27.813024', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4372, 'MASVS-NETWORK-2', 'Certificate Pinning', 'Verify that certificate pinning is implemented for high-security applications.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Network Communication', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:28.047424', '2026-02-06 13:43:28.047424', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(10, 'A.5.3', 'Segregation of duties', 'Conflicting duties and conflicting areas of responsibility shall be segregated.', 'ISO/IEC 27001:2022', '', '', NULL, 'active', 2, 'Organisational', 'Information Security Policy', '2025-12-19 06:15:26.34741', '2025-12-19 06:15:26.34741', 'Organisational', '- **Identify Conflicting Duties:**
  - Conduct a risk assessment to identify roles and responsibilities that could lead to conflicts of interest or fraud if not segregated.
  - Focus on critical processes such as financial transactions, access management, and data handling.

- **Define Roles and Responsibilities:**
  - Clearly document and define roles and responsibilities for each position within the organization.
  - Ensure that job descriptions reflect the segregation of duties to prevent conflicts.

- **Implement Segregation:**
  - Assign different individuals to roles that involve conflicting duties, such as authorization, execution, and review of transactions.
  - Use role-based access control (RBAC) to enforce segregation in IT systems.

- **Establish Approval Processes:**
  - Implement a system of checks and balances where critical tasks require approval from multiple individuals.
  - Ensure that no single individual has control over all phases of a critical process.

- **Monitor and Review:**
  - Regularly review access rights and role assignments to ensure compliance with segregation policies.
  - Conduct periodic audits to verify that segregation of duties is being maintained.

- **Implement Technical Controls:**
  - Use automated tools to monitor and alert on violations of segregation of duties.
  - Implement logging and monitoring to track activities and detect unauthorized actions.

- **Provide Training and Awareness:**
  - Educate employees about the importance of segregation of duties and how it protects the organization.
  - Conduct regular training sessions to reinforce policies and procedures related to segregation of duties.

- **Document and Communicate Policies:**
  - Develop and maintain a formal policy on segregation of duties.
  - Communicate the policy to all employees and ensure it is easily accessible.

- **Review and Update Regularly:**
  - Regularly review and update the segregation of duties policy to reflect changes in the organization or its processes.
  - Adapt to new threats or changes in the regulatory environment that may impact segregation requirements.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4373, 'MASVS-PLATFORM-2', 'The app uses WebViews securely.', 'WebViews are typically used by apps that have a need for increased control over the UI. This control ensures that WebViews are configured securely to prevent sensitive data leakage as well as sensitive functionality exposure (e.g. via JavaScript bridges to native code).', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Platform Interaction', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:28.283929', '2026-02-06 13:43:28.283929', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4374, 'MASVS-PLATFORM-3', 'The app uses the user interface securely.', 'Sensitive data has to be displayed in the UI in many situations (e.g. passwords, credit card details, OTP codes in notifications). This control ensures that this data doesn''t end up being unintentionally leaked due to platform mechanisms such as auto-generated screenshots or accidentally disclosed via e.g. shoulder surfing or sharing the device with another person.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Platform Interaction', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:28.517804', '2026-02-06 13:43:28.517804', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4375, 'MASVS-CODE-1', 'The app requires an up-to-date platform version.', 'Every release of the mobile OS includes security patches and new security features. By supporting older versions, apps stay vulnerable to well-known threats. This control ensures that the app is running on an up-to-date platform version so that users have the latest security protections.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Code Quality', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:28.751782', '2026-02-06 13:43:28.751782', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4376, 'MASVS-CODE-2', 'The app has a mechanism for enforcing app updates.', 'Sometimes critical vulnerabilities are discovered in the app when it is already in production. This control ensures that there is a mechanism to force the users to update the app before they can continue using it.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Code Quality', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:28.986001', '2026-02-06 13:43:28.986001', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4377, 'MASVS-CODE-3', 'The app only uses software components without known vulnerabilities.', 'To be truly secure, a full whitebox assessment should have been performed on all app components. However, as it usually happens with e.g. for third-party components this is not always feasible and not typically part of a penetration test. This control covers "low-hanging fruit" cases, such as those that can be detected just by scanning libraries for known vulnerabilities.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Code Quality', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:29.220705', '2026-02-06 13:43:29.220705', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4378, 'MASVS-CODE-4', 'The app validates and sanitizes all untrusted inputs.', 'Apps have many data entry points including the UI, IPC, the network, the file system, etc. This incoming data might have been inadvertently modified by untrusted actors and may lead to bypass of critical security checks as well as classical injection attacks such as SQL injection, XSS or insecure deserialization. This control ensures that this data is treated as untrusted input and is properly verified and sanitized before it''s used.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Code Quality', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:29.455322', '2026-02-06 13:43:29.455322', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4379, 'MASVS-RESILIENCE-1', 'The app validates the integrity of the platform.', 'Running on a platform that has been tampered with can be very dangerous for apps, as this may disable certain security features, putting the data of the app at risk. Trusting the platform is essential for many of the MASVS controls relying on the platform being secure (e.g. secure storage, biometrics, sandboxing, etc.). This control tries to validate that the OS has not been compromised and its security features can thus be trusted.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Resilience Against Reverse Engineering and Tampering', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:29.689261', '2026-02-06 13:43:29.689261', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4380, 'MASVS-RESILIENCE-2', 'The app implements anti-tampering mechanisms.', 'Apps run on a user-controlled device, and without proper protections it''s relatively easy to run a modified version locally (e.g. to cheat in a game, or enable premium features without paying), or upload a backdoored version of it to third-party app stores. This control tries to ensure the integrity of the app''s intended functionality by preventing modifications to the original code and resources.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Resilience Against Reverse Engineering and Tampering', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:29.924242', '2026-02-06 13:43:29.924242', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4381, 'MASVS-RESILIENCE-3', 'The app implements anti-static analysis mechanisms.', 'Understanding the internals of an app is typically the first step towards tampering with it (either dynamically, or statically). This control tries to impede comprehension by making it as difficult as possible to figure out how an app works using static analysis.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Resilience Against Reverse Engineering and Tampering', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:30.157272', '2026-02-06 13:43:30.157272', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4382, 'MASVS-RESILIENCE-4', 'The app implements anti-dynamic analysis techniques.', 'Sometimes pure static analysis is very difficult and time consuming so it typically goes hand in hand with dynamic analysis. Observing and manipulating an app during runtime makes it much easier to decipher its behavior. This control aims to make it as difficult as possible to perform dynamic analysis, as well as prevent dynamic instrumentation which could allow an attacker to modify the code at runtime.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Resilience Against Reverse Engineering and Tampering', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:30.392266', '2026-02-06 13:43:30.392266', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4383, 'MASVS-PRIVACY-1', 'The app minimizes access to sensitive data and resources.', '''Apps should only request access to the data they absolutely need for their functionality and always with informed consent from the user. This control ensures that apps practice data minimization and restricts access control, reducing the potential impact of data breaches or leaks.


      Furthermore, apps should share data with third parties only when necessary, and this should include enforcing that third-party SDKs operate based on user consent, not by default or without it. Apps should prevent third-party SDKs from ignoring consent signals or from collecting data before consent is confirmed.


      Additionally, apps should be aware of the ''''supply chain'''' of SDKs they incorporate, ensuring that no data is unnecessarily passed down their chain of dependencies. This end-to-end responsibility for data aligns with recent SBOM regulatory requirements, making apps more accountable for their data practices.''', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Privacy', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:30.631757', '2026-02-06 13:43:30.631757', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4384, 'MASVS-PRIVACY-2', 'The app prevents identification of the user.', '''Protecting user identity is crucial. This control emphasizes the use of unlinkability techniques like data abstraction, anonymization and pseudonymization to prevent user identification and tracking.


      Another key aspect addressed by this control is to establish technical barriers when employing complex ''''fingerprint-like'''' signals (e.g. device IDs, IP addresses, behavioral patterns) for specific purposes. For instance, a fingerprint used for fraud detection should be isolated and not repurposed for audience measurement in an analytics SDK. This ensures that each data stream serves its intended function without risking user privacy.''', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Privacy', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:30.866763', '2026-02-06 13:43:30.866763', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4385, 'MASVS-PRIVACY-3', 'The app is transparent about data collection and usage.', 'Users have the right to know how their data is being used. This control ensures that apps provide clear information about data collection, storage, and sharing practices, including any behavior a user wouldn''t reasonably expect, such as background data collection. Apps should also adhere to platform guidelines on data declarations.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Privacy', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:31.099263', '2026-02-06 13:43:31.099263', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4386, 'MASVS-PRIVACY-4', 'The app offers user control over their data.', 'Users should have control over their data. This control ensures that apps provide mechanisms for users to manage, delete, and modify their data, and change privacy settings as needed (e.g. to revoke consent). Additionally, apps should re-prompt for consent and update their transparency disclosures when they require more data than initially specified.', 'MASVS', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'MASVS, Privacy', NULL, '2026-02-06 13:43:31.334541', '2026-02-06 13:43:31.334541', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(50, 'A.6.6', 'Confidentiality or non-disclosure agreements', 'Confidentiality or non-disclosure agreements reflecting the organization''s needs shall be identified and signed.', 'ISO/IEC 27001:2022', '', '', NULL, 'active', 2, 'People', NULL, '2025-12-19 06:15:34.731244', '2025-12-19 06:15:34.731244', 'People', '**1. Identify Information Requiring Confidentiality**
*   Conduct an inventory of all sensitive information assets (e.g., customer data, source code, financial plans, trade secrets).
*   Classify this information based on its sensitivity (e.g., Confidential, Restricted) as defined in your information classification policy (A.8.2).

**2. Identify Parties Requiring an Agreement**
*   **Internal:** Employees, contractors, temporary staff, and board members.
*   **External:** Third-party suppliers, vendors, partners, consultants, and any party granted access to your confidential information.

**3. Develop and Maintain Formal Agreement Templates**
*   Create separate, legally-vetted templates for:
    *   **Employee/Internal Agreements:** Incorporated into employment contracts or as standalone documents.
    *   **Third-Party Agreements:** As part of supplier contracts or standalone NDAs.
*   Ensure agreements clearly define:
    *   What constitutes "Confidential Information."
    *   The obligations of the receiving party (e.g., use only for the defined purpose, protect from disclosure).
    *   The duration of the confidentiality obligation (e.g., term of agreement + 2-5 years, or indefinite for trade secrets).
    *   Permitted disclosures (e.g., if required by law).
    *   Return or destruction of information upon agreement termination.

**4. Implement a Formal Signing Process**
*   Integrate signing into onboarding processes for new employees and contractors.
*   Integrate signing into the procurement/third-party due diligence process before sharing any confidential information.
*   Maintain a central, up-to-date register of all signed agreements, including parties, effective date, and validity period.

**5. Review and Enforce Agreements**
*   Schedule periodic reviews (e.g., annually) of agreement templates to ensure legal and regulatory compliance.
*   Define and communicate consequences for breach of the agreement.
*   Upon termination of a relationship, proactively remind the party of their ongoing obligations and, if applicable, verify the return/destruction of your information.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3978, 'SAMM-STRATEGY-METRICS', 'Strategy & Metrics', 'Security Practice: Strategy & Metrics under Governance', 'SAMM', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Governance', NULL, '2026-02-05 00:27:19.790925', '2026-02-05 00:27:19.790925', 'SAMM', 'See OWASP SAMM (Maturity Model) for details.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4005, 'A03:2021', 'Injection', 'Injection', 'WEB-T10', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'WEB', NULL, '2026-02-05 00:27:26.053628', '2026-02-05 00:27:26.053628', 'WEB-T10', 'See OWASP Web Top 10 for details.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4040, 'A04:2025', 'Cryptographic Failures', '### Background
Focuses on failures related to the lack of cryptography, weak algorithms, or leaking of cryptographic keys. Notable CWEs: CWE-327, CWE-338 (Weak PRNG).

### Description
Failures to protect data at rest and in transit. This includes using old algorithms (MD5), insecure modes (ECB), or failing to validate server certificates.', 'WEB-T10', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Security', NULL, '2026-02-05 07:33:17.448', '2026-02-05 07:05:08.492749', 'owasp_top10', '### How to Prevent
- Classify data and encrypt sensitive assets at rest.
- Use authenticated encryption and strong standard algorithms (AES-GCM, Argon2).
- Disable unencrypted protocols (FTP, Telnet).
- Encrypt all data in transit with TLS 1.2+ and forward secrecy.
- Store passwords using strong adaptive hashing functions (Argon2, scrypt).
- Prepare for post-quantum cryptography (PQC).

### Example Attack Scenarios
- **Scenario #1**: An attacker on an insecure wireless network downgrades an HTTPS connection to HTTP and steals session cookies.
- **Scenario #2**: A password database using unsalted MD5 hashes is stolen; the attacker uses rainbow tables to recover all passwords in minutes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
Focuses on verifying software and data integrity at trust boundaries. Notable CWEs: CWE-502 (Insecure Deserialization), CWE-829 (Untrusted Control Sphere).

### Description
Code and infrastructure that does not protect against invalid or untrusted code/data. Includes unsigned updates and insecure deserialization (e.g., trusting serialized objects from the client).', 'WEB-T10', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Security', NULL, '2026-02-05 07:33:19.327', '2026-02-05 07:05:10.351935', 'owasp_top10', '### How to Prevent
- Use digital signatures to verify software and data sources.
- Host internal, vetted package repositories.
- Secure CI/CD pipelines with proper separation of duties.
- Do not use unsigned/unencrypted serialized data from untrusted clients.

### Example Attack Scenarios
- **Scenario #1**: An application uses a auto-update feature that downloads binary updates over HTTP without checking their digital signature. An attacker intercepts the request and serves a malicious update.
- **Scenario #2**: Insecure Deserialization where a Java object containing user privileges is serialized into a cookie; an attacker modifies the byte-stream to grant themselves admin rights.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4037, 'A01:2025', 'Broken Access Control', '### Background
Maintaining its position at #1, 100% of tested applications had some form of broken access control. Notable CWEs: CWE-200 (Exposure of Sensitive Information), CWE-918 (SSRF), CWE-352 (CSRF).

### Description
Access control enforces policy such that users cannot act outside of their intended permissions. Failures typically lead to unauthorized information disclosure, modification or destruction of all data, or performing a business function outside the user''s limits.', 'WEB-T10', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Security', NULL, '2026-02-05 07:33:16.034', '2026-02-05 07:05:07.090154', 'owasp_top10', '### How to Prevent
- Deny by default except for public resources.
- Implement access control mechanisms once and reuse them throughout the application.
- Model access controls should enforce record ownership.
- Disable web server directory listing and ensure file metadata (e.g., .git) are not present.
- Log access control failures and alert admins.
- Implement rate limits on API and controller access.

### Example Attack Scenarios
- **Scenario #1**: Changing the ''acct'' parameter in the URL (e.g., `?acct=12345` to `?acct=67890`) to view another user''s account details.
- **Scenario #2**: Forcing navigation to an admin page (e.g., `/app/admin_getappInfo`) as a regular user because the server fails to verify the session''s role.
- **Scenario #3**: Accessing administrative APIs directly via `curl` because the access control was only implemented in the frontend JavaScript.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4039, 'A03:2025', 'Software Supply Chain Failures', '### Background
Ranked #1 by 50% of community survey respondents. It includes all supply chain failures, not just ones involving known vulnerabilities. Notable CWEs: CWE-1104, CWE-1395.

### Description
Breakdowns in the process of building, distributing, or updating software. Often caused by malicious changes in third-party code, tools, or dependencies.', 'WEB-T10', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Security', NULL, '2026-02-05 07:33:16.977', '2026-02-05 07:05:08.031106', 'owasp_top10', '### How to Prevent
- Centrally manage a Software Bill of Materials (SBOM).
- Track direct and transitive dependencies continuously.
- Monitor sources like CVE, NVD, and OSV for vulnerabilities.
- Only obtain components from official, trusted sources over secure links.
- Harden code repositories and build servers (MFA, signed builds).

### Example Attack Scenarios
- **Scenario #1**: SolarWinds (2019) compromise where a trusted vendor''s update was injected with malware.
- **Scenario #2**: Bybit hack (2025) involving wallet software that only behaved maliciously under specific target conditions.
- **Scenario #3**: NPM worm (Shai-Hulud, 2025) which used post-install scripts to exfiltrate developer tokens and spread to other packages.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4042, 'A06:2025', 'Insecure Design', '### Background
Focuses on design and architectural flaws. Introduced in 2021. Notable CWEs: CWE-269 (Improper Privilege Management), CWE-434 (Unrestricted File Upload).

### Description
Insecure design is ''missing or ineffective control design''. An insecure design cannot be fixed by a perfect implementation because the necessary controls were never conceived.', 'WEB-T10', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Security', NULL, '2026-02-05 07:33:18.389', '2026-02-05 07:05:09.418178', 'owasp_top10', '### How to Prevent
- Use threat modeling for critical parts of the application.
- Integrate security language into user stories.
- Establish a library of secure design patterns or ''paved roads''.
- Segregate tenants robustly by design throughout all tiers.
- Write unit and integration tests to validate security requirements.

### Example Attack Scenarios
- **Scenario #1**: A cinema booking system has a 15-ticket limit for discounts but lacks protection against an attacker booking 600 seats across 40 theaters in seconds to disrupt revenue.
- **Scenario #2**: A web app uses ''secret questions'' for password recovery, which are easily guessable or found on social media (NIST 800-63b prohibited).
- **Scenario #3**: An e-commerce site lacks anti-bot design, allowing scalpers to buy high-end video cards instantly on release.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(1494, 'AC-2', 'Account Management', 'The organization identifies and selects the following types of information system accounts to support organizational missions/business functions: 

[Assignment: organization-defined information system account types]; assigns account managers for information system accounts; establishes conditions for group and role membership; specifies authorized users of the information system, group and role membership, and access authorizations (i.e., privileges) and other attributes (as required) for each account; requires approvals by 

[Assignment: organization-defined personnel or roles] for requests to create information system accounts; creates, enables, modifies, disables, and removes information system accounts in accordance with 

[Assignment: organization-defined procedures or conditions]; monitors the use of information system accounts; notifies account managers when accounts are no longer required, when users are terminated or transferred, and when individual information system usage or need-to-know changes; authorizes access to the information system based on a valid access authorization, intended system usage, and other attributes as required by the organization or associated mission/business functions; reviews accounts for compliance with account management requirements 

[Assignment: organization-defined frequency]; and establishes a process for reissuing shared/group account credentials (if deployed) when individuals are removed from the group.', 'NIST 800-53', '', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 6, 'Access Control', NULL, '2026-02-13 12:42:38.269', '2026-01-09 09:38:05.354048', 'AC', 'Examples of system account types include individual, shared, group, system, guest, anonymous, emergency, developer, temporary, and service. Identification of authorized system users and the specification of access privileges reflect the requirements in other controls in the security plan. Users requiring administrative privileges on system accounts receive additional scrutiny by organizational personnel responsible for approving such accounts and privileged access, including system owner, mission or business owner, senior agency information security officer, or senior agency official for privacy. Types of accounts that organizations may wish to prohibit due to increased risk include shared, group, emergency, anonymous, temporary, and guest accounts.

Where access involves personally identifiable information, security programs collaborate with the senior agency official for privacy to establish the specific conditions for group and role membership; specify authorized users, group and role membership, and access authorizations for each account; and create, adjust, or remove system accounts in accordance with organizational policies. Policies can include such information as account expiration dates or other factors that trigger the disabling of accounts. Organizations may choose to define access privileges or other attributes by account, type of account, or a combination of the two. Examples of other attributes required for authorizing access include restrictions on time of day, day of week, and point of origin. In defining other system account attributes, organizations consider system-related requirements and mission/business requirements. Failure to consider these factors could affect system availability.

Temporary and emergency accounts are intended for short-term use. Organizations establish temporary accounts as part of normal account activation procedures when there is a need for short-term accounts without the demand for immediacy in account activation. Organizations establish emergency accounts in response to crisis situations and with the need for rapid account activation. Therefore, emergency account activation may bypass normal account authorization processes. Emergency and temporary accounts are not to be confused with infrequently used accounts, including local logon accounts used for special tasks or when network resources are unavailable (may also be known as accounts of last resort). Such accounts remain available and are not subject to automatic disabling or removal dates. Conditions for disabling or deactivating accounts include when shared/group, emergency, or temporary accounts are no longer required and when individuals are transferred or terminated. Changing shared/group authenticators when members leave the group is intended to ensure that former group members do not retain access to the shared or group account. Some types of system accounts may require specialized training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4046, 'A10:2025', 'Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions', '### Background
New for 2025. Contains 24 CWEs. Notable CWEs: CWE-209 (Generation of Error Message with Sensitive Info), CWE-636 (Not Failing Securely).

### Description
When programs fail to prevent, detect, and respond to unusual situations, leading to crashes, unknown states, or vulnerabilities (failing open instead of closed).', 'WEB-T10', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Security', NULL, '2026-02-05 07:33:20.27', '2026-02-05 07:05:11.296251', 'owasp_top10', '### How to Prevent
- Catch exceptions directly and roll back transactions (fail closed).
- Implement a global exception handler for unexpected cases.
- Use rate limiting to prevent resource exhaustion from repeatedly triggered errors.
- Provide generic error messages to users while logging details internally.

### Example Attack Scenarios
- **Scenario #1**: Resource exhaustion where an exception is caught but a database connection isn''t released. An attacker triggers 100 errors to lock the entire pool, causing a DoS.
- **Scenario #2**: A financial transaction is interrupted by a network error after the debit but before the credit. The system fails to roll back, causing a loss of funds.
- **Scenario #3**: A system ''fails open'' when it cannot reach the LDAP server, granting access to anyone because the default behavior was ''permit'' if the check crashed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4000, 'API8:2023', 'Security Misconfiguration', '### Description
Complex configurations, default credentials, verbose error messages, or insecure TLS settings in the API infrastructure.', 'API-T10', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Security', NULL, '2026-02-05 07:33:24.499', '2026-02-05 00:27:24.753455', 'owasp_api_top10', '### How to Prevent
- Automate security configuration verification.
- Disable debug modes in production.
- Implement strict Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) policies.

### Example Attack Scenarios
- **Scenario #1**: An API gateway is left with the default admin password, allowing an attacker to reroute traffic to their own malicious server.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2711, '1.3.11', 'Verify that the application sanitizes user input before passing to mail systems to protect against SMTP or IMAP injection.', 'Verify that the application sanitizes user input before passing to mail systems to protect against SMTP or IMAP injection.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V1: Encoding and Sanitization', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:36.439', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.109604', 'V1.3: Sanitization', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2778, '4.4.4', 'Verify that dedicated WebSocket session management tokens are initially obtained or validated through the previously authenticated HTTPS session when transitioning an existing HTTPS session to a WebSocket channel.', 'Verify that dedicated WebSocket session management tokens are initially obtained or validated through the previously authenticated HTTPS session when transitioning an existing HTTPS session to a WebSocket channel.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V4: API and Web Service', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.292', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V4.4: WebSocket', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2811, '6.3.5', 'Verify that users are notified of suspicious authentication attempts (successful or unsuccessful). This may include authentication attempts from an unusual location or client, partially successful authentication (only one of multiple factors), an aut', 'Verify that users are notified of suspicious authentication attempts (successful or unsuccessful). This may include authentication attempts from an unusual location or client, partially successful authentication (only one of multiple factors), an authentication attempt after a long period of inactivity or a successful authentication after several unsuccessful attempts.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.3: General Authentication Security', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2837, '6.8.3', 'Verify that SAML assertions are uniquely processed and used only once within the validity period to prevent replay attacks.', 'Verify that SAML assertions are uniquely processed and used only once within the validity period to prevent replay attacks.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.082', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.8: Authentication with an Identity Provider', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2838, '6.8.4', 'Verify that, if an application uses a separate Identity Provider (IdP) and expects specific authentication strength, methods, or recentness for specific functions, the application verifies this using the information returned by the IdP. For example, ', 'Verify that, if an application uses a separate Identity Provider (IdP) and expects specific authentication strength, methods, or recentness for specific functions, the application verifies this using the information returned by the IdP. For example, if OIDC is used, this might be achieved by validating ID Token claims such as ''acr'', ''amr'', and ''auth_time'' (if present). If the IdP does not provide this information, the application must have a documented fallback approach that assumes that the minimum strength authentication mechanism was used (for example, single-factor authentication using username and password).', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.082', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.8: Authentication with an Identity Provider', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2985, '15.1.2', 'Verify that an inventory catalog, such as software bill of materials (SBOM), is maintained of all third-party libraries in use, including verifying that components come from pre-defined, trusted, and continually maintained repositories.', 'Verify that an inventory catalog, such as software bill of materials (SBOM), is maintained of all third-party libraries in use, including verifying that components come from pre-defined, trusted, and continually maintained repositories.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V15: Secure Coding and Architecture', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:39.875', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.843074', 'V15.1: Secure Coding and Architecture Documentation', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2993, '15.2.5', 'Verify that the application implements additional protections around parts of the application which are documented as containing "dangerous functionality" or using third-party libraries considered to be "risky components". This could include techniqu', 'Verify that the application implements additional protections around parts of the application which are documented as containing "dangerous functionality" or using third-party libraries considered to be "risky components". This could include techniques such as sandboxing, encapsulation, containerization or network level isolation to delay and deter attackers who compromise one part of an application from pivoting elsewhere in the application.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V15: Secure Coding and Architecture', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:40.124', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.962615', 'V15.2: Security Architecture and Dependencies', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3012, '16.3.2', 'Verify that failed authorization attempts are logged. For L3, this must include logging all authorization decisions, including logging when sensitive data is accessed (without logging the sensitive data itself).', 'Verify that failed authorization attempts are logged. For L3, this must include logging all authorization decisions, including logging when sensitive data is accessed (without logging the sensitive data itself).', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V16: Security Logging and Error Handling', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:40.38', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.962615', 'V16.3: Security Events', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2762, '3.7.5', 'Verify that the application behaves as documented (such as warning the user or blocking access) if the browser used to access the application does not support the expected security features.', 'Verify that the application behaves as documented (such as warning the user or blocking access) if the browser used to access the application does not support the expected security features.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.032', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.7: Other Browser Security Considerations', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2704, '1.3.4', 'Verify that user-supplied Scalable Vector Graphics (SVG) scriptable content is validated or sanitized to contain only tags and attributes (such as draw graphics) that are safe for the application, e.g., do not contain scripts and foreignObject.', 'Verify that user-supplied Scalable Vector Graphics (SVG) scriptable content is validated or sanitized to contain only tags and attributes (such as draw graphics) that are safe for the application, e.g., do not contain scripts and foreignObject.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V1: Encoding and Sanitization', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:35.651', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.109604', 'V1.3: Sanitization', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2776, '4.4.2', 'Verify that, during the initial HTTP WebSocket handshake, the Origin header field is checked against a list of origins allowed for the application.', 'Verify that, during the initial HTTP WebSocket handshake, the Origin header field is checked against a list of origins allowed for the application.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V4: API and Web Service', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.292', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V4.4: WebSocket', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2707, '1.3.7', 'Verify that the application protects against template injection attacks by not allowing templates to be built based on untrusted input. Where there is no alternative, any untrusted input being included dynamically during template creation must be san', 'Verify that the application protects against template injection attacks by not allowing templates to be built based on untrusted input. Where there is no alternative, any untrusted input being included dynamically during template creation must be sanitized or strictly validated.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V1: Encoding and Sanitization', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:35.651', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.109604', 'V1.3: Sanitization', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2775, '4.4.1', 'Verify that WebSocket over TLS (WSS) is used for all WebSocket connections.', 'Verify that WebSocket over TLS (WSS) is used for all WebSocket connections.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V4: API and Web Service', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.292', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V4.4: WebSocket', 'Applicable Levels: L1, L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2706, '1.3.6', 'Verify that the application protects against Server-side Request Forgery (SSRF) attacks, by validating untrusted data against an allowlist of protocols, domains, paths and ports and sanitizing potentially dangerous characters before using the data to', 'Verify that the application protects against Server-side Request Forgery (SSRF) attacks, by validating untrusted data against an allowlist of protocols, domains, paths and ports and sanitizing potentially dangerous characters before using the data to call another service.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V1: Encoding and Sanitization', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:35.651', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.109604', 'V1.3: Sanitization', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2708, '1.3.8', 'Verify that the application appropriately sanitizes untrusted input before use in Java Naming and Directory Interface (JNDI) queries and that JNDI is configured securely to prevent JNDI injection attacks.', 'Verify that the application appropriately sanitizes untrusted input before use in Java Naming and Directory Interface (JNDI) queries and that JNDI is configured securely to prevent JNDI injection attacks.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V1: Encoding and Sanitization', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:35.651', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.109604', 'V1.3: Sanitization', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2709, '1.3.9', 'Verify that the application sanitizes content before it is sent to memcache to prevent injection attacks.', 'Verify that the application sanitizes content before it is sent to memcache to prevent injection attacks.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V1: Encoding and Sanitization', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:36.439', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.109604', 'V1.3: Sanitization', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2728, '2.3.4', 'Verify that business logic level locking mechanisms are used to ensure that limited quantity resources (such as theater seats or delivery slots) cannot be double-booked by manipulating the application''s logic.', 'Verify that business logic level locking mechanisms are used to ensure that limited quantity resources (such as theater seats or delivery slots) cannot be double-booked by manipulating the application''s logic.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V2: Validation and Business Logic', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:36.44', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.109604', 'V2.3: Business Logic Security', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2729, '2.3.5', 'Verify that high-value business logic flows require multi-user approval to prevent unauthorized or accidental actions. This could include but is not limited to large monetary transfers, contract approvals, access to classified information, or safety ', 'Verify that high-value business logic flows require multi-user approval to prevent unauthorized or accidental actions. This could include but is not limited to large monetary transfers, contract approvals, access to classified information, or safety overrides in manufacturing.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V2: Validation and Business Logic', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:36.767', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.109604', 'V2.3: Business Logic Security', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3658, '12.5.2', '**Verify that** incident response teams have access to AI-specific forensic tools and expertise to investigate model behavior and attack vectors.', '**Verify that** incident response teams have access to AI-specific forensic tools and expertise to investigate model behavior and attack vectors.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:19.146811', '2026-02-04 23:49:19.146811', NULL, '**C12.5 AI Incident Response Planning & Execution**

', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(3659, '12.5.3', '**Verify that** post-incident analysis includes model retraining considerations, safety filter updates, and lessons learned integration into security controls.', '**Verify that** post-incident analysis includes model retraining considerations, safety filter updates, and lessons learned integration into security controls.', 'OWASP AISVS (AI Security)', NULL, 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-04 23:49:19.365325', '2026-02-04 23:49:19.365325', NULL, '**C12.5 AI Incident Response Planning & Execution**

', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2740, '3.3.5', 'Verify that when the application writes a cookie, the cookie name and value length combined are not over 4096 bytes. Overly large cookies will not be stored by the browser and therefore not sent with requests, preventing the user from using applicati', 'Verify that when the application writes a cookie, the cookie name and value length combined are not over 4096 bytes. Overly large cookies will not be stored by the browser and therefore not sent with requests, preventing the user from using application functionality which relies on that cookie.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:36.767', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.3: Cookie Setup', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2823, '6.5.3', 'Verify that lookup secrets, out-of-band authentication code, and time-based one-time password seeds, are generated using a Cryptographically Secure Pseudorandom Number Generator (CSPRNG) to avoid predictable values.', 'Verify that lookup secrets, out-of-band authentication code, and time-based one-time password seeds, are generated using a Cryptographically Secure Pseudorandom Number Generator (CSPRNG) to avoid predictable values.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.5: General Multi-factor authentication requirements', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2836, '6.8.2', 'Verify that the presence and integrity of digital signatures on authentication assertions (for example on JWTs or SAML assertions) are always validated, rejecting any assertions that are unsigned or have invalid signatures.', 'Verify that the presence and integrity of digital signatures on authentication assertions (for example on JWTs or SAML assertions) are always validated, rejecting any assertions that are unsigned or have invalid signatures.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.082', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.8: Authentication with an Identity Provider', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2898, '10.4.11', 'Verify that the authorization server configuration only assigns the required scopes to the OAuth client.', 'Verify that the authorization server configuration only assigns the required scopes to the OAuth client.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V10: OAuth and OIDC', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:38.855', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.720253', 'V10.4: OAuth Authorization Server', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2761, '3.7.4', 'Verify that the application''s top-level domain (e.g., site.tld) is added to the public preload list for HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS). This ensures that the use of TLS for the application is built directly into the main browsers, rather than ', 'Verify that the application''s top-level domain (e.g., site.tld) is added to the public preload list for HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS). This ensures that the use of TLS for the application is built directly into the main browsers, rather than relying only on the Strict-Transport-Security response header field.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V3: Web Frontend Security', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.032', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.343175', 'V3.7: Other Browser Security Considerations', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2702, '1.3.2', 'Verify that the application avoids the use of eval() or other dynamic code execution features such as Spring Expression Language (SpEL). Where there is no alternative, any user input being included must be sanitized before being executed.', 'Verify that the application avoids the use of eval() or other dynamic code execution features such as Spring Expression Language (SpEL). Where there is no alternative, any user input being included must be sanitized before being executed.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V1: Encoding and Sanitization', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:35.651', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.109604', 'V1.3: Sanitization', 'Applicable Levels: L1, L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2700, '1.2.10', 'Verify that the application is protected against CSV and Formula Injection. The application must follow the escaping rules defined in RFC 4180 sections 2.6 and 2.7 when exporting CSV content. Additionally, when exporting to CSV or other spreadsheet f', 'Verify that the application is protected against CSV and Formula Injection. The application must follow the escaping rules defined in RFC 4180 sections 2.6 and 2.7 when exporting CSV content. Additionally, when exporting to CSV or other spreadsheet formats (such as XLS, XLSX, or ODF), special characters (including ''='', ''+'', ''-'', ''@'', ''\t'' (tab), and ''\0'' (null character)) must be escaped with a single quote if they appear as the first character in a field value.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V1: Encoding and Sanitization', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:35.651', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.109604', 'V1.2: Injection Prevention', 'Applicable Levels: L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(2822, '6.5.2', 'Verify that, when being stored in the application''s backend, lookup secrets with less than 112 bits of entropy (19 random alphanumeric characters or 34 random digits) are hashed with an approved password storage hashing algorithm that incorporates a ', 'Verify that, when being stored in the application''s backend, lookup secrets with less than 112 bits of entropy (19 random alphanumeric characters or 34 random digits) are hashed with an approved password storage hashing algorithm that incorporates a 32-bit random salt. A standard hash function can be used if the secret has 112 bits of entropy or more.', 'ASVS', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 5, 'V6: Authentication', NULL, '2026-01-30 08:52:37.829', '2026-01-09 10:46:12.470153', 'V6.5: General Multi-factor authentication requirements', 'Applicable Levels: L2, L3', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4535, 'GV.OC-01', 'Organizational Context', 'The organizational mission, objectives, stakeholders, and legal, regulatory, and contractual requirements are understood and prioritized.', 'NIST CSF', 'Executive Management', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Govern', NULL, '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4536, 'ID.AM-01', 'Asset Management', 'Inventories of hardware, software, services, and data are maintained and managed.', 'NIST CSF', 'IT Manager', 'Quarterly', 'Log', 'active', 1, 'Identify', NULL, '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4537, 'ID.RA-01', 'Risk Assessment', 'Cybersecurity risks to the organization, assets, and individuals are identified and assessed.', 'NIST CSF', 'CISO', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Identify', NULL, '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4538, 'PR.AA-01', 'Identity Management & Access Control', 'Access to physical and logical assets is limited to authorized users, processes, and devices.', 'NIST CSF', 'IT Security', 'Monthly', 'Configuration', 'active', 1, 'Protect', NULL, '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4539, 'PR.DS-01', 'Data Security', 'Data is managed consistent with the organization''s risk strategy to protect the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of information.', 'NIST CSF', 'Data Privacy Officer', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Protect', NULL, '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4540, 'DE.CM-01', 'Continuous Monitoring', 'The information system and assets are monitored to identify cybersecurity events and verify the effectiveness of protective measures.', 'NIST CSF', 'SOC Lead', 'Daily', 'Log', 'active', 1, 'Detect', NULL, '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4541, 'RS.MA-01', 'Incident Management', 'Incident response processes and procedures are established, maintained, and exercised.', 'NIST CSF', 'Incident Response Team', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Respond', NULL, '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4542, 'RC.RP-01', 'Recovery Planning', 'Recovery processes and procedures are executed and maintained to ensure timely restoration of systems or assets affected by cybersecurity incidents.', 'NIST CSF', 'IT Operations', 'Annual', 'Document', 'active', 1, 'Recover', NULL, '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', '2026-03-09 17:07:36.934034', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4607, '21(2)(b)', 'Incident Handling', NULL, 'NIS2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'NIS2 Article 21', NULL, '2026-03-10 16:18:36.981', '2026-03-10 16:10:39.326', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Measures for incident handling, including prevention, detection, and response to incidents in a timely manner, and reporting obligations to authorities.', 'Entities must maintain continuous monitoring of their systems. An Incident Response Plan (IRP) must be in place defining roles, communication channels, and technical recovery steps. Note that significant incidents must be reported: an early warning within 24 hours and a full notification within 72 hours.', '"[{\"name\":\"Incident Management & Response Plan\",\"description\":\"Step-by-step procedures for handling different types of security incidents.\",\"source\":\"ENISA Technical Measure 3.1\"},{\"name\":\"Incident Register/Log (Live)\",\"description\":\"Record of all security events, their triage status, and final resolution details.\",\"source\":\"ISO 27001:2022 A.5.24\"},{\"name\":\"Notification & Reporting Process\",\"description\":\"Evidence of the existence of a process for reporting to CSIRT/National Authorities.\",\"source\":\"NIS2 Directive Art 23\"}]"'),
	(4608, '21(2)(c)', 'Business Continuity & Crisis Management', NULL, 'NIS2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'NIS2 Article 21', NULL, '2026-03-10 16:18:37.225', '2026-03-10 16:10:39.561', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Business continuity management ensuring the availability of services during and after an incident. This includes backup management, disaster recovery, and crisis management frameworks.', 'Resilience requires both technical and organizational measures. You must have redundant backups (offline/immutable preferred), a Disaster Recovery Plan for critical IT systems, and a Crisis Management Team (CMT) capable of handling major disruptions.', '"[{\"name\":\"Business Continuity Plan (BCP)\",\"description\":\"Strategic document defining the organization''s response to major service failures.\",\"source\":\"ISO 22301\"},{\"name\":\"Disaster Recovery Test Results\",\"description\":\"Logs proving that IT systems (DRP) were tested and recovered within the target RTO.\",\"source\":\"ENISA Technical Measure 4.1\"},{\"name\":\"Backup Policy & Restore Logs\",\"description\":\"Verification that backups are performed daily and restore tests are successful.\",\"source\":\"ISO 27001:2022 A.8.13\"}]"'),
	(4609, '21(2)(d)', 'Supply Chain Security', NULL, 'NIS2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'NIS2 Article 21', NULL, '2026-03-10 16:18:37.438', '2026-03-10 16:10:39.804', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Security in relationships with direct suppliers or service providers, specifically those providing ICT services and critical components.', 'The directive forces entities to take responsibility for their supply chain. This means performing security due diligence before onboarding a vendor (e.g. Cloud, MSP, Software) and ensuring security obligations are part of the legal contract.', '"[{\"name\":\"Third-Party Security Risk Management (TPRM) Policy\",\"description\":\"Defines risk thresholds and assessment criteria for external providers.\",\"source\":\"ENISA Technical Measure 5.1\"},{\"name\":\"Registry of Critical Suppliers & Assessments\",\"description\":\"A list of Tier 1 suppliers with updated security audits or certificates (SOC2/ISO).\",\"source\":\"ISO 27001:2022 A.5.19\"},{\"name\":\"Standard Security Clauses in Vendor Contracts\",\"description\":\"Legal templates requiring suppliers to report incidents and maintain security.\",\"source\":\"NIS2 Art 21(2)(d)\"}]"'),
	(4611, '21(2)(f)', 'Effectiveness & Compliance Monitoring', NULL, 'NIS2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'NIS2 Article 21', NULL, '2026-03-10 16:18:37.847', '2026-03-10 16:10:40.28', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Policies and procedures to evaluate the effectiveness of the cybersecurity risk-management measures implemented.', 'You cannot manage what you do not measure. Entities must conduct regular internal audits and security assessments (like penetration tests) to verify that the security program is effective and legally compliant with the Directive.', '"[{\"name\":\"Annual Internal Security Audit Report\",\"description\":\"Review of control compliance against the internal security policy framework.\",\"source\":\"ISO 27001:2022 CL 9.2\"},{\"name\":\"External Penetration Testing Report\",\"description\":\"Results from a recent professional security assessment and the remediation status.\",\"source\":\"ENISA Technical Measure 7.1\"},{\"name\":\"Security KPI & Performance Metric Reports\",\"description\":\"Quarterly reviews of security performance presented to executive management.\",\"source\":\"NIS2 Art 21(2)(f)\"}]"'),
	(4612, '21(2)(g)', 'Cyber Hygiene & Mandatory Training', NULL, 'NIS2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'NIS2 Article 21', NULL, '2026-03-10 16:18:38.055', '2026-03-10 16:10:40.537', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Basic cyber hygiene practices and cybersecurity training for all employees, including the management and board of directors.', 'Cyber hygiene includes least-privilege access, regular software updates, and secure device configuration. Training must be ongoing and mandatory, ensuring every staff member knows how to spot phishing and report security concerns.', '"[{\"name\":\"Training Attendance & Compliance Records\",\"description\":\"Employee logs showing 100% completion of annual security awareness training.\",\"source\":\"ISO 27001:2022 A.6.3\"},{\"name\":\"Management Education Records\",\"description\":\"Evidence that board members and management have been trained on NIS2 obligations.\",\"source\":\"NIS2 Art 20(2)\"},{\"name\":\"Cyber Hygiene Policy / Manual\",\"description\":\"Instructions for staff on password security, phishing, and workstation locking.\",\"source\":\"ENISA Technical Measure 8.1\"}]"'),
	(4613, '21(2)(h)', 'Cryptography & Data Protection', NULL, 'NIS2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'NIS2 Article 21', NULL, '2026-03-10 16:18:38.258', '2026-03-10 16:10:40.783', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Policies and procedures regarding the use of cryptography and, where appropriate, encryption for sensitive data at rest and in transit.', 'Encryption is a key technical safeguard. Policies must define required algorithms, key handling, and encryption requirements for laptops, databases, and portable media. Public communications must be secured using modern TLS versions.', '"[{\"name\":\"Cryptographic Control Policy\",\"description\":\"Standard defining approved encryption protocols and key rotation cycles.\",\"source\":\"ISO 27001:2022 A.8.24\"},{\"name\":\"Key Management Standard Operating Procedure\",\"description\":\"Workflow for generating, protecting, and archiving cryptographic keys.\",\"source\":\"ENISA Technical Measure 9.1\"},{\"name\":\"Inventory of Encrypted Assets\",\"description\":\"Record of encrypted databases, laptops, and backups protecting sensitive info.\",\"source\":\"ISO 27001:2022 A.8.1\"}]"'),
	(4614, '21(2)(i)', 'HR Security, Access Control & Asset Management', NULL, 'NIS2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'NIS2 Article 21', NULL, '2026-03-10 16:18:38.477', '2026-03-10 16:10:41.016', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Managing the security of human resources (onboarding/offboarding), implementing strict access control, and maintaining an accurate asset inventory.', 'Entities must know what they have (Asset Management) and who has access to it. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) should ensure ''least privilege''. HR processes must include security background checks (where legal) and immediate revocation of access upon termination.', '"[{\"name\":\"Privileged Access Review Log\",\"description\":\"Record of quarterly reviews ensuring administrator rights are limited to current needs.\",\"source\":\"ENISA Technical Measure 10.1\"},{\"name\":\"Comprehensive Asset Register\",\"description\":\"Electronic inventory of all hardware, virtual servers, and critical software.\",\"source\":\"ISO 27001:2022 A.5.9\"},{\"name\":\"Employee Offboarding Checklist\",\"description\":\"Standard procedure ensuring keys, tokens, and access are removed upon exit.\",\"source\":\"ISO 27001:2022 A.6.5\"}]"'),
	(4615, '21(2)(j)', 'MFA & Secure Communications', NULL, 'NIS2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'NIS2 Article 21', NULL, '2026-03-10 16:18:38.694', '2026-03-10 16:10:41.248', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Mandatory use of multi-factor authentication (MFA) or continuous authentication, and secured voice, video and text communications.', 'MFA is the single most effective technical defense. It must be enforced for all remote access (VPN, SaaS) and privileged administrator access. Corporate communications (email, VoIP) must be secured using specialized transit security.', '"[{\"name\":\"MFA Enforcement Configuration Report\",\"description\":\"System screenshot or report proving MFA is forced for all users in the Identity Provider.\",\"source\":\"ISO 27001:2022 A.8.5\"},{\"name\":\"Security Standard for Communications\",\"description\":\"Configuration requirements for secure email gateways and encrypted VoIP.\",\"source\":\"ENISA Technical Measure 11.2\"},{\"name\":\"Emergency Out-of-Band Communication Plan\",\"description\":\"Plan for securing communications during a total infrastructure failure.\",\"source\":\"NIS2 Art 21(2)(j)\"}]"'),
	(4606, '21(2)(a)', 'Risk Management & Security Policies', NULL, 'NIS2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'NIS2 Article 21', NULL, '2026-03-10 16:18:36.765', '2026-03-10 16:10:39.065', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Policies on risk analysis and information system security. This includes the establishment of a formal information security management system (ISMS) that governs how the entity identifies, assesses, and treats cybersecurity risks.', 'Compliance requires the formal adoption of an Information Security Policy approved by senior management. Risk assessments must be performed using a documented methodology and cover all network and information systems used in providing essential or important services. Policies must address confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data and services.', '"[{\"name\":\"Information Security Policy (Approved)\",\"description\":\"Top-level management-approved policy defining security objectives and governance.\",\"source\":\"ISO 27001:2022 CL 5.1\"},{\"name\":\"Cybersecurity Risk Management Methodology\",\"description\":\"Formal document describing how risks are identified, measured, and managed.\",\"source\":\"ENISA Technical Measure 2.1\"},{\"name\":\"Latest Risk Assessment & Treatment Plan\",\"description\":\"Evidence that a risk assessment was conducted and treatment was approved.\",\"source\":\"NIS2 Art 21(2)(a)\"}]"'),
	(4610, '21(2)(e)', 'Secure SDLC & Vulnerability Management', NULL, 'NIS2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'NIS2 Article 21', NULL, '2026-03-10 16:18:37.648', '2026-03-10 16:10:40.045', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Security in network and information systems acquisition, development and maintenance, including the handling and disclosure of vulnerabilities.', 'Entities must implement a Coordinated Vulnerability Disclosure (CVD) process. Systems must be tested for security flaws before going live. Patch management processes must ensure that critical updates are deployed rapidly across the infrastructure.', '"[{\"name\":\"Vulnerability Disclosure Policy (VDP)\",\"description\":\"Publicly accessible document (e.g. security.txt) for reporting vulnerabilities.\",\"source\":\"ISO 29147\"},{\"name\":\"System Security Acquisition Standards\",\"description\":\"Checklists used during the purchase of hardware/software to ensure they meet security baselines.\",\"source\":\"ENISA Technical Measure 6.1\"},{\"name\":\"Scanning & Patching Audit Records\",\"description\":\"Reports showing internal/external vulnerability scans and patch application status.\",\"source\":\"ISO 27001:2022 A.8.14\"}]"'),
	(4616, '4.1', 'Understanding the organization and its context', 'The organization shall determine external and internal issues that are relevant to its purpose and that affect its ability to achieve the intended outcome(s) of its information security management system.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4617, '4.2', 'Understanding the needs and expectations of interested parties', 'The organization shall determine interested parties that are relevant to the information security management system and the requirements of these interested parties.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4618, '4.3', 'Determining the scope of the ISMS', 'The organization shall determine the boundaries and applicability of the information security management system to establish its scope.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4619, '4.4', 'Information security management system', 'The organization shall establish, implement, maintain and continually improve an information security management system, including the processes needed and their interactions, in accordance with the requirements of this document.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4620, '5.1_C', 'Leadership and commitment', 'Top management shall demonstrate leadership and commitment with respect to the information security management system.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4621, '5.2_C', 'Policy', 'Top management shall establish an information security policy.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4622, '5.3_C', 'Organizational roles, responsibilities and authorities', 'Top management shall ensure that the responsibilities and authorities for roles relevant to information security are assigned and communicated.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4623, '6.1.1_C', 'General - Actions to address risks and opportunities', 'When planning for the information security management system, the organization shall consider the issues referred to in 4.1 and the requirements referred to in 4.2 and determine the risks and opportunities that need to be addressed.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4624, '6.1.2_C', 'Information security risk assessment', 'The organization shall define and apply an information security risk assessment process.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4625, '6.1.3_C', 'Information security risk treatment', 'The organization shall define and apply an information security risk treatment process.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4626, '6.2_C', 'Information security objectives and planning to achieve them', 'The organization shall establish information security objectives at relevant functions and levels.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4627, '6.3_C', 'Planning of changes', 'When the organization determines the need for changes to the information security management system, the changes shall be carried out in a planned manner.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4628, '7.1_C', 'Resources', 'The organization shall determine and provide the resources needed for the establishment, implementation, maintenance and continual improvement of the information security management system.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4629, '7.2_C', 'Competence', 'The organization shall determine the necessary competence of person(s) doing work under its control that affects its information security performance.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4630, '7.3_C', 'Awareness', 'Persons doing work under the organization''s control shall be aware of the information security policy, their contribution to ISMS effectiveness, and the implications of not conforming to the ISMS requirements.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4631, '7.4_C', 'Communication', 'The organization shall determine the need for internal and external communications relevant to the information security management system.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4632, '7.5.1_C', 'General - Documented information', 'The organization''s information security management system shall include documented information required by this document and documented information determined by the organization as being necessary for the effectiveness of the ISMS.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4633, '7.5.2_C', 'Creating and updating', 'When creating and updating documented information, the organization shall ensure appropriate identification, format and review/approval.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4634, '7.5.3_C', 'Control of documented information', 'Documented information required by the information security management system and by this document shall be controlled to ensure it is available, suitable for use, and adequately protected.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4635, '8.1_C', 'Operational planning and control', 'The organization shall plan, implement and control the processes needed to meet information security requirements, and to implement the actions determined in Clause 6.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4636, '8.2_C', 'Information security risk assessment', 'The organization shall perform information security risk assessments at planned intervals or when significant changes are proposed or occur.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4637, '8.3_C', 'Information security risk treatment', 'The organization shall implement the information security risk treatment plan.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4638, '9.1', 'Monitoring, measurement, analysis and evaluation', 'The organization shall evaluate the information security performance and the effectiveness of the information security management system.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4639, '9.2.1', 'General - Internal audit', 'The organization shall conduct internal audits at planned intervals to provide information on whether the ISMS conforms to requirements and is effectively implemented.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4640, '9.2.2', 'Internal audit programme', 'The organization shall plan, establish, implement and maintain an audit programme(s).', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4641, '9.3.1', 'General - Management review', 'Top management shall review the organization''s information security management system at planned intervals to ensure its continuing suitability, adequacy and effectiveness.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4642, '9.3.2', 'Management review inputs', 'The management review shall include consideration of various inputs like status of previous actions, changes in issues, and feedback on performance.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4643, '9.3.3', 'Management review results', 'The results of the management review shall include decisions related to continual improvement opportunities and any need for changes to the ISMS.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4644, '10.1', 'Continual improvement', 'The organization shall continually improve the suitability, adequacy and effectiveness of the information security management system.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4645, '10.2', 'Nonconformity and corrective action', 'When a nonconformity occurs, the organization shall react, evaluate the need for action, and implement any action needed.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Management System Clauses', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4646, '5.11', 'Return of assets', 'Personnel and other interested parties as appropriate should return all organization’s assets in their possession upon change or termination of their employment, contract or agreement.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4647, '5.12', 'Classification of information', 'Information should be classified according to the information security needs of the organization based on confidentiality, integrity, availability and relevant interested party requirements.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4648, '5.13', 'Labelling of information', 'An appropriate set of procedures for labelling information should be developed and implemented in accordance with the information classification scheme adopted by the organization.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4649, '5.14', 'Information transfer', 'Information transfer rules, procedures or agreements should be in place for all types of transfer facilities within the organization and between the organization and other parties.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4650, '5.19', 'Information security in supplier relationships', 'Processes and procedures should be defined and implemented to manage the information security risks associated with the use of supplier''s products or services.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4651, '5.20', 'Addressing information security within supplier agreements', 'Relevant information security requirements should be established and agreed with each supplier that may access, process, store, communicate, or provide IT infrastructure components for, the organization''s information.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4652, '5.21', 'Managing information security in the ICT supply chain', 'Processes and procedures should be defined and implemented to manage the information security risks associated with the ICT products and services supply chain.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4653, '5.22', 'Monitoring, review and change management of supplier services', 'The organization should regularly monitor, review and audit supplier service delivery and security performance against the information security requirements in supplier agreements.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4654, '5.23', 'Information security for the use of cloud services', 'Processes for acquisition, use, management and exit from cloud services should be established in accordance with the organization''s information security requirements.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4655, '5.24', 'Information security incident management planning and preparation', 'The organization should plan and prepare for information security incident management by defining, establishing and communicating information security incident management processes, roles and responsibilities.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4656, '5.25', 'Management of information security incidents', 'Information security incidents should be managed by following the established processes.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4657, '5.26', 'Learning from information security incidents', 'Knowledge gained from information security incidents should be used to strengthen and improve the information security controls.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4658, '5.27', 'Collection of evidence', 'The organization should establish and implement procedures for the identification, collection, acquisition and preservation of evidence related to information security events.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4659, '5.28', 'Information security during disruption', 'The organization should plan how to maintain information security at an appropriate level during disruption.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4660, '5.29', 'Information security event reporting', 'Information security events should be reported through the identified reporting channels as quickly as possible.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4661, '5.30', 'ICT readiness for business continuity', 'ICT readiness should be planned, implemented, maintained and tested based on business continuity objectives and ICT continuity requirements.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	(4662, '5.31', 'Legal, statutory, regulatory and contractual requirements', 'Legal, statutory, regulatory and contractual requirements relevant to information security and the organization''s approach to satisfy these requirements should be identified, documented and kept up to date.', 'ISO 27001:2022', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'active', 1, 'Organizational Controls', NULL, '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', '2026-03-17 07:01:59.400931', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

