4,-0.03200294,0.01208377,0.03154288,0.028552487,0.034562025,-0.0013208761,0.010768285,0.005916087,0.015196364,-0.03177291,0.042124264,0.0011627304,-0.0108833,-0.0027747382,0.03482081,-0.023247419,-0.021594077,-0.0026453463,0.0010809619,-0.012565395,0.024828875,0.0016892836,-0.0062467554,-0.022197906,0.039996486,0.0071596876,-0.009215581,-0.02494389,0.026381578,-0.0029850001,0.010236341,0.012270669,0.02540395,0.0063725533,-0.023836872,-0.0063258284,0.02531769,1.1547837e-06,-0.014793812,-0.037408646,0.0016407617,0.004413703,-0.007936039,0.005959218,0.011357737,0.0147794355,-0.006473191,0.00038817583,0.025720242,0.006340205,0.12571146,-0.01610211,-0.026769755,-0.0026345637,0.014240302,-0.017223505,0.0066852504,-0.011487129,-0.023995016,-0.019351283,0.029673886,0.008108562,-0.0075838054,0.052130576,0.00197143,-0.0027927095,0.00020116403,0.01531138,0.021953499,-0.017209128,-0.015713932,0.0038062795,0.027632369,0.018733077,0.011832174,0.0029041301,0.04126165,-0.009927237,-0.031169081,0.020415174,-0.007727574,-0.011889682,0.022284167,-0.033124335,0.02024265,-0.043360677,0.010581385,0.009043059,-0.03878883,-0.0029778117,-0.015167611,0.006027508,0.014261867,-1.1603997e-05,-0.007526298,0.0028448256,-0.024728237,-0.003730801,0.030277714,0.0018438351,0.027502976,-0.024110032,-0.019566936,-0.03634476,-0.002070271,0.03352689,0.018330526,-0.007156093,-0.020573318,0.00044366161,0.016274631,-0.0008046561,-0.028135559,0.010825792,-0.018459916]', 3, 'Physical and Environmental Security Policy 123 <h2>Purpose</h2>
<p>This policy establishes requirements for protecting Intellfence&#39;s physical premises, equipment, and information from unauthorized access, damage, and environmental threats. It ensures compliance with relevant industry standards such as SOC 2 and ISO/IEC 27001, which are critical for safeguarding sensitive information and maintaining operational integrity.</p>
<h2>Scope</h2>
<p>This policy applies to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Office facilities and data centers</li>
<li>Server rooms and network closets</li>
<li>Equipment and devices</li>
<li>Visitors and contractors</li>
<li>Environmental controls</li>
</ul>
<h2>Physical Security Perimeter</h2>
<h2>Security Zones</h2>
<p>Zone</p>
<p>Description</p>
<p>Access Control</p>
<p>Public</p>
<p>Reception, lobby</p>
<p>Open access</p>
<p>General</p>
<p>Office areas</p>
<p>Badge access</p>
<p>Restricted</p>
<p>Server rooms, executive areas</p>
<p>Badge + PIN</p>
<p>High Security</p>
<p>Data center, vault</p>
<p>Biometric + escort</p>
<h2>Perimeter Controls</h2>
<ul>
<li>Exterior doors with electronic locks</li>
<li>Security cameras at entry points, monitored 24/7</li>
<li>Intrusion detection systems integrated with alarm services</li>
<li>Security lighting with motion sensors</li>
</ul>
<h2>Access Control</h2>
<ul>
<li>All employees must wear visible ID badges at all times</li>
<li>Visitors must sign in and be escorted by an authorized employee</li>
<li>Access badges must not be shared; sharing is subject to disciplinary action</li>
<li>Lost badges must be reported immediately for revocation and re-issuance</li>
<li>Access rights must be reviewed and audited quarterly to comply with SOC 2 controls</li>
<li>Terminated employee badges must be deactivated on the same day as termination</li>
</ul>
<h2>Equipment Security</h2>
<ul>
<li>Servers must be housed in locked racks, accessible only by authorized personnel</li>
<li>Laptops must use cable locks when unattended and be encrypted as per company standards</li>
<li>Mobile devices must have remote wipe capability and comply with the company’s MDM policies</li>
<li>Equipment removal requires prior authorization and must be logged for audit purposes</li>
<li>Maintenance and repair activities must be logged, with access restricted to authorized personnel</li>
</ul>
<h2>Environmental Controls</h2>
<h2>Data Center Requirements</h2>
<ul>
<li>Temperature: 18-27°C (64-80°F) to adhere to ASHRAE guidelines</li>
<li>Humidity: 40-60% relative humidity</li>
<li>Fire suppression system compliant with NFPA standards</li>
<li>Uninterruptible power supply (UPS) with regular testing and maintenance</li>
<li>Generator backup tested monthly</li>
<li>Water detection sensors installed under raised floors</li>
</ul>
<h2>Monitoring</h2>
<ul>
<li>24/7 environmental monitoring with automated systems</li>
<li>Automated alerts for threshold breaches sent to designated personnel</li>
<li>Regular testing of backup systems to ensure operational readiness</li>
</ul>
<h2>Clear Desk and Clear Screen</h2>
<ul>
<li>Sensitive documents must be locked away when not in use to prevent unauthorized access</li>
<li>Workstations must be locked when unattended, with enforced screen lock after 5 minutes of inactivity</li>
<li>Whiteboards must be erased after meetings to prevent information leakage</li>
<li>Printers must be cleared of documents immediately, especially those containing sensitive information</li>
<li>Screen privacy filters should be used for work involving sensitive data</li>
</ul>
<h2>Document Control</h2>
<p>Field</p>
<p>Value</p>
