<h2>1. Purpose</h2>
<p>The purpose of this Security Awareness Training Policy is to establish the standards and procedures for enhancing cybersecurity awareness and resilience at Intellfence. This policy aims to equip all personnel with the necessary knowledge to protect the organization&#39;s information assets and comply with relevant cybersecurity regulations, such as SOC 2 and ISO/IEC 27001 standards.</p>
<h2>2. Scope</h2>
<p>This policy applies to all employees, contractors, and third parties who access Intellfence systems or data. It is imperative for all personnel to participate in security awareness training to understand potential threats, including phishing, social engineering, and other cyber attacks, and to adhere to best practices in data protection.</p>
<h2>3. Policy Statement</h2>
<p>Intellfence is committed to implementing comprehensive security awareness training programs to ensure the security and confidentiality of our data. These programs are designed to educate and empower our workforce to recognize and respond to cybersecurity threats effectively. Regular training sessions will be conducted to keep all personnel informed about the latest security trends and regulatory requirements, such as those outlined in SOC 2 and ISO/IEC 27001.</p>
<h2>4. Enforcement</h2>
<p>Violations of this policy may result in disciplinary action, which could include mandatory retraining, suspension of access privileges, or other appropriate measures. Compliance with this policy is mandatory to maintain the integrity and security of Intellfence&#39;s information systems and to uphold our commitment to cybersecurity excellence.</p>
 2026-01-29T09:40:47.285Z', NULL, NULL, NULL);


