                <h2 style="font-size: 24px; color: #2d3748; border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding-bottom: 10px; margin-bottom: 20px;">Risk Appetite & Compliance Drivers</h2>
                <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: #4a5568;">
                    <p style="margin-bottom: 20px; font-style: italic; color: #2d3748;">In this section, we will examine Intellfence''s risk appetite in the context of its cybersecurity operations, focusing on how it aligns with organizational objectives and industry standards. We will also explore the external compliance drivers that shape and influence this risk posture, highlighting the necessity for a strategic roadmap to navigate the evolving cybersecurity landscape effectively.</p>
                    Risk Analysis Summary:<br/>• Total Risks Identified: 23<br/>• High / Critical Risks: 14<br/>• Controls Implemented: 3 of 100<br/>• Implementation Rate: 3%<br/><br/>    Compliance Drivers:<br/>1. Regulatory Requirements: Industry standards<br/>2. Business Objectives: Establish governance framework, Implement key controls, Achieve target compliance score<br/>3. Risk Mitigation: Focus on 14 high - priority risks<br/>4. Control Implementation: Achieve target compliance through control deployment<br/><br/>Risk Appetite Statement:<br/>The organization should maintain a moderate risk appetite, focusing on mitigating critical risks while implementing essential controls to achieve compliance with relevant frameworks.
